:{"id":1099},"before":{"id":1099,"title":"Het bloemenmeisje","isbn_10":null,"isbn_13":"9789024593637","work_id":1099,"language":null,"publisher":"Luitingh Sijthoff","created_at":"2026-09-03T19:09:41.501931+00:00","open_library_edition_id":"OL60760087M"},"after":{"id":1099,"title":"Het bloemenmeisje","isbn_10":null,"isbn_13":"9789024593637","work_id":1099,"language":"nld","publisher":"Luitingh Sijthoff","created_at":"2026-09-03T19:09:41.501931+00:00","open_library_edition_id":"OL60760087M"},"changed":{"language":"nld"},"origin":"NL100-053","evidence":[]},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:125:nl","key":{"work_id":125,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/138134/de-oversteek.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:53:51.159Z","sha256":"a9551a5f6595307d87afa7d21375e0cc944ab31b1b0204dea8e290c0b7f9046c","isbn":"9789023425540","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789023425540 verschijningsdatum 03/10/2016 NUR 305 Literaire thriller imprint Cargo uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":125,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":106,"text":"Een geheim Amerikaans experiment met een gevaarlijk virus loopt uit op een ramp. Het meisje Amy ontsnapt, terwijl de wereld om haar heen ingrijpend verandert. Veel later probeert een kleine gemeenschap binnen haar muren te overleven. De komst van een onbekende jonge vrouw zet een groep overlevenden aan tot een tocht buiten die bescherming. Hun zoektocht naar de oorsprong van de ramp verbindt het verleden met de toekomst van de kolonie.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/138134/de-oversteek.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-001"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:199:nl","key":{"work_id":199,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1219767/de-testamenten.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:01.677Z","sha256":"c36c63a3e06184223c9e1304e3144b8273ec3ce5e250e2e615cdd9a934f9c52d","isbn":"9789044641882","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789044641882 verschijningsdatum 10/09/2019 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Prometheus uitgever Prometheus, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":199,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":8,"text":"Gilead bestaat nog steeds, maar achter het gesloten machtsapparaat ontstaan barsten. Drie vrouwen vertellen vanuit heel verschillende posities over hun leven met het regime. Een van hen groeit binnen Gilead op, een ander bekijkt het land vanuit Canada en de derde kent de geheimen van de machthebbers. Hun verhalen raken met elkaar verweven. Het vervolg op Het verhaal van de dienstmaagd onderzoekt hoe gehoorzaamheid, informatie en verzet een samenleving bepalen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1219767/de-testamenten.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-003"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2825:nl","key":{"work_id":2825,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/423967/2666.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:07.753Z","sha256":"a949f84371c1536c0ff22bd1685063e7bbcbeb3c578bd70ad75cc4c29038a0e7","isbn":"9789048818501","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789048818501 verschijningsdatum 18/09/2013 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Lebowski uitgever Overamstel Uitgevers taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":2825,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1359,"text":"In de grensstreek van Mexico en de Verenigde Staten worden vrouwen en meisjes vermoord. Een zoektocht naar een raadselachtige schrijver raakt aan het onderzoek naar die misdaden. De roman verbindt literaire speurtochten met een omgeving waarin geweld steeds aanwezig is en de verantwoordelijken onduidelijk blijven. De afzonderlijke verhaallijnen kijken vanuit verschillende hoeken naar dezelfde dreiging, zonder de slachtoffers of hun wereld tot een eenvoudig op te lossen raadsel te maken.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/423967/2666.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-004"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1894:nl","key":{"work_id":1894,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1114482/de-geesten-van-hill-house.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:10.885Z","sha256":"d164fea57e3c9c8164c30057f273373b727ec331c3699c5b9707990f9e3dea80","isbn":"9789020415742","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789020415742 verschijningsdatum 22/10/2018 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint LJ Veen Klassiek uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1894,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":961,"text":"Eleanor Vance gaat met drie anderen naar Hill House, een landhuis waar volgens de verhalen onverklaarbare dingen gebeuren. Een onderzoeker wil er bewijs verzamelen voor paranormale verschijnselen. Tijdens het verblijf neemt de spanning binnen de groep toe en wordt vooral Eleanors verhouding tot het huis steeds beklemmender. De roman laat de grens tussen een dreiging van buitenaf en de kwetsbaarheid van de bewoners onzeker. Angst en eenzaamheid sturen wat zij ervaren.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1114482/de-geesten-van-hill-house.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-005"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1951:nl","key":{"work_id":1951,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.atlascontact.nl/boek/de-roep-van-de-wildernis/","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:53.901Z","sha256":"dd397f33c59f2d0b8304c0dea66a9cee80c5ef5a9d656a9c9c1d35c58f405a63","isbn":"9789020415629","facts":"Publisher explicitly identifies Dutch paperback ISBN 9789020415629, translator Margot Bakker; exact book page displays this front cover."}],"work_id":1951,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":237,"text":"Buck wordt uit zijn comfortabele leven in Californië weggehaald en als sledehond verkocht. Tijdens de goudkoorts in het hoge noorden moet hij leren omgaan met kou, uitputting en een harde strijd om te overleven. De hond ontdekt geleidelijk hoe belangrijk zijn instincten zijn in deze nieuwe omgeving. Vanuit zijn ervaringen onderzoekt de roman het verschil tussen de regels van de menselijke beschaving en die van de wildernis, zonder het avontuur van zijn dierlijke hoofdpersoon los te laten.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Officiële uitgever","source_url":"https://www.atlascontact.nl/boek/de-roep-van-de-wildernis/","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-006"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:189:nl","key":{"work_id":189,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/61817/de-kraaien-list-leugens.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:22.999Z","sha256":"cfb20a6c11f8959aa2083539c81f800ade45299c24bc685bd8e0c2eb1f6ac886","isbn":"9789463492478","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789463492478 verschijningsdatum 07/05/2021 NUR 285 Fictie 15+ imprint Blossom Books uitgever Xander Uitgevers B.V. taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":189,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":142,"text":"In Ketterdam krijgt de jonge crimineel Kaz Brekker een opdracht die hem een fortuin kan opleveren. Hij verzamelt vijf buitenstaanders met uiteenlopende vaardigheden voor een gevaarlijke onderneming in Fjerda. Onderweg staan niet alleen vijanden en machtige magie hun in de weg: ook hun eigen belangen en onderlinge wantrouwen maken samenwerken moeilijk. De wisselende perspectieven laten zien wat ieder teamlid meebrengt. Dit is het eerste deel van de Kraaien-duologie binnen de Grishaverse.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/61817/de-kraaien-list-leugens.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-008"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1141:nl","key":{"work_id":1141,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/890528/lampje.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:25.889Z","sha256":"49968bffc5ba783acf8c99a2175649fe57011f8202eb4872dc6dbb6b1bcfdf2b","isbn":"9789045120379","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789045120379 verschijningsdatum 24/03/2017 NUR 283 Fictie 10-12 jaar imprint Querido uitgever Singel Uitgeverijen taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1141,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":675,"text":"Lampje is de dochter van een vuurtorenwachter. Iedere avond helpt zij het licht te laten branden, totdat tijdens een storm de lucifers op zijn en alles misgaat. Haar wereld omvat een eiland, de zee en het geheimzinnige Zwarte Huis van de Admiraal, waar volgens de verhalen een monster woont. Tussen piraten en wonderlijke zeewezens moet Lampje ontdekken waarop zij kan vertrouwen. Het verhaal draait om moed en mogelijkheden die zij zelf nog niet kent.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/890528/lampje.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-009"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1100:nl","key":{"work_id":1100,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1534884/de-camino-mp.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:28.861Z","sha256":"f7596441b476edf97fe838fef8af210cd953d31716723b636f46cc554d644cab","isbn":"9789024582273","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789024582273 verschijningsdatum 04/06/2021 NUR 305 Literaire thriller imprint Luitingh Sijthoff uitgever Luitingh-Sijthoff B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1100,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":665,"text":"Wanneer haar man Emil tijdens de Camino onverwacht zelfmoord pleegt, blijft chocolatier Lotte Bonnet met vragen achter. Bij een reis naar Bosnië ontdekt zij dat hij over zijn identiteit heeft gelogen. Ze laat zijn verleden onderzoeken en besluit ondertussen dezelfde pelgrimsroute te lopen. Lotte hoopt te begrijpen wat er is gebeurd, maar haar zoektocht trekt ongewenste aandacht. Iemand volgt haar en wil voorkomen dat de waarheid over Emil aan het licht komt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1534884/de-camino-mp.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-010"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1153:nl","key":{"work_id":1153,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1185373/de-meeste-mensen-deugen.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:33.485Z","sha256":"8ea84e3cb8543e8a4de7e2809fc6e386853fc8a5fa9d978b2d79605cdfa0928d","isbn":"9789493254411","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789493254411 verschijningsdatum 03/11/2023 NUR 320 Literaire non-fictie algemeen imprint De Correspondent uitgever De Correspondent Uitgevers B.V. taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1153,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":678,"text":"Rutger Bregman onderzoekt het idee dat mensen van nature vooral op hun eigen belang uit zijn. Met historische voorbeelden en een andere blik op het verleden stelt hij dat gangbare mensbeeld ter discussie. De vraag is niet alleen hoe mensen zich gedragen, maar ook welke gevolgen onze verwachtingen van elkaar hebben. Dit non-fictieboek combineert een betoog over de menselijke geschiedenis met vragen over vertrouwen en de inrichting van de samenleving.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1185373/de-meeste-mensen-deugen.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-011"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1033:nl","key":{"work_id":1033,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/2035787/het-diner-limited-edition-100e-druk.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:39.391Z","sha256":"53fab2cd265427d78b7a790ccc29d9cd8c70784d3087c508fdf53f0faa8f4e90","isbn":"9789026337260","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789026337260 verschijningsdatum 23/02/2017 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint Ambo|Anthos uitgever Ambo/Anthos B.V. taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1033,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":642,"text":"Twee echtparen spreken af in een restaurant. Tussen de gesprekken over werk, films en vakantie vermijden zij het onderwerp waarvoor ze werkelijk bij elkaar zijn: hun vijftienjarige zoons hebben samen iets ernstigs gedaan. De beelden zijn op televisie geweest, maar hun identiteit is nog niet vastgesteld. Terwijl de maaltijd voortgaat, wordt de spanning tussen ouderlijke bescherming en verantwoordelijkheid steeds groter. De politieke ambities van een van de vaders maken hun keuzes extra beladen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/2035787/het-diner-limited-edition-100e-druk.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-012"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1042:nl","key":{"work_id":1042,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1134532/grand-hotel-europa.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:49.925Z","sha256":"2e88314ad632a48f57583d146dcec45f7fa2073dccc2f325426c7a08d1b63d15","isbn":"9789029526227","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789029526227 verschijningsdatum 13/12/2018 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint De Arbeiderspers uitgever Singel Uitgeverijen taal Nederlands"},{"url":"https://www.singeluitgeverijen.nl/de-arbeiderspers/boek/grand-hotel-europa/","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","role":"summary_content_source"}],"work_id":1042,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":644,"text":"Een schrijver trekt in een oud Europees hotel om na te denken over zijn verbroken relatie met Clio. Hij haalt herinneringen op aan hun leven in Genua en Venetië, hun reizen en een zoektocht naar een schilderij van Caravaggio. Intussen leert hij de bewoners en geheimen van het hotel kennen. Zijn persoonlijke terugblik raakt verweven met vragen over Europa, massatoerisme en een continent dat steeds sterker van zijn eigen verleden lijkt te leven.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Officiële uitgever","source_url":"https://www.singeluitgeverijen.nl/de-arbeiderspers/boek/grand-hotel-europa/","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-014"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1058:nl","key":{"work_id":1058,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1032990/de-avond-is-ongemak.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:52.970Z","sha256":"d7cc4cdd8a981128ab62f555044b6ffa2e912911288519a8a0ad6a3048762805","isbn":"9789025475321","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789025475321 verschijningsdatum 27/09/2023 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint Atlas Contact uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"},{"url":"https://www.atlascontact.nl/boek/de-avond-is-ongemak/","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","role":"summary_content_source"}],"work_id":1058,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":650,"text":"Na de dood van een kind raakt een gereformeerd boerengezin ontwricht. Jas probeert te begrijpen wat het verlies betekent, terwijl haar ouders door verdriet nauwelijks zien wat er met hun andere kinderen gebeurt. Haar broer Obbe en zusje Hanna zoeken ieder hun eigen weg. Vanuit Jas'' beleving verkent de roman het gebied tussen kindertijd en volwassenheid, waar geloof, lichamelijkheid en rouw door elkaar lopen en vertrouwde zekerheden steeds minder houvast bieden.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Officiële uitgever","source_url":"https://www.atlascontact.nl/boek/de-avond-is-ongemak/","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-015"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1344:nl","key":{"work_id":1344,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1739564/oroppa.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:57.450Z","sha256":"303d58ce7cfe2f5de18c9a0be7e03d70224dd539e1f845a3e3f1af8c70c5040c","isbn":"9789493339132","facts":"E-book (epub) ISBN 9789493339132 verschijningsdatum 28/08/2024 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint Uitgeverij Pluim uitgever Uitgeverij Pluim taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1344,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":720,"text":"In Parijs houdt Irad Abergel een kroeg open voor mensen die elders nauwelijks een plek vinden. Zijn moeder Salomé is verdwenen. In Amsterdam ontdekt Hind in de kelder van Salomés huis schilderijen die haar niet loslaten. Hun verhalen verbinden verschillende steden en levens die door het verleden worden achtervolgd. De roman onderzoekt hoe macht mensen beïnvloedt en wat er gebeurt wanneer zij weigeren zich nog langer naar een systeem te voegen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1739564/oroppa.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-016"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1178:nl","key":{"work_id":1178,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1623006/komt-een-vrouw-bij-de-dokter.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:20.164Z","sha256":"17a39bd3f38518af5761875fa5b1e88da6e90b227c16911bc8e270c46108700f","isbn":"9789057598340","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789057598340 verschijningsdatum 15/02/2017 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint Podium uitgever NBC - Uitgeverij Kluun taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1178,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":691,"text":"Stijn heeft een eigen bedrijf, een vrouw en een dochter. Wanneer zijn vrouw kanker krijgt, verandert het leven van het gezin ingrijpend. Hij probeert haar te steunen, maar zoekt tegelijkertijd afleiding in het uitgaansleven en bij andere vrouwen. De roman volgt die spanning tussen zorg, liefde en de neiging aan een ondraaglijke situatie te ontsnappen. Het persoonlijke verhaal stelt ongemakkelijke vragen over trouw en verantwoordelijkheid tijdens een ernstige ziekte.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1623006/komt-een-vrouw-bij-de-dokter.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-022"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:wisselwachter::geertmak:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:wisselwachter::geertmak","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1919336/wisselwachter.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:56.937Z","sha256":"c2853149356fb5118caedd4d2a452f5123d62fe28472bde8fb8a71c2c539e14f","isbn":"9789045051734","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789045051734 verschijningsdatum 17/04/2025 NUR 680 Geschiedenis algemeen 320 Literaire non-fictie algemeen 697 Politieke geschiedenis en geschiedenis van de internationale betrekkingen imprint Atlas Contact uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:wisselwachter::geertmak","language":"nl","bound_author_id":677,"text":"Geert Mak beschrijft de verhouding tussen Amerika en Europa in de jaren dertig en veertig aan de hand van Harry Hopkins. Deze voormalige welzijnswerker werd een belangrijke medewerker van president Roosevelt en speelde een rol in de New Deal en het geallieerde bondgenootschap. Het boek verbindt zijn loopbaan met het leven rond het Witte Huis. Politieke beslissingen over economie, democratie en oorlog verschijnen zo binnen de persoonlijke omgeving waarin zij tot stand kwamen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1919336/wisselwachter.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-061"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:demeisjes::annetschaap:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:demeisjes::annetschaap","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1435347/de-meisjes.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T21:00:38.195Z","sha256":"486069fd746c836da48a508eb6d4a217af7dee04c635e165aa89d0ba70a63bcc","isbn":"9789045126692","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789045126692 verschijningsdatum 07/09/2021 NUR 283 Fictie 10-12 jaar imprint Querido uitgever Singel Uitgeverijen taal Nederlands"},{"url":"https://www.zwijsen.nl/product/de-meisjes-9789045126692/","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","role":"summary_content_source"}],"work_id":"@work:demeisjes::annetschaap","language":"nl","bound_author_id":675,"text":"Annet Schaap geeft zeven bekende sprookjes een andere invulling. Meisjes die gewoonlijk herkenbare sprookjesrollen spelen, krijgen eigen verlangens en twijfels. Er is een slaapster die niet wakker wordt, een kikker die geen prins wordt en een meisje dat als monster wordt gezien. De verhalen gebruiken vertrouwde motieven zonder de gebruikelijke afloop vanzelfsprekend te maken. Deze geïllustreerde bundel bestaat uit afzonderlijke vertellingen en is geen nieuw deel van Lampje.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Officiële uitgever","source_url":"https://www.zwijsen.nl/product/de-meisjes-9789045126692/","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-100"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1007:nl","key":{"work_id":1007,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/441858/de-aanslag.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:00.549Z","sha256":"73e44e6b12ad30ff8f4d445517715654092246e4c48de148daa1eeb2a9cc6912","isbn":"9789023473251","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789023473251 verschijningsdatum 03/09/2012 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1007,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":636,"text":"In januari 1945 wordt een collaborerende politieman vlak bij het huis van de familie Steenwijk doodgeschoten. De gevolgen treffen de twaalfjarige Anton en blijven hem ook na de oorlog achtervolgen. Wat er die nacht precies gebeurde, laat zich niet in één eenvoudig verhaal vatten. De roman volgt hoe een gewelddadige gebeurtenis doorwerkt in herinneringen en in een later leven. Vragen over verantwoordelijkheid, toeval, schuld en onschuld blijven daarbij met elkaar verbonden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/441858/de-aanslag.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-017"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1021:nl","key":{"work_id":1021,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/438962/het-verdriet-van-belgie.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:08.052Z","sha256":"6ad323b9b97bf500700b2b12e8f5707b1878a77ddc56d33aaf78fba803de7bba","isbn":"9789023428732","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789023428732 verschijningsdatum 05/02/2008 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1021,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":639,"text":"Louis Seynaeve is elf wanneer zijn verhaal op een nonneninternaat begint. Tussen 1939 en 1947 veranderen oorlog en collaboratie het Vlaamse leven waarin hij opgroeit. Binnen zijn familie lopen verlangens, leugens en tegenstrijdige overtuigingen door elkaar. Louis probeert te begrijpen wat volwassenen doen en wat hun verhalen verbergen. Zijn persoonlijke ontwikkeling staat niet los van de historische verwarring om hem heen. Zo verbindt de roman een jeugd met een samenleving die zichzelf opnieuw moet leren bekijken.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/438962/het-verdriet-van-belgie.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-019"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6278:nl","key":{"work_id":6278,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/55523/tonio.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:11.105Z","sha256":"ad1cb67c21f36b9a15d40841a1f270ebc8e07c5d53d514bde3f9d5e756b2e7db","isbn":"9789023465720","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789023465720 verschijningsdatum 01/05/2011 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint De Bezige Bij uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":6278,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3368,"text":"Na de dood van zijn eenentwintigjarige zoon Tonio probeert A.F.Th. van der Heijden te reconstrueren wat er voor het verkeersongeluk is gebeurd. Hij verzamelt herinneringen, spreekt betrokkenen en zoekt naar de laatste momenten van het leven van zijn kind. Die zoektocht wordt tegelijk een verslag van rouw en van het schrijven zelf. Het boek onderzoekt wat feitelijke kennis kan betekenen wanneer een verlies niet ongedaan kan worden gemaakt, zonder de persoonlijke herinnering tot een sluitend antwoord te reduceren.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/55523/tonio.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-020"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1111:nl","key":{"work_id":1111,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/69629/kruistocht-in-spijkerbroek.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:23.045Z","sha256":"e2b229c8cdb6de9d7ded499c8b900d0aae0e51c5fafc40f0ce0580f55954f4b9","isbn":"9789060691670","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789060691670 verschijningsdatum 01/01/1973 NUR 280 Fictie kinder- en jeugdboeken algemeen uitgever Lemniscaat B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1111,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":669,"text":"Dolf meldt zich voor een experiment waarmee hij korte tijd naar het verleden kan reizen. Een fout brengt hem in 1212, waar hij terechtkomt tussen duizenden kinderen die op kruistocht zijn. Hun vertrouwen in beloofde wonderen staat tegenover de gevaren van een lange reis. Dolf bekijkt hun onderneming met kennis uit een andere tijd, maar moet zelf ook zien te overleven. Ondertussen blijft onzeker of hij op de afgesproken manier naar huis kan terugkeren.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/69629/kruistocht-in-spijkerbroek.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-023"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1105:nl","key":{"work_id":1105,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/451367/de-brief-voor-de-koning.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:26.047Z","sha256":"7f2852ec50d8a215700a49e3c1532b20ad1edc389157ad3e328edaea02b47f28","isbn":"9789025852436","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789025852436 verschijningsdatum 26/06/2008 NUR 283 Fictie 10-12 jaar uitgever Leopold taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1105,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":668,"text":"In de nacht voordat hij tot ridder wordt geslagen, hoort Tiuri een dringende roep om hulp. Hij verbreekt de regels van zijn wake en krijgt een opdracht die hem ver van de veilige kapel voert. Een brief moet de koning van een naburig land bereiken, terwijl tegenstanders hem proberen tegen te houden. Tiuri moet bepalen wie hij kan vertrouwen en wat zijn belofte waard is. Het avontuur stelt zijn moed en verantwoordelijkheidsgevoel steeds opnieuw op de proef.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/451367/de-brief-voor-de-koning.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-024"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1119:nl","key":{"work_id":1119,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/256112/oorlogswinter.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:32.166Z","sha256":"c5a6aeea86bc7a902866560861527896a6b1ca8ac0eef0733b83253940b4ec42","isbn":"9789047701170","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789047701170 verschijningsdatum 09/10/2008 NUR 283 Fictie 10-12 jaar imprint Lemniscaat uitgever Lemniscaat B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"},{"url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/oorlogswinter","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","role":"summary_content_source"}],"work_id":1119,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":670,"text":"Tijdens de hongerwinter wil Michiel iets betekenen voor het verzet. Wanneer buurjongen Dirk hem een brief toevertrouwt voor het geval een actie mislukt, krijgt dat verlangen onverwachte gevolgen. Michiel raakt betrokken bij gebeurtenissen waarin hij niet eenvoudig op volwassenen kan vertrouwen. Hij moet zelfstandig beslissen, terwijl gevaar en verraad steeds dichtbij zijn. De roman laat zien hoe de oorlog het dagelijks leven verandert en hoe moeilijk het is om onder druk goed en kwaad te onderscheiden.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Officiële uitgever","source_url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/oorlogswinter","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-025"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1248:nl","key":{"work_id":1248,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/256734/pluk-van-de-petteflet.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:35.131Z","sha256":"ec74feac08d3bc79bbe53aa45b8ff379a4aa3c383e901659db421c4f463f4829","isbn":"9789045110950","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789045110950 verschijningsdatum 01/04/2010 NUR 281 Fictie 4-6 jaar uitgever Singel Uitgeverijen taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1248,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":667,"text":"Pluk vindt een woonplek in de torenkamer van de Petteflet. Met zijn rode kraanwagentje en zijn nieuwe vrienden ontdekt hij de buurt en haar bijzondere bewoners. Wanneer de Torteltuin moet verdwijnen voor een parkeerplaats, komen ook de dieren die daar leven in gevaar. Pluk probeert samen met zijn vrienden te voorkomen dat het parkje verloren gaat. De verschillende ontmoetingen vormen een doorlopend avontuur waarin hulp vragen en voor anderen opkomen belangrijker blijken dan groot of machtig zijn.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/256734/pluk-van-de-petteflet.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-026"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1103:nl","key":{"work_id":1103,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/324719/minoes.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:38.212Z","sha256":"23fb0feb5022949459b42b2f5e7aa40f00fa4bb0909b15b013d5eeb70c38eb43","isbn":"9789045105772","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789045105772 verschijningsdatum 19/10/2007 NUR 281 Fictie 4-6 jaar uitgever Singel Uitgeverijen taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1103,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":667,"text":"Minoes ziet eruit als een jonge vrouw, maar is vroeger een kat geweest. Ze kan nog altijd met katten praten en hoort daardoor nieuws dat andere mensen ontgaat. Wanneer ze verneemt dat er iets mis is bij een chemische fabriek, vertelt ze dit aan de verlegen journalist Tibbe. Voor hem kan het de kans op een belangrijk verhaal worden. Hun samenwerking brengt verborgen gebeurtenissen aan het licht en maakt de grens tussen de mensenwereld en de kattenwereld verrassend klein.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/324719/minoes.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-027"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1652:nl","key":{"work_id":1652,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/310866/turks-fruit.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:51.912Z","sha256":"4bd592692b0685ece84fdbd58cb347017e679318bf88d8ca2ae5e15804b1b58f","isbn":"9789029077033","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789029077033 verschijningsdatum 10/10/2005 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle 340 Populaire fiction algemeen imprint J.M. Meulenhoff uitgever Meulenhoff Boekerij B.V. taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1652,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":748,"text":"Beeldhouwer Erik en Olga beginnen een heftige liefdesrelatie en besluiten te trouwen, ondanks de bezwaren van haar ouders. Hun gezamenlijke leven lijkt aanvankelijk door verlangen en vrijheid te worden bepaald. Wanneer Olga afstand neemt en naar haar ouders terugkeert, probeert Erik te begrijpen wat hun verhouding heeft veranderd. Zijn herinneringen verbinden lichamelijke liefde met verlies en vergankelijkheid. De roman laat zien hoe iemand een relatie blijft navertellen wanneer het gedeelde leven niet meer binnen bereik ligt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/310866/turks-fruit.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-030"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1051:nl","key":{"work_id":1051,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/114973/de-helaasheid-der-dingen.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:59.357Z","sha256":"5040d01499510c74de96782e7e51fcee98d0ada8a02c1a4b87eb342cf8554e88","isbn":"9789046703502","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789046703502 verschijningsdatum 21/12/2012 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint Olympus uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1051,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":647,"text":"Een schrijver keert in zijn herinneringen terug naar Reetveerdegem, het dorp waar hij tussen zijn vader, grootmoeder en ooms opgroeide. Het gezinsleven wordt er getekend door drank, armoede en botsingen met de omgeving. De verteller bekijkt die wereld met zowel genegenheid als afstand. Grappige en pijnlijke gebeurtenissen komen naast elkaar te staan, zonder dat de familie tot een karikatuur wordt teruggebracht. Zo ontstaat een terugblik op de mensen en gewoonten waarvan iemand afkomstig is, maar ook probeert los te komen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/114973/de-helaasheid-der-dingen.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-032"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2444:nl","key":{"work_id":2444,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1297023/hamnet.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:05.402Z","sha256":"39e3874a98bef1aefe0a0ded7de3ead777092f3efcc4d76c5226814075f0b139","isbn":"9789038808345","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789038808345 verschijningsdatum 21/04/2020 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Nijgh & Van Ditmar uitgever Singel Uitgeverijen taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":2444,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1194,"text":"In Stratford-upon-Avon wordt Judith ziek terwijl haar tweelingbroer Hamnet hulp probeert te vinden. Hun moeder Agnes is buiten het dorp en hun vader werkt als toneelschrijver in Londen. Vanuit deze familie onderzoekt de roman hoe liefde en verlies een huishouden veranderen. Het verhaal is een verbeelding rond het gezin van William Shakespeare, niet een biografie die alle gesprekken als historische feiten presenteert. Het dagelijks leven en de verbondenheid tussen ouders en kinderen staan centraal.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1297023/hamnet.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-034"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:652:nl","key":{"work_id":652,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1299306/de-moordclub-op-donderdag.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:13.204Z","sha256":"fbf86850d2a4419015b4a6d3ccfcaa77964ad77a5bb88b7a3f1dc7561e308cce","isbn":"9789403197401","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789403197401 Nieuwe editie verschijningsdatum 03/09/2020 NUR 305 Literaire thriller imprint Cargo uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":652,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":391,"text":"Vier bewoners van een verzorgingshuis bespreken iedere donderdag onopgeloste moordzaken. Wanneer in de omgeving een vastgoedontwikkelaar wordt vermoord, krijgen hun bijeenkomsten een onverwacht praktisch vervolg. De zaak lijkt verband te houden met hun eigen woonplek. De vrienden gebruiken hun verschillende ervaringen om uit te zoeken wat er is gebeurd, maar een echte moordenaar laat zich minder gemakkelijk onderzoeken dan een oud dossier. Hun leeftijd maakt hen niet onkwetsbaar en ook niet vanzelf ongeschikt als speurders.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1299306/de-moordclub-op-donderdag.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-035"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:105:nl","key":{"work_id":105,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1140829/normale-mensen.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:17.508Z","sha256":"f826504f318b35855433307ce54a8e76c04e4faf3c913189d35afd38fa70e72b","isbn":"9789026343445","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789026343445 verschijningsdatum 15/01/2019 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Ambo|Anthos uitgever Ambo/Anthos B.V. taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":105,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":92,"text":"Marianne en Connell groeien op in hetzelfde Ierse stadje, maar nemen op school heel verschillende posities in. Hun contact begint buiten de blik van hun klasgenoten en ontwikkelt zich tot een band die ook tijdens hun studie in Dublin blijft doorwerken. Verschillen in achtergrond en onzekerheid beïnvloeden wat zij elkaar durven te zeggen. De roman volgt hoe twee mensen elkaar veranderen en toch telkens moeite houden om te begrijpen welke plaats zij in elkaars leven innemen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1140829/normale-mensen.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-037"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:180:nl","key":{"work_id":180,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/178792/carrie.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:54:16.814Z","sha256":"521ea2ee569f714cd122af25c12c70dfb36b7c175e35dfc6e711422498cf4ce6","isbn":"9789021035413","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789021035413 verschijningsdatum 21/09/2022 NUR 313 Pockets spanning imprint Luitingh Sijthoff uitgever Luitingh-Sijthoff B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":180,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":49,"text":"Carrie White wordt op school gepest en groeit thuis op onder de strenge religieuze overtuigingen van haar moeder. Ze ontdekt dat ze met haar gedachten voorwerpen kan laten bewegen, maar houdt dat vermogen verborgen. Een uitnodiging voor het schoolfeest lijkt haar voor het eerst een andere positie te geven. Niet iedereen gunt haar die kans. De roman verbindt de vernedering van een buitengesloten meisje met een kracht waarvan de gevolgen steeds moeilijker te beheersen zijn.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/178792/carrie.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-007"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1037:nl","key":{"work_id":1037,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/49470/joe-speedboot.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:15.648Z","sha256":"817e4b583ec754303e6063f58165fe4c6c8b5dcf81ab5facb03e00037c14a9cf","isbn":"9789023485735","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789023485735 verschijningsdatum 21/01/2014 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1037,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":643,"text":"Fransje Hermans kan na een ongeluk niet meer spreken en houdt het leven in zijn dorp Lomark nauwlettend bij. De komst van Joe Speedboot doorbreekt de vertrouwde verhoudingen. Joe bouwt, experimenteert en brengt anderen op ideeën die buiten hun gewone verwachtingen liggen. Fransje raakt door hem gefascineerd, terwijl vriendschap, liefde en rivaliteit steeds meer door elkaar gaan lopen. Vanuit zijn eigen beperkte bewegingsruimte beschrijft de verteller hoe nieuwkomers een dorp veranderen en hoe mensen elkaar tegelijk vooruithelpen en vastzetten.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/49470/joe-speedboot.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-021"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1118:nl","key":{"work_id":1118,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/93759/koning-van-katoren.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:55:42.926Z","sha256":"69de7dfe1f6fb480060055b881d8611124048ed478f75410f090a2cf7d5ab55f","isbn":"9789060690888","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789060690888 verschijningsdatum 01/01/1971 NUR 283 Fictie 10-12 jaar uitgever Lemniscaat B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1118,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":670,"text":"Stach wil koning worden van Katoren, het land dat sinds de dood van de vorige vorst door zes ministers wordt bestuurd. Die geven de zeventienjarige zeven opdrachten. Als hij ze allemaal voltooit, zou de troon voor hem zijn. De opdrachten brengen hem in aanraking met uiteenlopende problemen en met mensen die er dagelijks de gevolgen van ondervinden. Terwijl Stach oplossingen zoekt, groeit de vraag of de bestuurders werkelijk op een opvolger zitten te wachten.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/93759/koning-van-katoren.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-028"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:13:nl","key":{"work_id":13,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/295163/de-alchemist.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:31.085Z","sha256":"c3a783dcbf4454956bbd14ae3b2cd4b65c76405e614e3c8346589b5dd9ae8b6d","isbn":"9789029588607","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789029588607 verschijningsdatum 10/04/2013 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint De Arbeiderspers uitgever Singel Uitgeverijen taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":13,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":10,"text":"Schaapherder Santiago wil meer van de wereld zien dan zijn vertrouwde omgeving. Een terugkerende droom over een verborgen schat brengt hem ertoe op reis te gaan. Zijn zoektocht leidt langs mensen die hem verschillend uitleggen wat van waarde is en hoe hij zijn richting kan bepalen. In Egypte ontmoet hij een alchemist. Het verhaal gebruikt Santiago''s reis om vragen te stellen over verlangens, keuzes en de verhouding tussen een zichtbaar doel en wat iemand onderweg leert.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/295163/de-alchemist.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-040"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:336:nl","key":{"work_id":336,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/215336/als-je-het-licht-niet-kunt-zien.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:43.217Z","sha256":"a828edbe02aefca8a433f8cf7f73e3c0945b667ab1c3df89b21f0511b7ef2995","isbn":"9789044345940","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789044345940 verschijningsdatum 07/01/2015 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint The House of Books uitgever Overamstel Uitgevers taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":336,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":211,"text":"De blinde Marie-Laure vlucht met haar vader uit bezet Parijs naar Saint-Malo. Tegelijk groeit de Duitse wees Werner op in een wereld die hem naar de oorlog voert. Hun levens lijken aanvankelijk ver van elkaar verwijderd, maar bewegen naar dezelfde Franse kustplaats. De roman volgt hoe jonge mensen door grote historische gebeurtenissen worden meegesleept en welke beslissingen binnen die omstandigheden nog mogelijk blijven. Familie, kennis en kwetsbaarheid krijgen betekenis tegenover het geweld dat hun dagelijks bestaan binnendringt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/215336/als-je-het-licht-niet-kunt-zien.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-043"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:10:nl","key":{"work_id":10,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/356829/de-boekendief.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:49.164Z","sha256":"e6966f04868db7e9e209bbfcef7bceee13088f8375fcda3dd45fd651b35017c2","isbn":"9789044342628","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789044342628 verschijningsdatum 13/03/2014 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint The House of Books uitgever Overamstel Uitgevers taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":10,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":9,"text":"In nazi-Duitsland wordt Liesel bij een pleeggezin ondergebracht nadat haar broertje onderweg is gestorven. Een boekje dat ze bij zijn graf vindt, wordt het begin van haar belangstelling voor woorden. Met hulp van haar pleegvader leert ze lezen. Ze zoekt vervolgens overal naar boeken, ook op plaatsen waar dat gevaarlijk is. Tegen de achtergrond van vervolging en oorlog ontdekt Liesel wat verhalen voor haar kunnen betekenen en hoe haar nieuwe thuis met die dreigende wereld verbonden is.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/356829/de-boekendief.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-044"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:409:nl","key":{"work_id":409,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/739609/een-klein-leven.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:53.760Z","sha256":"89b781f8a4ac80f95966253ce6355f9591d273500ce607e38f135ba3cd718d9b","isbn":"9789046822708","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789046822708 verschijningsdatum 20/04/2017 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Nieuw Amsterdam uitgever Park Uitgevers taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":409,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":253,"text":"Vier studievrienden proberen in New York een bestaan op te bouwen. Hun verschillende ambities brengen hen in de wereld van het toneel, de kunst en de architectuur. Binnen hun vriendschap blijft vooral Jude moeilijk te doorgronden. Hij vertelt weinig over zijn verleden, terwijl de gevolgen ervan steeds zichtbaarder worden. De roman volgt de vrienden over een lange periode en onderzoekt hoe nabijheid, zorg en liefde zich verhouden tot pijn die zich niet eenvoudig laat delen of oplossen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/739609/een-klein-leven.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-045"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2656:nl","key":{"work_id":2656,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/164146/de-waarheid-over-de-zaak-harry-quebert.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:58.119Z","sha256":"999264369128b26614e31a9f8812ec978a8aff43b2d460810ea5f87684311d15","isbn":"9789023477600","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789023477600 verschijningsdatum 23/12/2013 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint De Bezige Bij uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":2656,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1274,"text":"Schrijver Marcus Goldman zit vast met zijn werk wanneer zijn mentor Harry Quebert wordt verdacht van moord. In diens tuin is het lichaam gevonden van een meisje dat tientallen jaren eerder verdween. Bij haar ligt het manuscript van de roman die Harry beroemd maakte. Marcus vertrekt naar New Hampshire om te achterhalen wat er is gebeurd. Terwijl hij verhalen en herinneringen verzamelt, blijken zijn vertrouwen in zijn mentor en de geschiedenis van het boek steeds minder vanzelfsprekend.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/164146/de-waarheid-over-de-zaak-harry-quebert.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-046"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2672:nl","key":{"work_id":2672,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1183183/het-parfum.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:02.853Z","sha256":"c4ad584cc34e0163d4201d7fc6739d7daa0410107b65b50bcf7bcfbd3ac692a6","isbn":"9789044627718","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789044627718 verschijningsdatum 18/11/2014 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Prometheus uitgever Prometheus, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":2672,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1280,"text":"Jean-Baptiste Grenouille groeit op in het achttiende-eeuwse Parijs, waar geuren het dagelijks leven beheersen. Bij hemzelf ontbreekt een herkenbare lichaamsgeur, maar zijn verhouding tot de geuren om hem heen is uitzonderlijk. Zijn weg voert hem naar de wereld van parfumeurs en naar een steeds sterkere obsessie. De roman verbindt de drukte en het vuil van de stad met verlangen, afzondering en geweld. De lezer volgt een hoofdpersoon voor wie het gewone menselijke contact nauwelijks houvast biedt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1183183/het-parfum.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-047"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1054:nl","key":{"work_id":1054,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/155547/kom-hier-dat-ik-u-kus.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:05.597Z","sha256":"dd6d96d8acabe0fa71e19c08ff645bb956b88b815adc5279802c8425e49d4fa2","isbn":"9789044623109","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789044623109 verschijningsdatum 26/09/2014 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle uitgever Prometheus, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1054,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":648,"text":"Mona vertelt over haar leven op drie momenten: als kind, als vierentwintigjarige en als vijfendertigjarige. In haar relaties werken de verhoudingen uit haar gezin telkens door. Ze probeert rekening te houden met anderen, maar moet ook ontdekken wat zij zelf nodig heeft. De roman onderzoekt hoe zwijgen, geheimen en schuldgevoel tussen mensen kunnen groeien. Door de verschillende leeftijden naast elkaar te plaatsen wordt zichtbaar hoe patronen ontstaan en hoe moeilijk het is om er een eigen antwoord op te vinden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/155547/kom-hier-dat-ik-u-kus.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-048"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3547:nl","key":{"work_id":3547,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/75732/de-niet-verhoorde-gebeden-van-jacob-de-zoet.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T21:39:23.526Z","sha256":"dc138020050faff9ebaad07fb1c3d9b61656337b21143958c095f3bd0d291b06","isbn":"9789089530097","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789089530097 verschijningsdatum 01/05/2010 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Ailantus uitgever Park Uitgevers taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":3547,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1666,"text":"Boekhouder Jacob de Zoet vertrekt aan het einde van de achttiende eeuw naar Deshima, de Nederlandse handelspost bij Japan. Hij hoopt er geld te verdienen voor een huwelijk, maar moet ook corruptie binnen de handel aantonen. Dat maakt zijn positie kwetsbaar. Wanneer hij de vroedvrouw Orito ontmoet, worden zijn persoonlijke verlangens en zijn opdracht steeds moeilijker van elkaar te scheiden. De roman verbindt de afgesloten handelswereld met vragen over vertrouwen, macht, bedrog en de mogelijkheid van contact tussen verschillende werelden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/75732/de-niet-verhoorde-gebeden-van-jacob-de-zoet.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-050"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1099:nl","key":{"work_id":1099,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1198624/het-bloemenmeisje.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:19.368Z","sha256":"47429f5f499a4887ec94f442b59180b7f2e70e800fefee2ae4214d3fbd976474","isbn":"9789024593637","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789024593637 verschijningsdatum 18/06/2021 NUR 305 Literaire thriller imprint Luitingh Sijthoff uitgever Luitingh-Sijthoff B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1099,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":665,"text":"Als tiener wordt Nina bij het lichaam van haar moeder gevonden in de Franse Pyreneeën. De moord blijft onopgelost. Jaren later heeft zij een succesvol bestaan opgebouwd rond geneesmiddelen op basis van kruiden, maar over haar afkomst weet ze nog weinig. De ontdekking dat ze een tweelingzus heeft, brengt beide vrouwen op het spoor van hun moeder. Wanneer haar zus verdwijnt, verandert dat onderzoek in een zoektocht waarin het verleden opnieuw gevaarlijk dichtbij komt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1198624/het-bloemenmeisje.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-053"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1101:nl","key":{"work_id":1101,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1756137/de-nomade.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:35.763Z","sha256":"1b933d8361497fffd058a96284a870bb1e42d3eb0746f0d0c43c3394ccebfad0","isbn":"9789021032559","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789021032559 verschijningsdatum 28/05/2024 NUR 305 Literaire thriller imprint Luitingh Sijthoff uitgever Luitingh-Sijthoff B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1101,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":665,"text":"Documentairemaker Olga Liebke woont met haar vader in het Harz-gebergte. Hun band is hecht, maar wanneer hij dement wordt, vertelt hij dingen die niet passen bij wat zij over haar familie weet. Documenten uit de voormalige Sovjet-Unie vergroten haar twijfel. Olga besluit zijn verleden te onderzoeken en reist naar het grensgebied van Polen, Litouwen en Belarus. De thriller verbindt haar persoonlijke zoektocht met een geschiedenis die haar vader tot dan toe verborgen heeft gehouden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1756137/de-nomade.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-056"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1363:nl","key":{"work_id":1363,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1669072/nirwana.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:47.917Z","sha256":"bbe6dc92108a0501dd70459bf9f342650e1b75a8b7e88135993d93ec09473b1d","isbn":"9789403132877","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789403132877 verschijningsdatum 05/03/2024 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1363,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":643,"text":"Kunstenaar Hugo Adema komt uit een familie die groot werd in de offshore-industrie. Achter het succes staat zijn grootvader Willem, wiens rol in de Tweede Wereldoorlog tegenstrijdige verhalen heeft opgeleverd. Wanneer Hugo na een persoonlijke crisis terugkeert naar het familielandgoed, begint hij dat verleden te onderzoeken. Teruggevonden dagboeken maken het vertrouwde familiebeeld onzeker. De roman brengt een persoonlijke zoektocht samen met de manier waarop rijkdom, oorlog en herinnering tussen generaties blijven doorwerken.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1669072/nirwana.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-058"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1345:nl","key":{"work_id":1345,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1516259/het-lied-van-ooievaar-en-dromedaris.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:51.309Z","sha256":"79c3675bfafc26fc11dfd73a6e43426b42dadcc55007d5c821434e6cf6fb2cae","isbn":"9789054524106","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789054524106 verschijningsdatum 17/05/2022 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint Uitgeverij Passage uitgever Passage, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1345,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":721,"text":"Schrijfster Eliza May Drayden is al overleden wanneer deze roman in 1847 begint. Via de levens van anderen verschuift het verhaal steeds verder in de tijd. Haar aanvankelijk verguisde boek krijgt andere betekenissen, terwijl over haar eigen leven weinig met zekerheid bekend is. Biografieën, herinneringen en raadselachtige aantekeningen houden haar aanwezigheid levend. De roman onderzoekt hoe mensen een schrijver blijven lezen en verklaren, en hoe een werk zich kan losmaken van wat over zijn maker bekend is.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1516259/het-lied-van-ooievaar-en-dromedaris.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-059"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1350:nl","key":{"work_id":1350,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1710983/ik-kom-hier-nog-op-terug.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:54.063Z","sha256":"086223a49d909871613fd341a59ebc59beb5916b7939a0e40195b1a09b6ba990","isbn":"9789025475277","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789025475277 verschijningsdatum 14/11/2023 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint Atlas Contact uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1350,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":723,"text":"Journalist Rob Hollander bezoekt een vroegere studiegenoot in Los Angeles. Die biedt hem een onverwachte mogelijkheid: terugreizen in de tijd om fouten uit het verleden te herstellen. Tijdens de tocht die volgt, krijgt een gebeurtenis uit zijn jeugd een nieuwe betekenis. Ook oude studievrienden komen weer in beeld. De roman mengt het alledaagse met het onmogelijke en stelt vragen over herinnering, verbondenheid en het verlangen om een eenmaal afgelegd leven toch nog een andere richting te geven.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1710983/ik-kom-hier-nog-op-terug.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-060"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1616:nl","key":{"work_id":1616,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/360695/de-tweeling-grote-letter.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:58:07.583Z","sha256":"93594d685718243de1f065ba443410fe41cc891dee545b7dade69718c1bf793b","isbn":"9789029584494","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789029584494 Grootletterboek verschijningsdatum 13/02/2012 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint Oorsprong, Uitgeverij uitgever Singel Uitgeverijen taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1616,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":863,"text":"In een kuuroord ontmoeten twee oudere vrouwen elkaar en ontdekken dat zij tweelingzussen zijn. Lotte groeide in Nederland op, Anna in Duitsland. Hun gescheiden levens hebben hun verschillende ervaringen met de oorlog gegeven. Terwijl ze elkaar vertellen wat er is gebeurd, komen vertrouwde overtuigingen onder druk te staan. De roman onderzoekt hoe persoonlijke herinneringen zich verhouden tot een gedeelde geschiedenis en hoe moeilijk het is om de ander te begrijpen wanneer die aan de overkant van een historische scheidslijn heeft geleefd.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/360695/de-tweeling-grote-letter.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-063"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1162:nl","key":{"work_id":1162,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1387507/het-zwijgen-van-maria-zachea.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:58:15.024Z","sha256":"82ca47159d728bdc45dfe5972ab5f4de5a053399a7f289cef35c5cb632731c27","isbn":"9789045011929","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789045011929 verschijningsdatum 02/09/2008 NUR 320 Literaire non-fictie algemeen imprint Atlas uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1162,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":681,"text":"Na een hersenbloeding spreekt Maria Zachea nauwelijks meer. Haar twaalf kinderen nemen de zorg op zich, maar haar lange stilzwijgen roept ook vragen op over hun gezamenlijke verleden. Kleindochter Judith Koelemeijer onderzoekt wat de kinderen over hun moeder en over elkaar weten. Hun herinneringen aan dezelfde jeugd blijken niet gelijk. Het boek maakt van de familiegeschiedenis een onderzoek naar de verhoudingen binnen een groot gezin en naar wat gewone gesprekken jarenlang onbesproken kunnen laten.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1387507/het-zwijgen-van-maria-zachea.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-065"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:debuitenjongen::paolocognetti:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:debuitenjongen::paolocognetti","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1079845/de-buitenjongen.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:02.745Z","sha256":"f4f70ecc4cc95e091cec935397c0c5a4a1304e68e84af01ab640edc4337b9d88","isbn":"9789403128887","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789403128887 verschijningsdatum 02/03/2023 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:debuitenjongen::paolocognetti","language":"nl","bound_author_id":1022,"text":"Op zijn dertigste verruilt een man zijn leven in Milaan voor een afgelegen hut in de bergen. Het verblijf brengt niet onmiddellijk de rust waarop hij hoopte. Hij moet wennen aan het landschap, de seizoenen en een bestaan waarin zijn gebruikelijke zekerheden ontbreken. Ontmoetingen met andere bewoners geven zijn afzondering een ander karakter. Het boek beschrijft hoe een tijdelijk vertrek uit de stad uitgroeit tot een onderzoek naar de verhouding tussen een mens en zijn omgeving.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1079845/de-buitenjongen.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-033"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:detatoeeerdervanauschwitz::heathermorris:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:detatoeeerdervanauschwitz::heathermorris","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1440207/de-tatoeeerder-van-auschwitz.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:20.603Z","sha256":"932517e5c8f7ae08e3d3a56fcb4ae10cc4628c269e06f5dcce6a0f9e8dbf4a5d","isbn":"9789402729801","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789402729801 verschijningsdatum 08/04/2019 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint HarperCollins uitgever HarperCollins Holland taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:detatoeeerdervanauschwitz::heathermorris","language":"nl","bound_author_id":"@author:Heather Morris","text":"Lale wordt in 1942 naar Auschwitz gedeporteerd en krijgt er de taak nummers op de armen van medegevangenen te tatoeëren. Tijdens dat werk ontmoet hij Gita. Hun contact groeit onder omstandigheden waarin iedere ontmoeting risico''s met zich meebrengt. Het verhaal volgt hoe zij proberen elkaar niet kwijt te raken en een toekomst te blijven voorstellen. Deze historische roman verbindt hun relatie met het dagelijks overleven binnen het kamp; hij wordt niet als een rechtstreeks getuigenverslag gepresenteerd.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1440207/de-tatoeeerder-van-auschwitz.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-038"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:327:nl","key":{"work_id":327,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/164153/de-vliegeraar.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:56:37.280Z","sha256":"286d9043486c1b0aba097df627b002fe902dc2ceb8d23647b0f27265cfa831f3","isbn":"9789023477327","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789023477327 verschijningsdatum 03/05/2013 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":327,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":203,"text":"Amir en Hassan groeien samen op in Kabul, maar hun maatschappelijke posities zijn niet gelijk. Hun band wordt op de proef gesteld door een gebeurtenis die Amir niet loslaat. De veranderingen in Afghanistan brengen hem later ver van zijn jeugd. Wanneer hij de kans krijgt terug te kijken en iets recht te zetten, blijkt het verleden nauw verbonden met het heden. De roman volgt schuld, vriendschap en verantwoordelijkheid binnen een familiegeschiedenis die door oorlog en vlucht wordt veranderd.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/164153/de-vliegeraar.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-041"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:hetachtstelevenvoorbrilka::ninoharatischwili:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:hetachtstelevenvoorbrilka::ninoharatischwili","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1219105/het-achtste-leven-voor-brilka.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:08.994Z","sha256":"c1d159247fae485a40b0bc66f4add2c9cc2525c55d1c9511618e970fccc224d9","isbn":"9789025448417","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789025448417 verschijningsdatum 02/01/2017 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Atlas Contact uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:hetachtstelevenvoorbrilka::ninoharatischwili","language":"nl","bound_author_id":"@author:Nino Haratischwili","text":"Nitsa vertelt vanuit Berlijn de geschiedenis van haar Georgische familie aan Brilka. Het verhaal begint bij Stasia, de dochter van een chocolatier, en volgt meerdere generaties door de twintigste eeuw. Liefdes, familiebanden en persoonlijke verlangens worden telkens beïnvloed door politieke omwentelingen en geweld. Terwijl Nitsa de lotgevallen van haar voorouders reconstrueert, probeert ze te begrijpen wat hun geschiedenis voor de jongste generatie betekent. De roman verbindt een omvangrijke familiegeschiedenis met de veranderingen in Georgië en daarbuiten.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1219105/het-achtste-leven-voor-brilka.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-049"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:alhetblauwvandehemel::melissadacosta:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:alhetblauwvandehemel::melissadacosta","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1791920/al-het-blauw-van-de-hemel.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:13.337Z","sha256":"321f1d93524e5abc982c88f3fe63d6c0263c5c16403f4e79d64bc26d24f99030","isbn":"9789022340479","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789022340479 verschijningsdatum 07/03/2024 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Manteau uitgever Standaard Uitgeverij - Algemeen taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:alhetblauwvandehemel::melissadacosta","language":"nl","bound_author_id":718,"text":"Émile krijgt op jonge leeftijd de diagnose alzheimer en wil de tijd die hem rest niet alleen in het ziekenhuis doorbrengen. Via een advertentie zoekt hij iemand die met hem in een camper wil reizen. Joanne reageert en vertrekt met hem, zonder veel over haar eigen verleden te vertellen. Onderweg leren ze elkaars gewoonten en stiltes kennen. De roman volgt hoe een onverwacht reisgezelschap ontstaat terwijl ziekte, verlies en de behoefte aan vrijheid steeds aanwezig blijven.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1791920/al-het-blauw-van-de-hemel.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-051"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:gaalseenrivier::shelleyread:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:gaalseenrivier::shelleyread","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/2085799/ga-als-een-rivier-special-bruna-2026.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:16.558Z","sha256":"1fc6aeefc9b5fef2da043ba887fec2017d22d34c873f8350414310ae5cb27459","isbn":"9789021036991","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789021036991 verschijningsdatum 12/04/2023 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Luitingh Sijthoff uitgever Luitingh-Sijthoff B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:gaalseenrivier::shelleyread","language":"nl","bound_author_id":"@author:Shelley Read","text":"Victoria Nash groeit op in een familie die in Colorado perziken verbouwt. In 1949 ontmoet ze een jonge vreemdeling, en die ontmoeting verandert haar verhouding tot het leven dat voor haar leek vast te liggen. Wanneer ze zich uit haar vertrouwde omgeving terugtrekt, moet ze zelfstandig een weg vinden. De roman verbindt haar persoonlijke keuzes met het berglandschap en met de gemeenschap waaruit ze afkomstig is. Verlies en de mogelijkheid opnieuw te beginnen blijven haar verhaal bepalen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/2085799/ga-als-een-rivier-special-bruna-2026.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-052"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:vrijuitzicht::anyaniewierra:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:vrijuitzicht::anyaniewierra","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/276006/vrij-uitzicht.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:22.358Z","sha256":"4a0c0e9e4ab640ba8862fcf44f1c36fdb64c069f6af72c7163968e45615a92d2","isbn":"9789024592104","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789024592104 verschijningsdatum 25/09/2020 NUR 305 Literaire thriller imprint Luitingh Sijthoff uitgever Luitingh-Sijthoff B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:vrijuitzicht::anyaniewierra","language":"nl","bound_author_id":665,"text":"Tess Clement keert na vijfentwintig jaar terug naar Mosset, het Franse dorp waar zij is opgegroeid. Een bouwproject rond een landgoed dreigt de omgeving te veranderen. Haar terugkomst roept ook vragen op over gebeurtenissen uit het verleden, waaronder een verdwijning die niet is opgelost. Terwijl Tess probeert te achterhalen wat er speelt, raken oude banden en nieuwe belangen met elkaar verweven. De thriller volgt hoe haar persoonlijke geschiedenis de actuele conflicten in het dorp ingewikkelder maakt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/276006/vrij-uitzicht.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-054"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:deengelenmaker::stefanbrijs:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:deengelenmaker::stefanbrijs","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/127933/de-engelenmaker.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:58:12.014Z","sha256":"e0911b403fed17d5a4734398d3df3c2e11e3a1054eb3abb51d1f0c7ce9257ec6","isbn":"9789045020068","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789045020068 verschijningsdatum 05/10/2011 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint Atlas uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:deengelenmaker::stefanbrijs","language":"nl","bound_author_id":3313,"text":"Victor Hoppe keert terug naar het dorp Wolfheim met drie kleine kinderen. Zijn komst trekt de aandacht van de bewoners, die vragen hebben over de kinderen en over zijn verleden. Terwijl zij proberen te begrijpen wie hun nieuwe buurman is, blijkt zijn geschiedenis steeds belangrijker. De roman verbindt het leven in het dorp met vragen over wetenschap, geloof en de grenzen van menselijk handelen. Vertrouwen en argwaan veranderen gaandeweg de manier waarop de betrokkenen elkaar bekijken.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/127933/de-engelenmaker.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-064"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:totindehemel::richardpowers:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:totindehemel::richardpowers","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1102340/tot-in-de-hemel.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:58:18.096Z","sha256":"3c895a2c8b7894184d53527b1d4c2cce956b185cde4b9e47934522b0a9070ec5","isbn":"9789025452773","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789025452773 verschijningsdatum 22/08/2018 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Atlas Contact uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:totindehemel::richardpowers","language":"nl","bound_author_id":3281,"text":"Negen mensen raken ieder op hun eigen manier betrokken bij bomen en bossen. Een familie houdt een boom fotografisch bij, een wetenschapper onderzoekt het leven van bomen en anderen komen in aanraking met de strijd om oude bossen te behouden. Hun afzonderlijke verhalen groeien naar elkaar toe. De roman zet de korte duur van een mensenleven naast de veel langere tijd van een landschap. Zo ontstaan vragen over verbondenheid, bescherming en wat mensen in hun omgeving over het hoofd zien.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1102340/tot-in-de-hemel.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-066"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:43:nl","key":{"work_id":43,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/311064/honderd-jaar-eenzaamheid.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:58:25.947Z","sha256":"6b695061434cdab554ac6ea3d75e0337348b2538fa29268eb8b51308fb5be3ac","isbn":"9789029090452","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789029090452 verschijningsdatum 26/09/2014 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Meulenhoff uitgever Meulenhoff Boekerij B.V. taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":43,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":35,"text":"De familie Buendía staat centraal in de geschiedenis van Macondo. Over meerdere generaties keren namen, verlangens en conflicten terug, terwijl de nederzetting voortdurend verandert. Persoonlijke gebeurtenissen raken verweven met politieke strijd en met ontwikkelingen van buiten het dorp. Het bijzondere en het alledaagse bestaan in deze roman naast elkaar. Door een eeuw familiegeschiedenis te volgen, onderzoekt het verhaal hoe herinnering, herhaling en afzondering vorm geven aan het leven van de bewoners en aan hun beeld van het verleden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/311064/honderd-jaar-eenzaamheid.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-069"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:197:nl","key":{"work_id":197,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/186727/het-laatste-rijk.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:58:45.156Z","sha256":"fe592e12539b4b8db37fe99b956557be85759ac2f71f51464314bd6c03a47538","isbn":"9789024581269","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789024581269 verschijningsdatum 28/11/2017 NUR 334 Fantasy imprint Luitingh Sijthoff uitgever Luitingh-Sijthoff B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":197,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":19,"text":"In een wereld waar as uit de lucht valt, regeert een schijnbaar onaantastbare heerser. Kelsier verzamelt een groep die zijn bewind wil ondermijnen. Vin, een jonge dief die heeft geleerd niemand te vertrouwen, raakt bij hun plannen betrokken. Ze ontdekt dat metalen bijzondere vermogens kunnen ontsluiten en moet leren die te gebruiken. De roman verbindt haar ontwikkeling met een riskante onderneming waarin vertrouwen, sociale verhoudingen en de verborgen basis van de macht een belangrijke rol spelen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/186727/het-laatste-rijk.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-074"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:16:nl","key":{"work_id":16,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/935666/fahrenheit-451.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:58:58.803Z","sha256":"7839c5d59062d160488094fddeeb7b6ca51fa0febc138200df252cb25422c32c","isbn":"9789048855742","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789048855742 verschijningsdatum 18/12/2019 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Lebowski uitgever Overamstel Uitgevers taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":16,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":13,"text":"Guy Montag werkt als brandweerman in een samenleving waar zijn taak niet het blussen van branden is, maar het verbranden van boeken. Aanvankelijk volgt hij de regels van dat bestaan. Ontmoetingen en gebeurtenissen brengen hem echter aan het twijfelen over de wereld waarin hij leeft. Hij begint belangstelling te krijgen voor wat hij geacht wordt te vernietigen. De roman onderzoekt hoe een samenleving omgaat met kennis, afleiding en afwijkende gedachten, en wat het betekent om zelfstandig te lezen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/935666/fahrenheit-451.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-077"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:9:nl","key":{"work_id":9,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/876755/verhaal-van-de-dienstmaagd.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:59:03.312Z","sha256":"46574f34fb26ee37dc44b732881693d57480c4c500d1eb0905c8c0841a10291b","isbn":"9789044634280","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789044634280 verschijningsdatum 20/02/2017 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Prometheus uitgever Prometheus, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":9,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":8,"text":"In Gilead wordt het leven van vrouwen streng door de staat geregeld. Vanfred is een dienstmaagd die bij een invloedrijk gezin wordt geplaatst om een kind te krijgen. Haar bestaan wordt bepaald door toezicht, vaste rituelen en de herinnering aan een leven waarin zij andere mogelijkheden had. Ze probeert te begrijpen wie nog te vertrouwen is en waar ruimte voor verzet bestaat. De roman laat vanuit haar beperkte positie zien hoe politieke macht het dagelijks leven en persoonlijke relaties binnendringt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/876755/verhaal-van-de-dienstmaagd.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-078"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2718:nl","key":{"work_id":2718,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/127860/laat-me-nooit-alleen.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:59:06.250Z","sha256":"d971274504a25843eddf58f516806f6cf886cff59fbd017dc4527a35e80a0db4","isbn":"9789025452483","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789025452483 verschijningsdatum 13/10/2017 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle imprint Atlas Contact uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":2718,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":172,"text":"Kathy kijkt terug op haar jeugd met Ruth en Tommy op een bijzondere Engelse kostschool. Hun herinneringen aan lessen, vriendschappen en onderlinge spanningen krijgen later een andere betekenis. Terwijl de drie ouder worden, moeten ze zich verhouden tot verwachtingen over hun toekomst die ze als kind maar gedeeltelijk begrepen. De roman bouwt vanuit gewone herinneringen een steeds ongemakkelijker beeld op van hun wereld. Zorg, liefde en het verlangen naar een eigen leven blijven daarbij nauw met elkaar verbonden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/127860/laat-me-nooit-alleen.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-079"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1942:nl","key":{"work_id":1942,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/162030/het-ontstaan-van-soorten.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:59:16.905Z","sha256":"4e7dc9a9c378d5f2febe606edcbe785617fddc477e66a937a424222770b48893","isbn":"9789057122545","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789057122545 verschijningsdatum 28/11/2007 NUR 911 Algemene naturwetenschappen uitgever Nieuwezijds b.v., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1942,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":983,"text":"Darwin onderzoekt hoe soorten kunnen veranderen en hoe verschillen tussen organismen ontstaan en blijven bestaan. Hij bespreekt waarnemingen uit de natuur naast ervaringen met het fokken van planten en dieren. Zijn redenering verbindt variatie, erfelijkheid en de omstandigheden waaronder organismen leven. Deze Nederlandse editie vertaalt de door Darwin herziene tekst uit 1872. Het boek wordt daarmee als een historische wetenschappelijke uiteenzetting gepresenteerd, niet als een hedendaags handboek dat alle latere biologische kennis omvat.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/162030/het-ontstaan-van-soorten.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-081"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1442:nl","key":{"work_id":1442,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1105230/simpel.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:59:21.390Z","sha256":"afa21a315200258e0facf137333a4bde2d03c3fc27cc00cb8ff5b4401e8da133","isbn":"9789464042818","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789464042818 verschijningsdatum 12/09/2023 NUR 440 Eten en drinken algemeen imprint Fontaine Uitgevers uitgever Park Uitgevers taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1442,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":763,"text":"Ottolenghi verzamelt ruim honderd recepten rond het idee dat koken op verschillende manieren eenvoudiger kan worden. Sommige gerechten vragen weinig voorbereiding, andere hebben een korte ingrediëntenlijst of kunnen grotendeels vooraf worden gemaakt. Symbolen helpen de lezer bij het kiezen van een aanpak die bij de beschikbare tijd past. De nadruk ligt op gerechten en combinaties van smaken, niet op één vaste kookmethode. Het is een kookboek en geen verhalend boek dat door deze catalogusaanvulling automatisch voor de smaaktest geschikt wordt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1105230/simpel.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-082"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:oersterk::richarddeleth:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:oersterk::richarddeleth","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/93042/oersterk.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:59:30.314Z","sha256":"466fe1216ef2a96a307a435dc4154e4948a17609e57801dddd7c2d671f551237","isbn":"9789081899000","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789081899000 verschijningsdatum 11/06/2012 NUR 860 Gezondheid algemeen imprint Leth, Uitgeverij Richard de uitgever Vrije Uitgevers, De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:oersterk::richarddeleth","language":"nl","bound_author_id":"@author:Richard de Leth","text":"Richard de Leth bespreekt zijn opvattingen over voeding, beweging en leefgewoonten. Hij verbindt dagelijkse keuzes met zijn ideeën over lichamelijk en geestelijk functioneren en geeft praktische aanwijzingen voor het aanpassen van een leefstijl. Het boek is opgebouwd als een benadering van gezondheid vanuit die eigen visie. Deze beschrijving geeft het onderwerp weer en bevestigt geen medische werkzaamheid. De adviezen moeten niet worden gelezen als een individuele diagnose of als vervanging van passende professionele gezondheidszorg.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/93042/oersterk.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-084"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:90:nl","key":{"work_id":90,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1706368/de-zin-van-het-bestaan.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:59:46.870Z","sha256":"3a995b732dcd264d3d15122771be6edef3a6b269b4e33723afd820408644619d","isbn":"9789061001737","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789061001737 verschijningsdatum NUR 770 Psychologie algemeen uitgever Donker B.V., Uitgeversmaatschappij Ad. taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":90,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":77,"text":"Viktor Frankl beschrijft ervaringen uit de concentratiekampen en verbindt die met zijn denken over betekenis in het leven. Hij vraagt hoe mensen zich tot omstandigheden kunnen verhouden wanneer hun handelingsruimte sterk is ingeperkt. Het boek combineert persoonlijke herinneringen met een uiteenzetting van zijn psychologische benadering, de logotherapie. De nadruk ligt op het zoeken naar zin onder moeilijke omstandigheden. Het is zowel een historisch getuigenis als een presentatie van Frankls eigen ideeën, niet een belofte dat ieder probleem daarmee kan worden opgelost.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1706368/de-zin-van-het-bestaan.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-088"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:107:nl","key":{"work_id":107,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1185011/elementaire-gewoontes.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:59:51.576Z","sha256":"166640c289d63bdec7ffe5649ffd610b238b7e65139c04be51177e5dd335baad","isbn":"9789400511415","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789400511415 verschijningsdatum 03/06/2019 NUR 770 Psychologie algemeen imprint Lev. uitgever Bruna Uitgevers B.V., A.W. taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":107,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":93,"text":"James Clear beschrijft hoe kleine, herhaalde handelingen kunnen uitgroeien tot vaste gewoonten. Hij bespreekt onder meer de invloed van de omgeving, het zichtbaar maken van gewenst gedrag en het minder vanzelfsprekend maken van ongewenste routines. De nadruk ligt op systemen in het dagelijks leven in plaats van alleen op einddoelen. Het boek biedt voorbeelden en praktische stappen om gedrag te onderzoeken en aan te passen. Deze samenvatting beschrijft de aanpak, zonder een bepaald resultaat voor iedere lezer te garanderen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1185011/elementaire-gewoontes.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-089"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:deepdemocracy::jitskekramer:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:deepdemocracy::jitskekramer","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1011530/deep-democracy.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:59:54.748Z","sha256":"7c8905bd189c5d00d741aeda4b5e92690c0479ba916f712cd38bfa36c72ec771","isbn":"9789058719324","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789058719324 verschijningsdatum 06/10/2014 NUR 801 Management algemeen uitgever Uitgeverij Thema taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":"@work:deepdemocracy::jitskekramer","language":"nl","bound_author_id":"@author:Jitske Kramer","text":"Jitske Kramer bespreekt hoe groepen besluiten nemen en wat er gebeurt met standpunten die daarbij minder steun krijgen. Vanuit de Lewis-methode onderzoekt ze hoe afwijkende stemmen kunnen worden gehoord voordat een besluit wordt uitgevoerd. Voorbeelden en werkvormen richten zich op gesprekken, spanningen en samenwerking binnen teams. Het boek beschrijft een werkwijze voor groepsprocessen, geen garantie dat ieder conflict verdwijnt. De aandacht voor minderheidsstandpunten staat naast de vraag hoe een groep uiteindelijk tot een uitvoerbaar gezamenlijk besluit komt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1011530/deep-democracy.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-090"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1450:nl","key":{"work_id":1450,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/135562/bonita-avenue.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T21:00:00.678Z","sha256":"a83fb81c36b1870b798288aa20255377bae438bce70251602cfc5013a4e6b3d6","isbn":"9789023475705","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789023475705 verschijningsdatum 01/10/2012 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle uitgever Bezige Bij b.v., Uitgeverij De taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1450,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":769,"text":"Siem Sigerius lijkt een geslaagd leven te hebben opgebouwd en staat aan het hoofd van een technische universiteit. De levens van zijn stiefdochter Joni en haar vriend Aaron raken met zijn wereld verweven. Tegen de achtergrond van Twente en de gebeurtenissen rond de vuurwerkramp blijken familieverhoudingen en zorgvuldig opgebouwde beelden minder stabiel dan ze lijken. De roman vertelt vanuit verschillende perspectieven hoe geheimen, ambities en onderling wantrouwen een gezin onder druk zetten en hoe herinneringen elkaar daarbij tegenspreken.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/135562/bonita-avenue.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-091"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1644:nl","key":{"work_id":1644,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/482367/hersenschimmen.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T21:00:03.539Z","sha256":"ae16abf5a5237f5e92fff3e5f44dcbe6194bdd3dbc81541153961ecf0e41f5d4","isbn":"9789021433776","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789021433776 verschijningsdatum 08/05/2008 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle uitgever Singel Uitgeverijen taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1644,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":874,"text":"Maarten Klein merkt dat zijn herinneringen niet meer samenvallen met wat er om hem heen gebeurt. Gewone situaties worden onzeker en vertrouwde mensen krijgen soms een andere plaats in zijn gedachten. Zijn vrouw probeert hem in het dagelijks leven bij te staan, terwijl zijn eigen beleving steeds verder verandert. De roman blijft dicht bij Maartens perspectief. Daardoor ervaart de lezer hoe taal, tijd en herkenning hun vanzelfsprekendheid verliezen en hoe moeilijk het wordt om een gedeelde werkelijkheid vast te houden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/482367/hersenschimmen.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-092"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1165:nl","key":{"work_id":1165,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1596000/het-zijn-net-mensen.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T21:00:11.008Z","sha256":"995781970d5be74b339cb8aba8c5603bfe3acc941607625d4e2e1c7a660dac33","isbn":"9789493304741","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789493304741 verschijningsdatum 25/01/2024 NUR 320 Literaire non-fictie algemeen imprint Uitgeverij Pluim uitgever Uitgeverij Pluim taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1165,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":682,"text":"Joris Luyendijk kijkt terug op zijn werk als correspondent in het Midden-Oosten. Hij vergelijkt wat hij ter plaatse meemaakt met het beeld dat nieuwsberichten kunnen overbrengen. Gesprekken, journalistieke routines en beperkingen van de toegang tot informatie spelen daarbij een rol. Het boek onderzoekt hoe verslaggeving tot stand komt en welke onderdelen van een samenleving buiten beeld blijven. Het presenteert zijn ervaringen en kritiek op nieuwsproductie, niet één volledig of neutraal overzicht van alle landen en conflicten in de regio.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1596000/het-zijn-net-mensen.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-094"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:455:nl","key":{"work_id":455,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1429964/dog-man-1-dog-man.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T21:00:27.597Z","sha256":"29763c61f075eb517de0ea7fe7926a6e8e2ada66e75f6d729a3965682837bc0c","isbn":"9789492899019","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789492899019 Nieuwe editie verschijningsdatum 14/06/2018 NUR 282 Fictie 7-9 jaar 280 Fictie kinder- en jeugdboeken algemeen imprint Condor uitgever WPG Kindermedia taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":455,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":283,"text":"Wanneer een politieagent en zijn hond bij een ongeluk gewond raken, ontstaat door een bijzondere operatie Dog Man. Hij combineert eigenschappen van een mens en een hond en probeert als agent zijn werk te doen. Dat levert problemen op wanneer zijn hondeninstinct het overneemt. Tegelijk krijgt hij te maken met tegenstanders, onder wie de kat Karel. Dit eerste stripboek vertelt zijn avonturen met tekeningen, korte scènes en humor, en vormt het begin van de reeks.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1429964/dog-man-1-dog-man.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-098"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1451:nl","key":{"work_id":1451,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/385958/de-gorgels.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T21:00:33.686Z","sha256":"1d52e0bb9b1153dd5ec6da07520020415d0ee58e69a6cf6b0847e656b4a76842","isbn":"9789025867898","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789025867898 Nieuwe editie verschijningsdatum 02/09/2015 NUR 281 Fictie 4-6 jaar 282 Fictie 7-9 jaar imprint Leopold uitgever WPG Kindermedia taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1451,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":770,"text":"Melle ziet op een nacht een klein harig wezen op de rand van zijn bed. Hij kijkt anders naar de wereld dan veel mensen om hem heen en probeert te begrijpen wat hij heeft ontdekt. Zijn ontmoeting opent de deur naar het leven van de Gorgels, terwijl volwassenen niet zomaar geloven wat hij vertelt. Het verhaal combineert zijn nieuwsgierigheid met een fantasiewereld die dicht bij het gewone gezinsleven ligt. De illustraties van Rick de Haas maken deel uit van deze kinderboekeditie.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/385958/de-gorgels.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-099"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1264:nl","key":{"work_id":1264,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1711370/het-dossier.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:29.907Z","sha256":"5464678d7badd354219e8e504558be13766698da0b80f9d7420780640011f2a7","isbn":"9789021042503","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789021042503 verschijningsdatum 31/10/2023 NUR 332 Thriller imprint Luitingh Sijthoff uitgever Luitingh-Sijthoff B.V., Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"}],"work_id":1264,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":665,"text":"Josta Bresse heeft een teruggetrokken bestaan opgebouwd wanneer geweld haar opnieuw met het verleden confronteert. Haar vroegere leven in de DDR en haar werk met vervalsingen krijgen een onverwachte betekenis. Een dossier brengt oude verbanden aan het licht en maakt onzeker wie zij nog kan vertrouwen. De thriller verbindt haar persoonlijke geschiedenis met de nasleep van een verdwenen staatsapparaat. Josta moet onderzoeken welke informatie over haar is vastgelegd en waarom anderen daar nu belang bij hebben.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1711370/het-dossier.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-055"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:@work:luister::sachabronwasser:nl","key":{"work_id":"@work:luister::sachabronwasser","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1820180/luister-limited-edition.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:57:40.252Z","sha256":"a59408207a390fc9384777895b769c9799bf7623a37cec70b8955d5e26ed59f9","isbn":"9789026352065","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789026352065 verschijningsdatum 08/02/2023 NUR 301 Literaire roman, novelle imprint Ambo|Anthos uitgever Ambo/Anthos B.V. taal Nederlands"},{"url":"https://www.amboanthos.nl/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Aanbiedingsbrochure-AmboAnthos-voorjaar-2024.pdf","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","role":"summary_content_source"}],"work_id":"@work:luister::sachabronwasser","language":"nl","bound_author_id":1166,"text":"Marie vertrekt in 1989 uit Nederland en gaat als au pair werken in Parijs. De nieuwe taal, de stad en het gezin waarin ze terechtkomt, vragen een ingrijpende aanpassing. Jaren later brengen de aanslagen van 2015 haar verleden opnieuw dichtbij, omdat haar vroegere docent Flo erbij betrokken is. Marie probeert de geschiedenis van hun verhouding te ontwarren. De roman verbindt twee perioden in Parijs en onderzoekt hoe herinneringen, afhankelijkheid en schuld de betekenis van eerdere gebeurtenissen veranderen.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Officiële uitgever","source_url":"https://www.amboanthos.nl/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Aanbiedingsbrochure-AmboAnthos-voorjaar-2024.pdf","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-057"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1171:nl","key":{"work_id":1171,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1545562/wij-zijn-ons-brein.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:59:36.412Z","sha256":"e9ae99eb286ce8d812a64b4085b36f19680de4f01e3daef371d94481251b8f28","isbn":"9789025439149","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789025439149 verschijningsdatum 07/03/2012 NUR 870 Geneeskunde algemeen imprint Atlas Contact uitgever Atlas Contact, Uitgeverij taal Nederlands"},{"url":"https://uitgeverijpluim.nl/media/catalog/product/book_preview/Inkijkex_Jij_bent_je_brein.pdf","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","role":"author_authority"}],"work_id":1171,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":685,"text":"Dick Swaab bespreekt het menselijk brein vanaf de ontwikkeling voor de geboorte tot veranderingen op latere leeftijd. Hij verbindt hersenonderzoek met uiteenlopende onderwerpen uit het dagelijks leven en met vragen over gedrag, identiteit en aandoeningen. Het boek presenteert zijn visie op de rol van de hersenen in wat mensen doen en ervaren. Deze beschrijving vat het onderwerp samen en geeft geen persoonlijk medisch advies. De besproken verklaringen moeten worden gelezen in de context van de auteur en de publicatie.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1545562/wij-zijn-ons-brein.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-086"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:10172:nl","key":{"work_id":10172,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/353100/oblomov.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T21:00:15.888Z","sha256":"38fa0302ea1ee6e7a6a875c9d92b11bdb8109a8e486eb2529c83aa8a25c55513","isbn":"9789028212381","facts":"Hardback ISBN 9789028212381 verschijningsdatum 06/07/2021 NUR 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle uitgever Uitgeverij G.A. Van Oorschot B.V. taal Nederlands"},{"url":"https://ci.nii.ac.jp/ncid/BC09520143","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","role":"author_authority"}],"work_id":10172,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":5656,"text":"Ilja Iljitsj Oblomov leidt een teruggetrokken bestaan en stelt beslissingen steeds opnieuw uit. Zijn positie als landeigenaar biedt hem ruimte om weinig te ondernemen, maar praktische problemen verdwijnen daardoor niet. Mensen om hem heen proberen hem in beweging te krijgen, terwijl liefde en vriendschap nieuwe verwachtingen meebrengen. De roman onderzoekt het verschil tussen plannen en handelen. Oblomovs verlangen naar rust staat voortdurend tegenover een wereld die verandering verlangt en waarin ook nietsdoen gevolgen blijkt te hebben.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/353100/oblomov.html","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary"},"origin":"NL100-095"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1284:nl","key":{"work_id":1284,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1284,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":713,"text":"Tijdens een vakantie in Umbrië verdwijnt Nienkes moeder Carolien, die alzheimer heeft. Haar spoor leidt naar Florence. Met een medaillon als aanwijzing probeert Nienke te achterhalen wat er is gebeurd.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"A.W. Bruna Uitgevers","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/souvenir/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/souvenir/","checkedAt":"2026-10-21","isbn":"9789044978834","role":"Existing reviewed original source summary; not newly generated"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:253:en","key":{"work_id":253,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":253,"language":"en","bound_author_id":125,"text":"After the war, Nesta Archeron struggles with becoming High Fae and finding her place in the Night Court. Training with Cassian forces her to face old wounds, while a renewed threat puts their court at risk.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Bloomsbury","source_url":"https://www.bloomsbury.com/au/court-of-silver-flames-9781526602312/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.bloomsbury.com/au/court-of-silver-flames-9781526602312/","checkedAt":"2026-10-23","isbn":"9781526602312","role":"Existing reviewed original source summary; not newly generated"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:148:en","key":{"work_id":148,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":148,"language":"en","bound_author_id":21,"text":"Polly and Digory unexpectedly reach Narnia. Their adventure explains how travel between Narnia and our world began.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"NSW Department of Education","source_url":"https://online.education.nsw.gov.au/prc/booklist/listBooksByTitle.html?letter=M&levelId=3","evidence":[{"url":"https://online.education.nsw.gov.au/prc/booklist/listBooksByTitle.html?letter=M&levelId=3","checkedAt":"2026-10-23","isbn":"9780064471107","role":"Existing reviewed original source summary; not newly generated"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:228:en","key":{"work_id":228,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":228,"language":"en","bound_author_id":120,"text":"Lyra and Will face a dangerous journey as Lord Asriel’s rebellion draws forces from many worlds into conflict. Their choices become central to the fate of the living and the dead.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Penguin Random House","source_url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/136441/his-dark-materials-the-amber-spyglass-book-3-by-philip-pullman/9780440418566/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/136441/his-dark-materials-the-amber-spyglass-book-3-by-philip-pullman/9780440418566/","checkedAt":"2026-10-23","isbn":"9780440418566","role":"Existing reviewed original source summary; not newly generated"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:553:en","key":{"work_id":553,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":553,"language":"en","bound_author_id":339,"text":"A housemaid takes a job with the wealthy Garricks, hoping to keep her past hidden. The mysterious absence of Mrs Garrick and signs of distress lead her to investigate what is happening behind a closed bedroom door.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Bookouture","source_url":"https://bookouture.com/books/2903/","evidence":[{"url":"https://bookouture.com/books/2903/","checkedAt":"2026-10-23","isbn":"9781837901326","role":"Existing reviewed original source summary; not newly generated"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1:nl","key":{"work_id":1,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1,"text":"Ver van de aarde ontwaakt Ryland Grace in een ruimteschip, zonder te weten hoe hij daar is terechtgekomen. Langzaam ontdekt hij dat hij als enige bemanningslid nog leeft en dat zijn opdracht van belang is voor het voortbestaan van de mensheid. Terwijl zijn herinneringen terugkomen, moet hij een onbekend wetenschappelijk gevaar onderzoeken. Zijn beperkte middelen en de grote afstand tot huis maken iedere beslissing onzeker.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Penguin Random House","source_url":"https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/440237/project-hail-mary-by-weir-andy/9781807840020","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/440237/project-hail-mary-by-weir-andy/9781807840020","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Ryland Grace wakes on a spacecraft without his memory","Only surviving crew member","Scientific investigation concerns survival of Earth"],"role":"Same underlying novel, not evidence that selected edition ISBN or publication date changed"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1:en","key":{"work_id":1,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1,"text":"Far from Earth, Ryland Grace wakes on a spacecraft without knowing what brought him there. He gradually discovers that he is the only surviving member of a mission whose outcome could determine humanity’s survival. Recovering his memories is only part of the problem: he must also understand an unfamiliar scientific threat. The novel follows his attempts to investigate it with the limited resources available to him.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Penguin Random House","source_url":"https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/440237/project-hail-mary-by-weir-andy/9781807840020","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/440237/project-hail-mary-by-weir-andy/9781807840020","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Ryland Grace wakes on a spacecraft without his memory","Only surviving crew member","Scientific investigation concerns survival of Earth"],"role":"Same underlying novel, not evidence that selected edition ISBN or publication date changed"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6:nl","key":{"work_id":6,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":6,"text":"Bilbo Balings leidt een rustig leven wanneer de tovenaar Gandalf en dertien dwergen hem voor een onverwachte onderneming benaderen. De dwergen willen hun verloren schat terugvinden, die door de draak Smaug wordt bewaakt. Bilbo gaat mee, hoewel hij weinig ervaring met avontuur heeft. Onderweg moet hij zich redden in situaties die ver van zijn vertrouwde huis liggen. Zijn rol binnen het gezelschap verandert terwijl de reis hem laat ontdekken welke moed en vindingrijkheid hij bezit.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/162568/de-hobbit.html","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/162568/de-hobbit.html","isbn":"9789022561942","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789022561942 verschijningsdatum 25/07/2011 NUR 334 Fantasy 302 Vertaalde literaire roman, novelle uitgever Meulenhoff Boekerij B.V. taal Nederlands","sha256":"30fc061d3c08579ef254c1bbdd84b861d0e2d80088fe053ba281497c869bbb6f","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:58:39.262Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6:en","key":{"work_id":6,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6,"language":"en","bound_author_id":6,"text":"Bilbo Baggins is drawn away from his quiet home when Gandalf and a company of dwarves ask him to join their expedition. They want to recover treasure guarded by the dragon Smaug, but reaching it means crossing unfamiliar and dangerous places. Bilbo must take on responsibilities he never expected. The adventure tests whether someone who values comfort can find a place among companions with a very different purpose.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/162568/de-hobbit.html","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/162568/de-hobbit.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Bilbo joins Gandalf and a company of dwarves","Journey concerns treasure guarded by Smaug","Comfortable home contrasts with dangerous journey"],"role":"Exact Dutch print edition already reviewed in pilot; Work synopsis applies to original novel, not to a retelling or sampler"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:8:nl","key":{"work_id":8,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":8,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":7,"text":"De familie Atreides krijgt het bestuur over Arrakis, een woestijnplaneet waar een zeldzame specerij wordt gewonnen. Die grondstof maakt de planeet belangrijk voor de machtsverhoudingen in het rijk. Paul Atreides raakt verwikkeld in een strijd waarin rivaliserende families, religie en het leven van de woestijnbewoners samenkomen. De roman volgt hoe politieke belangen en de bijzondere omstandigheden van Arrakis zijn toekomst bepalen. Overleven vraagt er niet alleen macht, maar ook begrip van een kwetsbare omgeving.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1318002/duin.html","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1318002/duin.html","isbn":"9789038817996","facts":"Paperback ISBN 9789038817996 verschijningsdatum 16/07/2026 NUR 333 Science fiction imprint Mint Books uitgever Singel Uitgeverijen taal Nederlands","sha256":"69bd8907f5630f4b7d3f08dc3e351ec2a91ecf59e8019f59384b07d1cdd2245b","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:58:42.257Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:8:en","key":{"work_id":8,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":8,"language":"en","bound_author_id":7,"text":"Paul Atreides arrives on the desert planet Arrakis with a family entrusted with governing a valuable and contested territory. Control of its spice brings competing powers into conflict, while the harsh environment makes survival a struggle of its own. As his family’s position becomes dangerous, Paul must understand the people and forces around him. The novel connects his choices with wider questions about power, belief and scarce resources.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1318002/duin.html","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1318002/duin.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Paul Atreides and his family move to Arrakis","Desert planet and valuable spice","Political power, scarce resources and survival"],"role":"Exact Dutch edition and same Work identity reviewed in pilot; not a replacement of the English Gollancz ISBN"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:30:nl","key":{"work_id":30,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":30,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":24,"text":"Een grote ramp treft de Stillness, een wereld die geregeld door verwoestende veranderingen wordt geteisterd. Voor Essun valt de ontwrichting samen met een persoonlijk verlies: haar zoon is gedood en haar dochter is verdwenen. Ze gaat op zoek naar het kind, terwijl de strijd om voedsel en veiligheid steeds heviger wordt. Haar reis voert door een samenleving waarin angst voor de krachten van de aarde het leven van mensen bepaalt.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Orbit / Hachette","source_url":"https://www.hachette.co.uk/titles/n-k-jemisin/the-fifth-season/9780356508191/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.hachette.co.uk/titles/n-k-jemisin/the-fifth-season/9780356508191/","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Stillness experiences catastrophic geological upheaval","Essun loses her son and searches for her missing daughter","Survival and conflict over scarce resources"],"role":"Publisher and author confirm the same novel; alternate UK ISBN is source identity, not a catalog edition substitution"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:30:en","key":{"work_id":30,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":30,"language":"en","bound_author_id":24,"text":"A catastrophe tears across the Stillness, leaving its inhabitants facing a long struggle for basic resources. For Essun, the disaster coincides with the destruction of her family: her son has been killed and her daughter is missing. She sets out to find the child while the world around her becomes increasingly hostile. The novel follows a personal search within a society shaped by fear of the earth’s destructive power.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Orbit / Hachette","source_url":"https://www.hachette.co.uk/titles/n-k-jemisin/the-fifth-season/9780356508191/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.hachette.co.uk/titles/n-k-jemisin/the-fifth-season/9780356508191/","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Stillness experiences catastrophic geological upheaval","Essun loses her son and searches for her missing daughter","Survival and conflict over scarce resources"],"role":"Publisher and author confirm the same novel; alternate UK ISBN is source identity, not a catalog edition substitution"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1049:nl","key":{"work_id":1049,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Eva groeit op in een klein Vlaams dorp, waar haar vriendschap met twee jongens een groot deel van haar jeugd bepaalt. Tijdens de puberteit veranderen de verhoudingen en wordt het steeds moeilijker om bij het gezelschap te blijven zonder haar eigen grenzen te verliezen. Jaren later keert ze met een blok ijs terug naar Bovenmeer. De roman verbindt die terugkeer met herinneringen aan een zomer die de drie niet ongeschonden heeft achtergelaten.","work_id":1049,"evidence":[{"url":"https://dasmag.nl/product/het-smelt/","facts":["Eva grows up in Bovenmeer with two boys","Puberty changes their relationship","She returns years later with ice in her car"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-30"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://dasmag.nl/product/het-smelt/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Das Mag","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":646},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1050:nl","key":{"work_id":1050,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Leo heeft in Brussel een leven opgebouwd met Simon, met wie ze al tien jaar samen is. Hun moeilijke jeugd vormt een belangrijke band tussen hen. Wanneer zijn gedrag plotseling verandert, raakt de zekerheid van hun gezamenlijke bestaan aangetast. Leo probeert vast te houden aan wat ze samen hebben, terwijl de situatie steeds moeilijker te begrijpen wordt. De roman onderzoekt hoe zorg voor een ander kan botsen met de behoefte jezelf te beschermen.","work_id":1050,"evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1403243/ik-ben-er-niet.html","facts":["Leo and Simon live in Brussels","Their difficult childhoods shaped their relationship","Simon''s changed behaviour unsettles Leo"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-30"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1403243/ik-ben-er-niet.html","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":646},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1055:nl","key":{"work_id":1055,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Lucas besluit zijn vertrouwde bestaan als rechter te onderbreken en gaat in de buurt van een brug wonen. Hij wil mensen die daar in nood verkeren helpen, maar zijn nieuwe rol brengt ook onzekerheid met zich mee. Tegelijk krijgt hij meer ruimte om naar zijn eigen familie en verleden te kijken. De roman volgt iemand die iets voor anderen probeert te betekenen, terwijl hij moet onderzoeken welke ervaringen zijn eigen leven blijven bepalen.","work_id":1055,"evidence":[{"url":"https://rozet.nl/catalogus/1869989/","facts":["Lucas leaves his work as a judge temporarily","He moves near a bridge and tries to help people in crisis","Family history and his own past matter"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-30"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://rozet.nl/catalogus/1869989/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Rozet bibliotheek","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":648},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1076:nl","key":{"work_id":1076,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Anne is gewend aan publieke aandacht door haar werk als televisiepresentatrice en journaliste. Wanneer haar relatie onder druk komt te staan, dreigt ook de toekomst die zij voor zichzelf zag te verdwijnen. Haar verdriet blijft niet privé: de belangstelling van de pers maakt het moeilijker om grip op de situatie te houden. Ze probeert haar plaats binnen familie en vriendenkring te behouden, terwijl haar vertrouwen in anderen en in haar eigen oordeel wordt aangetast.","work_id":1076,"evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/760644/huidpijn.html","facts":["Anne works as a television presenter and journalist","Her relationship and plans for the future are threatened","Her private distress becomes public"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-30"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/760644/huidpijn.html","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":659},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1086:nl","key":{"work_id":1086,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Het vooruitzicht van een schoolreünie haalt bij Sabine herinneringen naar boven aan haar verdwenen klasgenoot Isabel. Ooit waren ze bevriend, maar tijdens hun schooltijd veranderde hun verhouding. De verdwijning is nooit opgehelderd en Sabine blijft zich afvragen welke betekenis haar eigen gedrag heeft gehad. Ze gaat opnieuw naar het verleden kijken en probeert herinneringen van veronderstellingen te onderscheiden. Haar zoektocht maakt duidelijk dat een vertrouwd verhaal over vroeger niet noodzakelijk het volledige verhaal is.","work_id":1086,"evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/54569/de-reunie.html","facts":["Sabine receives news of a school reunion","Former friend Isabel disappeared","She re-examines her memories of their school years"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-30"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/54569/de-reunie.html","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":661},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1112:nl","key":{"work_id":1112,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Marije verlaat op haar vijftiende Brugge omdat ze niet wil trouwen met de man die voor haar is uitgekozen. Onderweg ontmoet ze een zanger en reist met hem door Frankrijk. De Honderdjarige Oorlog maakt het bestaan onzeker, terwijl burgers en steden naar meer zelfstandigheid zoeken. Haar verlangen zelf over haar leven te beslissen krijgt zo een plaats binnen een grotere maatschappelijke verandering. Deze historische roman vormt het begin van een trilogie.","work_id":1112,"evidence":[{"url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/geef-me-de-ruimte","facts":["Fifteen-year-old Marije leaves Bruges to escape a marriage","She travels with a singer through France","Hundred Years War is the historical setting"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-30"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/geef-me-de-ruimte","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Lemniscaat","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":669},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1124:nl","key":{"work_id":1124,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"David ziet hoe zijn klasgenoot Jochem op school wordt gepest. Hij doet er zelf niet aan mee, maar durft ook niet tegen de anderen in te gaan. Daardoor blijft Jochem steeds meer alleen staan. Wanneer hij na een klassenavond niet thuiskomt, krijgen de eerdere gebeurtenissen voor David een andere betekenis. Het verhaal volgt zijn schuldgevoel en zoektocht, en stelt de vraag welke verantwoordelijkheid iemand draagt die onrecht wel ziet maar niet ingrijpt.","work_id":1124,"evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/20015/spijt.html","facts":["Jochem is bullied at school","David does not participate but remains silent","Jochem''s disappearance makes David question that silence"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-30"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/20015/spijt.html","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":671},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1151:nl","key":{"work_id":1151,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Rutger Bregman onderzoekt hoe mensen door de geschiedenis heen over vooruitgang hebben gedacht. Hij zet verbeteringen in welvaart, gezondheid en veiligheid naast het onbehagen dat desondanks blijft bestaan. Voor zijn betoog verbindt hij historische voorbeelden met inzichten uit onder meer wetenschap en filosofie. Het boek vraagt niet alleen wat er is veranderd, maar ook welke verwachtingen mensen aan die veranderingen verbinden. Zo wordt de betekenis van vooruitgang zelf het onderwerp van onderzoek.","work_id":1151,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.debezigebij.nl/boek/de-geschiedenis-van-de-vooruitgang/","facts":["Historical investigation of the idea of progress","Contrasts improved material conditions with dissatisfaction","Combines history with ideas from other disciplines"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-30"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.debezigebij.nl/boek/de-geschiedenis-van-de-vooruitgang/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"De Bezige Bij","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":678},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2031:nl","key":{"work_id":2031,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Pietro leert via zijn vader de bergen kennen en sluit er vriendschap met Bruno. Naarmate ze ouder worden, kiezen de twee mannen verschillende wegen. Pietro reist onder meer naar Nepal, terwijl zijn band met de bergen en met Bruno hem blijft bezighouden. De roman volgt hoe hun vriendschap, hun familiegeschiedenis en hun verhouding tot het landschap door de jaren veranderen. De terugkeer naar een vertrouwde plek roept vragen op over de richting die een leven kan nemen.","work_id":2031,"evidence":[{"url":"https://rozet.nl/catalogus/1873744/","isbn":"9789023466413","facts":["Paolo Cognetti; De acht bergen; Nederlands","Book, 239 pages, 23 cm; De Bezige Bij, 2017","Translation of Le otto montagne, Einaudi, 2016"],"caution":"Book establishes printed material, not a specific paperback/hardcover binding. No verified cover imported.","checkedAt":"2026-10-30"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://rozet.nl/catalogus/1873744/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Rozet bibliotheek","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":1022},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:860:en","key":{"work_id":860,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":860,"language":"en","bound_author_id":514,"text":"Rhonda Byrne presents a self-help approach built around the belief that thoughts attract corresponding experiences. She draws on accounts from contemporary teachers to explain how this idea might be applied to money, relationships, health and personal goals. The book moves between explanations of that belief and examples of everyday practice. Its promises are the author''s claims, rather than established medical or scientific findings, and form the central perspective of the book.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Simon & Schuster","source_url":"https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/The-Secret/Rhonda-Byrne/The-Secret-Library/9781582701707","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/The-Secret/Rhonda-Byrne/The-Secret-Library/9781582701707","facts":["Exact ISBN/title/author; hardcover; book explains Byrne''s law-of-attraction belief and applications to everyday life"],"readState":"publisher page read"},{"url":"https://catalog.freelibrary.org/Record/1551503","facts":["Indexed library record explicitly English, ISBN9781582701707, hardcover, Rhonda Byrne"],"readState":"search-index evidence; direct open returned403, not bypassed"},{"url":"https://catalog.dmpl.org/Record/170838","facts":["Independent public library: exact ISBN, author, English print198pages"],"readState":"indexed library record"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1152:nl","key":{"work_id":1152,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1152,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":678,"text":"Rutger Bregman onderzoekt welke maatschappelijke veranderingen mogelijk worden als bestaande economische aannames ter discussie worden gesteld. Hij bespreekt onder meer een onvoorwaardelijk basisinkomen, een kortere werkweek en andere manieren om vooruitgang te beoordelen. Historische voorbeelden en onderzoek vormen de basis van zijn betoog. De verschillende voorstellen draaien om de vraag hoe welvaart beter kan worden verdeeld en benut. Het boek presenteert daarmee een verzameling samenhangende ideeën voor een andere inrichting van de samenleving.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Rozet bibliotheek","source_url":"https://rozet.nl/catalogus/1508405/","evidence":[{"url":"https://rozet.nl/catalogus/1508405/","facts":["Exact ISBN, author, Dutch, printed book255pages22cm, De Correspondent2014","Six ideas include basic income, shorter working week, poverty, taxation, progress measures and borders"],"readState":"library page read"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1804:nl","key":{"work_id":1804,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1804,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":913,"text":"Dit geïllustreerde boek verkent de geschiedenis van de Verenigde Oost-Indische Compagnie aan de hand van archiefmateriaal en bijdragen van verschillende auteurs. De tocht begint in Nederland en volgt de gebieden waarin de compagnie actief was. Beelden en persoonlijke verhalen verbinden handel en scheepvaart met de mensen die daarbij betrokken waren. Naast economische activiteiten komen ook onderdrukking en geweld aan bod. Het resultaat is een gezamenlijke verkenning van een omvangrijk koloniaal verleden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Rijksmuseum Research Library","source_url":"https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/en/collection/publication/Het-grote-VOC-boek--adff56a593ab275ed78fefc17c2d1862","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.rijksmuseum.nl/en/collection/publication/Het-grote-VOC-boek--adff56a593ab275ed78fefc17c2d1862","facts":["Exact ISBN, Dutch publication language, WBooks2017; Ramsey Nasr is contributor; Guleij and Knaap editors","Uses VOC archives, images and individual stories; discusses trade and colonial violence"],"readState":"museum library page read"},{"url":"https://pure.knaw.nl/portal/nl/publications/het-grote-voc-boek/","facts":["Exact printed ISBN9789462581777; Dutch; editorsRonGuleij/GerritKnaap"],"readState":"institutional publication record read"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:5227:en","key":{"work_id":5227,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":5227,"language":"en","bound_author_id":2659,"text":"Nel Verhoeven introduces the practical decisions involved in carrying out applied research. The book follows the process from developing a question and planning a study to gathering information, interpreting findings and reporting results. It connects research methods with situations students may encounter in higher education and professional practice. Examples and guidance are intended to make that process more approachable, while encouraging readers to consider why a particular method suits the question they are investigating.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"Boom uitgevers","source_url":"https://www.boom.nl/media/21/9789024424757_inkijkexemplaar_doing_research_5edruk.pdf","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.boom.nl/media/21/9789024424757_inkijkexemplaar_doing_research_5edruk.pdf","facts":["Publisher''s actual English title/copyright/contents pages, Nel Verhoeven, fifth edition2019, exact print ISBN9789024424757","Introduction to applied research; planning, questions, collection, analysis and reporting"],"readState":"publisher sample pages read, not just title language"},{"url":"https://www.fontys.nl/en/Download-4/Course-manual-IFC-semester-1.htm","facts":["Exact ISBN identified as English version; Dutch alternative listed separately"],"readState":"institutional course reading list"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:348:en","key":{"work_id":348,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":348,"language":"en","bound_author_id":172,"text":"During a journey through the English countryside in 1956, Stevens looks back on the years he spent serving at Darlington Hall. His memories return to the household''s life between the wars and to the private possibilities that accompanied his professional commitments. What initially appears to be a modest holiday becomes an examination of a life shaped by service, attachment and causes whose meaning is difficult to reassess.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL59048W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL59048W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Stevens is ageing butler at DarlingtonHall","1956 countryside holiday prompts memories of interwar household, lost causes/love"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9780571249350","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p441465536","title":"The Remains of the Day","language":"en","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","author":"Kazuo Ishiguro","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:40:35.630Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:827:en","key":{"work_id":827,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":827,"language":"en","bound_author_id":489,"text":"Patti Smith recalls her early years in New York and the relationship she formed with Robert Mapplethorpe. Their shared life unfolds among bookstores, artists and the communities around the Hotel Chelsea and Max''s Kansas City. Through memories of friendship and creative ambition, Smith describes the surroundings in which they began finding their artistic directions. The memoir connects a personal bond with the experience of trying to build a life devoted to art.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15474046W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15474046W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Memoir byPattiSmith","NewYork/Brooklyn, friendship withRobertMapplethorpe, HotelChelsea andMax''sKansasCity"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9780062008442","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p448557991","title":"Just Kids","language":"en","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","author":"Patti Smith","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:39:48.919Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1042:en","key":{"work_id":1042,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1042,"language":"en","bound_author_id":644,"text":"A writer takes a room in an old European hotel while reflecting on the end of his relationship with Clio. Memories of their life in Italy and their travels mingle with encounters among the hotel''s residents. His personal account opens onto broader questions about tourism and a continent increasingly occupied by its own past. The novel brings a love story together with a critical, often comic examination of contemporary Europe.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24320267W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24320267W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Same Work as existing approved Dutch summary ontestWork930100014","Writer,Clio,Italy,hotel residents,tourism andEuropean past"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"url":"https://www.singeluitgeverijen.nl/de-arbeiderspers/boek/grand-hotel-europa/","state":"Existing Dutch pilot source review reused; no new claim about this URL''s live response"},{"isbn":"9780008375379","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p437805948","title":"Grand Hotel Europa","language":"en","author":"Ilja Leonard Pfeijffer","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:39:45.707Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1047:nl","key":{"work_id":1047,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1047,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":645,"text":"Een man en een vrouw leven samen, maar hun verhouding is op een dieptepunt beland. Wanneer de vrouw met een asielzoeker trouwt en deze bij hen komt wonen, verandert hun bestaande situatie ingrijpend. De aanwezigheid van een derde persoon maakt van hun gedeelde huis een andere leefwereld. Grunberg onderzoekt vanuit deze ongewone verhouding hoe een intieme verbintenis onder druk komt te staan en hoe mensen zich tegenover elkaar opstellen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL850956W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL850956W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Man/vrouwverhouding opdieptepunt","Vrouw trouwt metasielzoeker diebijhen intrekt"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789038894102","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p371404037","title":"De asielzoeker","language":"nl","author":"Arnon Grunberg","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:09.666Z"},{"isbn":"9789038894102","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p328677191","title":"De asielzoeker","language":"nl","author":"Arnon Yasha Yves Grunberg","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:09.666Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1053:nl","key":{"work_id":1053,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1053,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":647,"text":"De gepensioneerde bibliothecaris Désiré Cordier wil ontsnappen aan het bestaan dat zijn familie en omgeving voor hem bepalen. Hij besluit dementie voor te wenden en slaagt erin in een verzorgingshuis te worden opgenomen. Daar houdt hij zijn omgeving nauwlettend in de gaten terwijl hij zijn nieuwe rol speelt. De komst van een vroegere geliefde geeft zijn verblijf een andere betekenis. Zijn plan vormt het uitgangspunt van een ironische terugblik op zijn leven.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.atlascontact.nl","source_url":"https://www.atlascontact.nl/boek/de-laatkomer-ebook/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.atlascontact.nl/boek/de-laatkomer-ebook/","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Gepensioneerde bibliothecarisDésiréCordier veinst dementie","Opnameverzorgingshuis; vroegeregeliefde verschijnt"],"editionNote":"Publisher ebook of same Work used for content only; exact selected print ISBN separately verified","state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789025441265","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p355179113","title":"De laatkomer","language":"nl","author":"Dimitri Verhulst","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:41:59.873Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1070:nl","key":{"work_id":1070,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1070,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":659,"text":"Een jonge alleenstaande moeder verdient haar leven als popmuzikante wanneer zij door een stalker wordt belaagd. De onbekende lijkt haar geheimen en angsten te kennen en zet daarmee haar gevoel van veiligheid onder druk. Terwijl de dreiging voortduurt, wordt ook haar geestelijke weerbaarheid op de proef gesteld. De thriller volgt een persoonlijke confrontatie waarin kennis over iemands verleden een middel wordt om haar steeds verder te ontregelen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24302287W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24302287W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Alleenstaandemoeder/popmuzikante wordtgestalkt","Stalker kentgeheimenenangsten; geestelijkegezondheid onderdruk"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789041409294","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p269468609","title":"Terug naar de kust","language":"nl","author":"Saskia Noort","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1071:nl","key":{"work_id":1071,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1071,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":659,"text":"Een vriendenkring van welgestelde echtparen wordt opgeschrikt wanneer een van de leden bij een brand om het leven komt. Na zijn dood blijkt dat de onderlinge verhoudingen minder hecht zijn dan ze naar buiten toe leken. De gebeurtenis verandert de manier waarop de vrienden elkaar bezien. De thriller draait om de spanning tussen een gezamenlijk opgebouwd sociaal leven en de voorwaarden waaronder mensen elkaar werkelijk blijven vertrouwen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20906472W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20906472W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Welgesteldeechtparenvriendenkring","Eénlid sterftbijbrand; vriendschappen blijkenvoorwaardelijk"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789041411150","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p297175890","title":"De eetclub","language":"nl","author":"Saskia Noort","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1075:nl","key":{"work_id":1075,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1075,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":659,"text":"Na de dood van haar man bij een verkeersongeluk probeert een vrouw verder te leven met wat zij over hem wist. Gaandeweg ontdekt ze echter dat hij belangrijke zaken voor haar verborgen heeft gehouden. Wat zij aantreft, verandert haar beeld van hun gedeelde bestaan. De thriller volgt hoe verlies en onzekerheid samengaan wanneer een achterblijvende partner zich moet verhouden tot een verleden dat minder vertrouwd blijkt dan zij dacht.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24173760W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24173760W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Manoverlijdt verkeersongeluk","Vrouwontdekt watmanverborgenhield"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789026328824","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p377066478","title":"Debet","language":"nl","author":"Saskia Noort","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:02.656Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1081:nl","key":{"work_id":1081,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1081,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":660,"text":"Vera Zagt heeft haar leven opgebouwd rond haar huwelijk met ondernemer Lucien Reinders, haar werk als dierenfotografe en hun huis. Haar moeilijke jeugd blijft echter doorwerken in de manier waarop zij zichzelf ziet. Wanneer haar relatie onder druk komt te staan, zoekt zij houvast in een buitenechtelijke verhouding. Tegelijk verliest zij steeds meer de controle. De roman verbindt haar huidige keuzes met de gevolgen van haar vroegere ervaringen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/120743/tegenlicht.html","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/120743/tegenlicht.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["VeraZagt,LucienReinders,dierenfotografe","Ontregeldejeugd,relatiedruk,buitenechtelijkeverhouding,controleverlies"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789041414298","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p340156899","title":"Tegenlicht","language":"nl","author":"Esther Verhoef","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1088:nl","key":{"work_id":1088,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1088,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":661,"text":"Birgit en Jef reizen naar Egypte om duidelijkheid te krijgen over een verdwijning. Jefs vader is daar tijdens archeologisch onderzoek spoorloos geraakt. Voor het jonge stel is de zoektocht daardoor zowel een reis naar een onbekende omgeving als een persoonlijke poging om hun familie terug te vinden. Het verhaal draait om hun onderzoek naar wat hem is overkomen, met de archeologische werkzaamheden in Egypte als achtergrond van het raadsel.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24269387W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24269387W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["BirgitenJef zijnjongstel","Jefsvader spoorloostijdensarcheologischonderzoekEgypte;zezoekenhem"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789041412973","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p307457648","title":"Het laatste offer","language":"nl","author":"Simone van der Vlugt","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1090:nl","key":{"work_id":1090,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1090,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":661,"text":"Nadine wil schrijfster worden en lijkt haar doel dichterbij te zien komen wanneer zij een uitgever vindt. Haar professionele kans krijgt ook een persoonlijke kant: zij wordt verliefd op hem. Dan wordt haar omgeving opgeschrikt door een gewelddadige moord. De thriller brengt haar verlangen naar een schrijversbestaan en een nieuwe relatie samen met een misdaad die de wereld waarin zij terechtkomt in een ander licht zet.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"www.bibliotheek.nl","source_url":"https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.338540385.html/herfstlied/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.338540385.html/herfstlied/","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Nadine wilschrijfsterworden,vindtuitgever enwordtverliefd","Moordinhaaromgeving"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Indexed primary catalogue evidence; direct host subsequently blocked byrobots, not retried"},{"isbn":"9789041414007","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p315870451","title":"Herfstlied","language":"nl","author":"Simone van der Vlugt","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1091:nl","key":{"work_id":1091,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1091,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":661,"text":"Nathalie probeert uit de handen van haar gewelddadige ex-vriend te blijven. Ook de politie zoekt haar, omdat zij haar wil spreken over de dood van haar beste vriendin. Onder een andere identiteit ontmoet Nathalie rechercheur Julia Vriens, die aanvankelijk niet weet wie zij tegenover zich heeft. Hun ontmoeting verbindt een persoonlijke vlucht met een moordonderzoek, terwijl de dreiging van Nathalies verleden dichtbij blijft.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.amboanthos.nl","source_url":"https://www.amboanthos.nl/boek/op-klaarlichte-dag/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.amboanthos.nl/boek/op-klaarlichte-dag/","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Nathalie vluchtgewelddadigeex;politiezoekt haarna moordvriendin","Nieuweidentiteit,ontmoetingrechercheurJuliaVriens"],"editionNote":"Same Work/current publisher print content; selected historical ISBN separately bound via KB","state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789041418159","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p330543814","title":"Op klaarlichte dag","language":"nl","author":"Simone van der Vlugt","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1102:nl","key":{"work_id":1102,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1102,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":666,"text":"Een advocate die haar kind alleen opvoedt, krijgt te maken met een man die als autistisch wordt beschreven en in een tbs-instelling verblijft. Hij houdt vol dat hij zijn buurvrouw en haar dochter niet heeft vermoord. Voor de advocate wordt zijn herhaalde beroep op onschuld een vraag die zij niet zomaar naast zich neer kan leggen. De thriller draait om wat er gebeurt wanneer een vaststaand lijkende zaak opnieuw aandacht vraagt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27974484W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27974484W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Advocate/alleenstaandemoeder","Autistischetbs''er ontkentmoord opbuurvrouwendochter"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789041415196","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p318209608","title":"Daglicht","language":"nl","author":"Marion Pauw","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1130:nl","key":{"work_id":1130,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1130,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":671,"text":"Naomi, haar zus Elise en hun buurjongen Jelle dragen alle drie de gevolgen van ingrijpende ervaringen uit hun verleden met zich mee. Wanneer Elise vastloopt in haar nieuwe baan, zoekt zij een uitweg bij een sekte. Haar keuze brengt een nieuwe invloed binnen hun levens. Het verhaal volgt hoe persoonlijke kwetsbaarheid en het verlangen naar houvast kunnen samenkomen, en hoe mensen die elkaar nabij zijn daarmee te maken krijgen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24739344W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24739344W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["NaomienElisezijnzussen,Jellebuurjongen,alledriegetraumatiseerd","Elise functioneertnietnieuwebaan enzoektsekte"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789049925826","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p340827262","title":"Brainwash","language":"nl","author":"Carry Slee","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:19.510Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1140:nl","key":{"work_id":1140,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1140,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":674,"text":"Sven en Parker beginnen met heel verschillende verwachtingen aan hun nieuwe schooljaar. Hij wil niet als een zielige jongen worden gezien; zij probeert na een moeilijke zomer juist buiten beeld te blijven. Dan ontdekt Parker dat haar vroegere hond Alaska nu bij Sven woont als hulphond. Omdat zij hem overdag liever mijdt, probeert ze Alaska op een andere manier terug te zien. Zo raken hun levens toch met elkaar verbonden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL19735880W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL19735880W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["SvenenParker startenschooljaar,verschillendeomgangmetproblemen","Parkersvroegerehond Alaska isnuSvenshulphond;zijzoekt''snachts"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789045119762","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p404327184","title":"Alaska","language":"nl","author":"Anna Woltz","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z"},{"isbn":"9789045119762","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p409768553","title":"Alaska","language":"nl","author":"Anna Woltz","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z"},{"isbn":"9789045119762","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p41120372X","title":"Alaska","language":"nl","author":"Anna Woltz","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z"},{"isbn":"9789045119762","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p412760177","title":"Alaska","language":"nl","author":"Anna Woltz","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z"},{"isbn":"9789045119762","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p459804561","title":"Alaska","language":"nl","author":"Anna Woltz","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1184:nl","key":{"work_id":1184,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1184,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":694,"text":"Een jong stel zet een volgende stap in de relatie door samen te gaan wonen. Het gedeelde dagelijkse leven brengt echter niet alleen de verwachte nabijheid, maar ook een reeks grotere en kleinere moeilijkheden met zich mee. Hun verhouding krijgt daarmee te maken met de praktische kant van bij elkaar zijn. Dit vervolg op Zwaar verliefd! richt zich op de uitdagingen die ontstaan wanneer een liefde een gezamenlijke huishouding wordt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL26181155W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL26181155W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Jongstel gaatsamenwonen;grotere/kleinereproblemen","VervolgopZwaarverliefd"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789044325294","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p31894328X","title":"Zwaar beproefd!","language":"nl","author":"Chantal van Gastel","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:12.733Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1186:nl","key":{"work_id":1186,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1186,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":694,"text":"Na de bruiloft van een vriendin merkt Lucy hoe weinig plaats zij als single lijkt te hebben in de zomerplannen van haar vrienden. Een nachtelijk gesprek met haar oude vriend Kasper biedt een onverwachte uitweg. Hij nodigt haar uit om bij hem en zijn vriendin in New York te komen logeren. Lucy besluit te gaan en raakt verliefd op de stad en op iemand die zij daar ontmoet. Of dat gevoel wordt beantwoord, is onzeker.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"BoekenBalie catalogus","source_url":"https://boekenbalie.nl/zomer-in-new-york/9789044341027","evidence":[{"url":"https://boekenbalie.nl/zomer-in-new-york/9789044341027","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Lucyissingle,organiseerdevriendinsbruiloft","KaspernodigthaaruitbijhemenvriendininNewYork;Lucywordtverliefd"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Exact-ISBN retailer text corroborates the same Work''s library content; no user review used"},{"isbn":"9789044341027","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p355352532","title":"Zomer in New York","language":"nl","author":"Chantal van Gastel","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:12.733Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1187:nl","key":{"work_id":1187,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1187,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":696,"text":"Sophie wil vooruitkomen bij het reclamebureau waar zij werkt, maar haar bazin Karlin maakt dat moeilijk. De situatie is extra pijnlijk omdat Karlin vroeger haar beste vriendin was en nu een relatie heeft met Rein, de man op wie Sophie verliefd is. Wanneer de vernederingen blijven doorgaan, besluit Sophie zelf in te grijpen. Haar werkambities raken daardoor onlosmakelijk verweven met oude vriendschap, gekrenkte gevoelens en de behoefte haar positie te veranderen.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.lsuitgeverij.nl","source_url":"https://www.lsuitgeverij.nl/boek/glazuur/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.lsuitgeverij.nl/boek/glazuur/","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Sophieopreclamebureau,wilcarrière","VroegerevriendinKarlin isbazinenheeftrelatiemetRein;Sophiegrijptin"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789021806419","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p338707263","title":"Glazuur","language":"nl","author":"Lisette Jonkman","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:41:49.976Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1189:nl","key":{"work_id":1189,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1189,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":696,"text":"Lucy en Kikker krijgen te maken met spanning in hun relatie wanneer hij besluit een duet op te nemen met een aantrekkelijke, populaire zangeres. De samenwerking roept bij Lucy onzekerheid op over hun verhouding. Het verhaal richt zich op wat deze ontwikkeling tussen hen teweegbrengt en op de vraag hoe zij met die druk omgaan. Muzikale samenwerking en de verwachtingen binnen een liefdesrelatie komen zo rechtstreeks tegenover elkaar te staan.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL26182328W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL26182328W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["Lucy/Kikkerrelatie","Kikkerneemtdutopeenaantrekkelijkepopulairezangeres;relatieonderdruk"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789021809809","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p372468950","title":"Verslingerd","language":"nl","author":"Lisette Jonkman","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:41:49.976Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1218:nl","key":{"work_id":1218,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1218,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":712,"text":"Plastisch chirurg Tomas Augustus twijfelt aan zijn leven en huwelijk wanneer hij verliefd wordt op de jongere Maria. Juist als een andere toekomst mogelijk lijkt, breekt een dodelijke epidemie uit die het land ontwricht. Tomas behoort tot de overlevenden en trekt zich terug in zijn huis. Daar vertelt hij zijn levensverhaal. Zijn terugblik verbindt een onverwachte liefde met de vraag hoe een afstandelijke man uiteindelijk door anderen geraakt kan worden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL45029610W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL45029610W","checkedAt":"2026-10-30","facts":["PlastischchirurgTomasAugustus,getrouwd,verliefdopjongereMaria","Dodelijkeepidemie,Tomasoverleeft,verteltlevensverhaalvanuit huis"],"editionNote":null,"state":"Work source facts reviewed independently of edition language"},{"isbn":"9789044626919","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p394094441","title":"Quarantaine","language":"nl","author":"W.B. Versteeg","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"isbn":"9789044626919","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p397803303","title":"Quarantaine","language":"nl","author":"Wytske Versteeg","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"isbn":"9789044626919","url":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p398076081","title":"Quarantaine","language":"nl","author":"W.B. Versteeg","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1082:nl","key":{"work_id":1082,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1082,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":660,"text":"Didi herstelt moeizaam van de geboorte van haar eerste kind en is afhankelijk van de vrouw die thuis de kraamzorg verzorgt. Tegelijk onderzoekt een Rotterdamse politieagente de plotselinge dood van haar broer. Haar vermoedens richten zich op diens weduwe. Terwijl beide vrouwen proberen grip te krijgen op hun situatie, blijken de veiligheid van een jong gezin en vragen over een verdacht verleden nauw met elkaar verbonden.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.amboanthos.nl","source_url":"https://www.amboanthos.nl/boek/de-kraamhulp/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.amboanthos.nl/boek/de-kraamhulp/","role":"Work content, publisher; current paperback9789026331855 is NOT substituted for selected historical ISBN","facts":["Didi recovering after difficult childbirth, home maternity care","Rotterdam policewoman Miriam investigates brother''s death and suspects widow; young family in danger"]},{"url":"https://libris.nl/a/esther-verhoef/de-kraamhulp/100018439","role":"Exact historical edition","facts":["9789041423696, paperback, Dutch, EstherVerhoef, Ambo/Anthos2014"]},{"isbn":"9789041423696","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p369577140","title":"De kraamhulp","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p134307704","authorName":"Esther Verhoef","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z","batchId":"ff251a17eb6ce494423a7e4cb328c9e896cf9580c0a7d1c2713179e7060115a0"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1083:nl","key":{"work_id":1083,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1083,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":660,"text":"Verpleegkundige Helen woont met haar man Werner en hun drie kinderen in een gezin dat van buitenaf weinig problemen lijkt te hebben. De achttienjarige Ralf laat zich ondertussen betrekken bij een plan om hun huis te overvallen. Die ontmoeting zet twee zeer verschillende levens op ramkoers. Voor Helen wordt het beschermen van haar familie een vraag naar grenzen: welke keuzes zijn nog aanvaardbaar wanneer de mensen om wie zij geeft worden bedreigd?","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"uitgeverijprometheus.nl","source_url":"https://uitgeverijprometheus.nl/boeken/lieve-mama-gebonden/","evidence":[{"url":"https://uitgeverijprometheus.nl/boeken/lieve-mama-gebonden/","role":"Publisher Work content, hardcover page; NOT evidence for selected paperback format","facts":["Helen nurse, Werner husband, three children","Ralf18 drawn into plan to rob their home; threat to family"]},{"url":"https://www.boekhandeldominicanen.nl/a/esther-verhoef/lieve-mama/100026815","role":"Exact paperback edition","facts":["9789044628791, Dutch, Paperback, Prometheus, EstherVerhoef"]},{"isbn":"9789044628791","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p392104512","title":"Lieve mama","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p134307704","authorName":"Esther Verhoef","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5"},{"isbn":"9789044628791","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p390636940","title":"Lieve mama","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p134307704","authorName":"Esther Verhoef","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5"},{"isbn":"9789044628791","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p410610690","title":"Lieve mama","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p134307704","authorName":"Esther Verhoef","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1084:nl","key":{"work_id":1084,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1084,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":660,"text":"Onder de naam Vivian D. heeft Claudia een succesvolle loopbaan in de internationale mode opgebouwd. Haar jeugd in een achtergesteld milieu lijkt ver weg, totdat onverwacht nieuws vlak voor een belangrijk evenement in Parijs het verleden opnieuw dichtbij brengt. Wat zij heeft bereikt, laat zich niet gemakkelijk verenigen met wat eerder is gebeurd. De roman volgt hoe een zorgvuldig opgebouwde nieuwe identiteit onder druk komt te staan door ervaringen die niet verdwenen blijken.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"rozet.nl","source_url":"https://rozet.nl/catalogus/1870724/","evidence":[{"url":"https://rozet.nl/catalogus/1870724/","role":"Exact edition and content","facts":["9789049805647, Dutch, Dwarsligger683pages12cm, third printingJuly2017, cooperationAmboAnthos","Claudia from disadvantaged background becomes designerVivianD; past returns before Paris event"]},{"isbn":"9789049805647","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p411266373","title":"Nazomer","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p134307704","authorName":"Esther Verhoef","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:19.510Z","batchId":"9b87a1ddabbfc8b342ba30c97ae00f98aa655dca8ba7a48c26cea370a6ec16a0"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1085:nl","key":{"work_id":1085,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1085,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":660,"text":"Een nachtelijke hulpvraag verandert het werk van dierenarts Emma van Eerd in een directe bedreiging voor haarzelf en haar dochter. Twee mannen met bedekte gezichten brengen een ernstig gewonde vriend naar de praktijk en eisen dat Emma hem opereert. Ze woont met haar veertienjarige dochter boven de kliniek, waardoor werk en thuis niet van elkaar te scheiden zijn. Haar poging om de patiënt te helpen blijkt het gevaar niet te beëindigen.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"uitgeverijprometheus.nl","source_url":"https://uitgeverijprometheus.nl/boeken/nachtdienst-paperback/","evidence":[{"url":"https://uitgeverijprometheus.nl/boeken/nachtdienst-paperback/","role":"Exact publisher edition and content","facts":["9789044643589, Dutch, Paperback, EstherVerhoef, July2021","VeterinarianEmmaVanEerd lives above practice with14yearolddaughter; two masked men force surgery on injured friend"]},{"isbn":"9789044643589","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p433472944","title":"De nachtdienst","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p134307704","authorName":"Esther Verhoef","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5"},{"isbn":"9789044643589","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p432651489","title":"De nachtdienst","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p134307704","authorName":"Esther Verhoef","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1097:nl","key":{"work_id":1097,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1097,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":664,"text":"Michael Bellicher denkt getuige te zijn van een fataal verkeersongeval, maar belandt zelf als verdachte in een politieverhoor. De beschuldiging past niet bij wat hij zich herinnert en ook zijn advocaat raakt niet overtuigd van zijn verhaal. Intussen lijkt ieder verweer nieuw wantrouwen op te roepen. Michael moet achterhalen waarop de zaak tegen hem berust en hoe hij zijn eigen werkelijkheid kan aantonen in een omgeving die zijn identiteit en verklaringen niet vertrouwt.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.singeluitgeverijen.nl","source_url":"https://www.singeluitgeverijen.nl/volt/boek/cel-2/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.singeluitgeverijen.nl/volt/boek/cel-2/","role":"Publisher Work content; new2022paperback not used as exact old format proof","facts":["MichaelBellicher witnesses fatal car accident then arrested; investigators and lawyer doubt his account; seeks truth","Second Bellicher novel; no series links/progress changed here"]},{"url":"https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.437041379.html/cel/","role":"Indexed national library print record; no direct access bypass","facts":["Dutch printed DeGeusBreda2008, exact9789044511086,378pages"]},{"url":"https://www.deslegte.com/leiden/cel-120944/","role":"Exact binding corroboration","facts":["9789044511086, CharlesdenTex, DeGeus, Hardback,2008"]},{"isbn":"9789044511086","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p308220897","title":"Cel","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p134442806","authorName":"Charles den Tex","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:12.733Z","batchId":"e908d938b4ce7e739d86a00b45cdc5e9543389352abecdefc9543bc49f518bd2"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1098:nl","key":{"work_id":1098,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1098,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":664,"text":"Wanneer zijn vriendin Guusje verdwijnt, probeert Michael Bellicher haar terug te vinden via de sporen die mensen in digitale netwerken en het openbare leven achterlaten. Camerabeelden, verbindingen en informatie leveren echter niet vanzelf zekerheid op. Zijn zoektocht brengt hem dichter bij een criminele wereld waarin vrouwen worden uitgebuit. Hij zet zijn gewone leven opzij om te begrijpen wat er met haar is gebeurd, terwijl ook de betekenis van haar verdwijning onzeker blijft.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.singeluitgeverijen.nl","source_url":"https://www.singeluitgeverijen.nl/volt/boek/wachtwoord-2/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.singeluitgeverijen.nl/volt/boek/wachtwoord-2/","role":"Publisher Work content; not selected old edition format","facts":["MichaelBellicher searches for missing girlfriendGuusje using digital/public traces; organized exploitation of women","Third Bellicher novel; no series/progress mutation proposed"]},{"url":"https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.437041395.html/wachtwoord/","role":"Indexed exact library edition, not audio record with print ISBN reference","facts":["Dutch printed, DeGeusBreda2010,347pages, ISBN9789044514308"]},{"url":"https://www.deslegte.com/wachtwoord-161412/","role":"Exact binding corroboration","facts":["9789044514308, Hardback, CharlesdenTex, DeGeusSpanning2010"]},{"isbn":"9789044514308","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p322868149","title":"Wachtwoord","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p134442806","authorName":"Charles den Tex","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:14.079Z","batchId":"19a06c1ebcef1076663fad615f82d0275d34ec07f67727f39a166b3ad1bef4c9"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1139:nl","key":{"work_id":1139,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1139,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":674,"text":"Fitz is kwaad over de scheiding van haar ouders, maar de verwonding van haar zusje brengt een andere onrustige dag op gang. In het ziekenhuis raakt zij betrokken bij de levens van mensen die ze daar ontmoet, onder wie een vijftienjarige jongen en een verpleegster. Terwijl buiten sneeuw ligt, bedenkt Fitz plannen die verder gaan dan rustig afwachten. Haar boosheid raakt vermengd met nieuwe gevoelens en de vraag of zij zelf iets kan veranderen.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"singeluitgeverijen.nl","source_url":"https://singeluitgeverijen.nl/querido/boek/gips/","evidence":[{"url":"https://singeluitgeverijen.nl/querido/boek/gips/","role":"Exact publisher edition and Work content","facts":["AnnaWoltz,9789045117829,GarPapBand,2015; distinct ebook/audio ISBNs","Fitz angry after parents separate; injured sister in hospital; boy15 and nurse; one snowy day"]},{"url":"https://www.zwijsen.nl/product/gips-9789045117829/","role":"Publishing/distribution catalogue, exact binding","facts":["9789045117829, AnnaWoltz, Hardback,168pages; same narrative premise"]},{"isbn":"9789045117829","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p403917867","title":"Gips","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p174442165","authorName":"Anna Woltz","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z","batchId":"a22e20a976507a7f1a872e63f6caf57164de4f0928f643b0ecc83999d9b7d090"},{"isbn":"9789045117829","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p383765374","title":"Gips","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p174442165","authorName":"Anna Woltz","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z","batchId":"a22e20a976507a7f1a872e63f6caf57164de4f0928f643b0ecc83999d9b7d090"},{"isbn":"9789045117829","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p405405855","title":"Gips","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p174442165","authorName":"Anna Woltz","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z","batchId":"a22e20a976507a7f1a872e63f6caf57164de4f0928f643b0ecc83999d9b7d090"},{"isbn":"9789045117829","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p40741780X","title":"Gips","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p174442165","authorName":"Anna Woltz","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z","batchId":"a22e20a976507a7f1a872e63f6caf57164de4f0928f643b0ecc83999d9b7d090"},{"isbn":"9789045117829","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p421638575","title":"Gips","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p174442165","authorName":"Anna Woltz","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z","batchId":"a22e20a976507a7f1a872e63f6caf57164de4f0928f643b0ecc83999d9b7d090"},{"isbn":"9789045117829","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p459742914","title":"Gips","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p174442165","authorName":"Anna Woltz","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:16.794Z","batchId":"a22e20a976507a7f1a872e63f6caf57164de4f0928f643b0ecc83999d9b7d090"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1040:nl","key":{"work_id":1040,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1040,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":643,"text":"Paul Krüzen woont met zijn vader in een oude boerderij bij de Duitse grens. Hun onderlinge rollen zijn veranderd: Paul zorgt nu voor de man die hem heeft grootgebracht. Ook Mariënveen is niet meer het dorp van vroeger. Terwijl nieuwe bewoners en gewoonten hun omgeving veranderen, blijven vader en zoon verbonden aan een gebeurtenis uit de Koude Oorlog. Een gevluchte Sovjetpiloot stortte achter hun boerderij neer en liet sporen na in hun levens.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/993728/de-heilige-rita.html","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/993728/de-heilige-rita.html","role":"Exact printed ISBN block and Work content","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Tommy Wieringa, Dutch, paperback9789023458753,26October2017,DeBezigeBij","PaulKruzen lives with ageing father near Germanborder; changing villageMarienveen; crash of escaping Sovietpilot behind farm affected both men"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1043:nl","key":{"work_id":1043,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1043,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":644,"text":"De Atheense politicus en veldheer Alkibiades legt rekenschap af van zijn leven en zijn rol in de oorlog tegen Sparta. Zijn persoonlijke ambities raken verweven met politieke idealen, militaire keuzes en de strijd om invloed in de Griekse wereld. Terwijl Athene onder druk staat, wordt steeds onduidelijker of zijn optreden de stad kan redden of haar verder verzwakt. De historische roman benadert zijn omstreden loopbaan vanuit vragen over leiderschap, democratie en verantwoordelijkheid.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Bureau ISBN","source_url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1698132/alkibiades.html","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/1698132/alkibiades.html","role":"Exact Dutch hardcover edition and Work content","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["IljaLeonardPfeijffer, Dutch, Hardback9789029549868,23May2023,DeArbeiderspers","Athenian politician and strategist Alcibiades recounts ambitions, ideals and actions during war with Sparta; decline of democracy and his contested responsibility"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1057:nl","key":{"work_id":1057,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1057,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":649,"text":"Een christelijke jonkvrouw uit de elfde eeuw kiest voor een liefde die haar buiten de vertrouwde wereld van haar familie brengt. Samen met een Joodse jongen slaat zij op de vlucht, in een tijd waarin geloof en geweld hun bewegingsvrijheid bepalen. Stefan Hertmans volgt haar sporen in historische documenten en landschappen. Zijn zoektocht verbindt een dorp in de Provence met vondsten in Caïro en met het onzekere bestaan van de vrouw die hij probeert terug te vinden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"www.debezigebij.nl","source_url":"https://www.debezigebij.nl/boek/de-bekeerlinge/ebook/9789023499534/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.debezigebij.nl/boek/de-bekeerlinge/ebook/9789023499534/","role":"Publisher Work content ONLY; the displayed ebook/new paperback is NOT format evidence for selected9789023499626","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Hertmans follows historical traces of11th-centuryChristian noblewoman and her love for a Jewish young man","Flight through religious violence; documents found in Cairo and a village in Provence connect historical investigation"]},{"format":"hardcover","url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/806257/de-bekeerlinge.html","facts":["Exact Hardback block ISBN9789023499626, Stefan Hertmans, Dutch; other paperback/ebook ISBNs kept distinct"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact edition format/identity evidence; images require separate verification"},{"isbn":"9789023499626","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p405076258","title":"De bekeerlinge","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p072194561","authorName":"Stefan Hertmans","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:41:55.827Z","batchId":"8682f8c55bde755db29ac8d3ed7733a75c612a11be6a3874bdfffb79b6f09a4a"},{"isbn":"9789023499626","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p408791942","title":"De bekeerlinge","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p072194561","authorName":"Stefan Hertmans","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:41:55.827Z","batchId":"8682f8c55bde755db29ac8d3ed7733a75c612a11be6a3874bdfffb79b6f09a4a"},{"isbn":"9789023499626","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p412451719","title":"De bekeerlinge","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p072194561","authorName":"Stefan Hertmans","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:41:55.827Z","batchId":"8682f8c55bde755db29ac8d3ed7733a75c612a11be6a3874bdfffb79b6f09a4a"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1060:nl","key":{"work_id":1060,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1060,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":651,"text":"Metin groeit op in de Bijlmermeer nadat zijn gezin uit Turkije naar Nederland is gekomen. Thuis probeert hij zo min mogelijk op te vallen om de woede van zijn vader te ontlopen. Buiten het gezin veranderen de flats, de school en de buurt waarin hij zijn weg zoekt. Naarmate Metin ouder wordt, ontdekken hij, zijn moeder en zijn zus mogelijkheden om zich te verzetten. Zijn jeugd verbindt de veranderingen in de wijk met de zoektocht naar veiligheid en zelfstandigheid.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24328099W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24328099W","role":"Matched official monthly Work export, not a new API fetch","snapshot":"2026-09-30","facts":["Metin arrives age5withTurkishfamily in1980sBijlmermeer","Father unemployed communist and violent at home; mother/children gradually resist; neighbourhood changes through childhood"]},{"format":"paperback","url":"https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.410340391.html/wees-onzichtbaar/","facts":["Dutch printed edition9789041422903 by Murat Isik,596pages,2017; paperback binding corroborated by exact monthly edition record and physical-book listing"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact edition format/identity evidence; images require separate verification"},{"isbn":"9789041422903","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p410340391","title":"Wees onzichtbaar","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p341433659","authorName":"Murat Isik","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z","batchId":"ff251a17eb6ce494423a7e4cb328c9e896cf9580c0a7d1c2713179e7060115a0"},{"isbn":"9789041422903","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p417771428","title":"Wees onzichtbaar","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p341433659","authorName":"Murat Isik","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z","batchId":"ff251a17eb6ce494423a7e4cb328c9e896cf9580c0a7d1c2713179e7060115a0"},{"isbn":"9789041422903","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p419772405","title":"Wees onzichtbaar","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p341433659","authorName":"Murat Isik","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z","batchId":"ff251a17eb6ce494423a7e4cb328c9e896cf9580c0a7d1c2713179e7060115a0"},{"isbn":"9789041422903","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p424328674","title":"Wees onzichtbaar","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p341433659","authorName":"Murat Isik","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z","batchId":"ff251a17eb6ce494423a7e4cb328c9e896cf9580c0a7d1c2713179e7060115a0"},{"isbn":"9789041422903","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p41758489X","title":"Wees onzichtbaar","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p341433659","authorName":"Murat Isik","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z","batchId":"ff251a17eb6ce494423a7e4cb328c9e896cf9580c0a7d1c2713179e7060115a0"},{"isbn":"9789041422903","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p434036242","title":"Wees onzichtbaar","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p341433659","authorName":"Murat Isik","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z","batchId":"ff251a17eb6ce494423a7e4cb328c9e896cf9580c0a7d1c2713179e7060115a0"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1061:nl","key":{"work_id":1061,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1061,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":651,"text":"De dertienjarige Mehmet groeit in de jaren zestig op in een Oost-Turks dorp dat door Armenen is gesticht. Zijn vader vertelt verhalen en draagt de verliezen van een eerdere oorlog met zich mee, terwijl zijn moeder een heel andere kracht in het gezin vormt. Hun dagelijkse samenleven verandert ingrijpend wanneer zijn vader een ongeluk krijgt. Mehmet moet omgaan met wat zijn familie uit elkaar drijft en met de geschiedenis die hun bestaan blijft beïnvloeden.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.amboanthos.nl","source_url":"https://www.amboanthos.nl/boek/verloren-grond/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.amboanthos.nl/boek/verloren-grond/","role":"Publisher Work content; currenthardcover9789026361623 NOT selected compact-edition format evidence","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Mehmet13growsupinEastTurkishvillage1960s, once founded by Armenians","Father storyteller affected byWWI, outspoken mother, brother/sister; father''s accident disrupts family"]},{"format":"other","url":"https://boekenbalie.nl/verloren-grond-dwarsligger-350/9789049807078","facts":["ExactISBN9789049807078, Dutch, Murat Isik, title Verloren grond / Dwarsligger /350; compact printed Dwarsligger classified other, not ebook/audio or ordinary paperback"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact edition format/identity evidence; images require separate verification"},{"isbn":"9789049807078","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p421664215","title":"Verloren grond","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p341433659","authorName":"Murat Isik","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:19.510Z","batchId":"9b87a1ddabbfc8b342ba30c97ae00f98aa655dca8ba7a48c26cea370a6ec16a0"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1074:nl","key":{"work_id":1074,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1074,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":659,"text":"Dorien staat op het punt een voorspelbaar leven met haar partner op te bouwen, totdat haar nieuwe vriendin Ellen haar aan het twijfelen brengt. Na het beëindigen van haar relatie vertrekt zij met de styliste naar Ibiza. Het uitgaan en de vrijheid lijken aanvankelijk precies wat zij zoeken. Wanneer een van de twee verdwijnt, krijgt de vakantie een andere betekenis. De zoektocht voert langs een eiland waar de feestelijke buitenkant niet alles laat zien.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL19964029W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL19964029W","role":"Matched official monthly Work export","snapshot":"2026-09-30","facts":["Dorien35magazineeditor, meets single stylistEllen, breaks relationship","Friends travel toIbiza; one disappears and a search follows amid apparent holiday freedom"]},{"format":"hardcover","url":"https://www.bol.com/nl/nl/p/koorts/1001004011523512/","facts":["Exact hardcover9789041417664, Dutch, Saskia Noort,18November2011; not other paperback/audio variants"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact edition format/identity evidence; images require separate verification"},{"isbn":"9789041417664","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p33453559X","title":"Koorts","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p138796726","authorName":"Saskia Noort","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:11.385Z","batchId":"ff251a17eb6ce494423a7e4cb328c9e896cf9580c0a7d1c2713179e7060115a0"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1188:nl","key":{"work_id":1188,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1188,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":696,"text":"Lucy verwacht dat haar studententijd haar eindelijk losmaakt van haar ouders en haar hoogbegaafde zusje. Het huis op de campus valt echter niet samen met het sociale leven dat zij zich had voorgesteld. Haar nieuwe huisgenoten lijken vooral nerds met wie zij niets wil delen. Vooral een lange, blonde jongen brengt haar in verwarring. Terwijl Lucy haar plaats probeert te vinden, blijkt haar beeld van de anderen minder stevig dan zij dacht.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.lsuitgeverij.nl","source_url":"https://www.lsuitgeverij.nl/boek/verkikkerd/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.lsuitgeverij.nl/boek/verkikkerd/","role":"Publisher Work content;2019paperback9789024583331 NOT the selected2013ISBN","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Lucy starts university away from parents and gifted sister","Campus household of nerds; attraction to tall blond housemate challenges assumptions; first series volume"]},{"format":"paperback","url":"https://boekenbalie.nl/verkikkerd-verkikkerd-1/9789021808499","facts":["Exact Dutch paperback9789021808499,Lisette Jonkman,Luitingh-Sijthoff,2013; image for otherISBN9789024583331 explicitly NOT approved"],"additional":{"url":"https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.420517103.html/verkikkerd/","facts":["Printed2013editionISBN9789021808499 distinguished from accessible audio rendition using print-sourceISBN"]},"checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact edition format/identity evidence; images require separate verification"},{"url":"https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.420517103.html/verkikkerd/","facts":["Printed2013editionISBN9789021808499 distinguished from accessible audio rendition using print-sourceISBN"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"isbn":"9789021808499","book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p352199628","title":"Verkikkerd","language":"nl","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p341586250","authorName":"Lisette Jonkman","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:41:49.976Z","batchId":"92b573eaaa930ca1a1b25b516a1cb624a000812ef692dffcd0d2bce4f2063e14"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1351:nl","key":{"work_id":1351,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1351,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":724,"text":"Rond een moskee in Iran deelt een uitgebreide familie een huis dat al eeuwen met haar geschiedenis verbonden is. Koopman Aqa Jaan en zijn verwanten hebben er te maken met huwelijken, verwachtingen en botsende verlangens tussen generaties. Buiten de muren neemt de politieke onrust toe. Terwijl de positie van de sjah verzwakt en een nieuwe machtsstrijd ontstaat, dringen de veranderingen door in het huishouden. Familiebanden bieden niet langer vanzelf bescherming tegen wat daarbuiten gebeurt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15179541W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15179541W","role":"Matched monthly Work text; independent exact Dutch and English edition bindings in author-primary-identity-review","snapshot":"2026-09-30","facts":["AqaJaan merchant, imam and muezzin cousins share familyhouse connected to mosque","Family life and wishes unfold as shah loses power and ayatollah returns toIran; political upheaval affects family"]},{"format":"hardcover","url":"https://boekenbalie.nl/het-huis-van-de-moskee/9789044507683","facts":["Exact Dutch hardcover9789044507683,Kader Abdolah,413pages; existingdut preserved"],"additional":{"url":"https://nieuw.passendlezen.nl/zoeken/boeken/2.103478/kader-abdolah/het-huis-van-de-moskee","facts":["Work content and Dutch print-source identity; no audio-as-print substitution"]},"checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact edition format/identity evidence; images require separate verification"},{"url":"https://nieuw.passendlezen.nl/zoeken/boeken/2.103478/kader-abdolah/het-huis-van-de-moskee","facts":["Work content and Dutch print-source identity; no audio-as-print substitution"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1351:en","key":{"work_id":1351,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1351,"language":"en","bound_author_id":724,"text":"Aqa Jaan''s family has lived beside an Iranian mosque for generations. Within the household, ordinary hopes about marriage, work and growing up coexist with religious duties and the expectations of older relatives. Beyond the house, the shah''s authority is weakening and political unrest is gathering force. As the country changes, private loyalties and public convictions become harder to separate. The family''s familiar surroundings cannot keep the consequences of the struggle for power outside.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15179541W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15179541W","role":"Matched monthly English Work text; exact English ebook binding separately confirmed","snapshot":"2026-09-30","facts":["AqaJaan merchant shares historic mosquehouse with relatives includingimam/muezzin","Everyday family wishes across generations; Iranian political turmoil and shah''s weakening power alter their world"]},{"format":"ebook","url":"https://www.vitalsource.com/products/the-house-of-the-mosque-kader-abdolah-v9781847678126","facts":["Digital/eTextISBN9781847678126,The House of the Mosque,Kader Abdolah,Canongate; printISBN9781847672414 kept distinct; cached exactKBrow languageen/EBook"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact edition format/identity evidence; images require separate verification"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2322:nl","key":{"work_id":2322,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":2322,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1145,"text":"De dood van haar veel oudere zus dwingt een schrijfster terug te kijken op het gezin waarin zij opgroeide. Herinneringen aan haar vader en haar zussen maken een jeugd zichtbaar waarin verbeelding, geweld en angst met elkaar verbonden waren. Door dat verleden in verhalen vast te leggen, probeert zij woorden te vinden voor ervaringen die moeilijk te bevatten zijn. Het boek onderzoekt wat herinneren en vertellen kunnen betekenen wanneer familiegeschiedenis niet als een veilig thuis voelt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24317781W","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24317781W","role":"Matched official monthly Work export","snapshot":"2026-09-30","facts":["Death of narrator''s mucholder sister triggers anger and examination of violentchildhood","Father calledHolbein; sisters and family stories; writing as testimony and reconstruction"]},{"format":"paperback","url":"https://www.bruna.nl/boeken/vallen-is-als-vliegen-9789021408026","facts":["Exact Dutch paperback9789021408026,Manon Uphoff,March2019; cached library record411208713 independently matches title/author/language"],"checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact edition format/identity evidence; images require separate verification"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1113:nl","key":{"work_id":1113,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1113,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":669,"text":"De zestienjarige Matthis vindt zijn plaats niet zozeer als soldaat, maar als heraut en secretaris van Bertrand du Guesclin. In Bretagne maakt hij van dichtbij mee hoe het verzet tegen de Engelse overheersing wordt georganiseerd. Een opdracht om geld te halen brengt hem naar Parijs, waar burgers zelf in opstand komen. Matthis raakt betrokken bij belangen die niet gemakkelijk te verenigen zijn. Zijn werk vraagt steeds meer durf wanneer hij in die onrust een dubbele rol krijgt.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"lemniscaat.nl","source_url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/triomf-van-de-verschroeide-aarde","evidence":[{"url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/triomf-van-de-verschroeide-aarde","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Official publisher Work facts; current ISBNs not substituted for historical editions","facts":["Matthis16 serves as herald and secretary to Bertrand du Guesclin in resistance against English rule in Brittany","Sent to Paris for money during bourgeois revolution; dangerous double role; second Hundred Years War trilogy volume"]},{"url":"https://www.boekwinkeltjes.nl/b/189088979/Triomf-van-de-verschroeide-aarde/","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact selected edition/binding evidence","facts":["9789060693261, Dutch, Thea Beckman, hardcover; exact monthly sole-parent binding separately checked"]},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL42945035M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Matched exact edition/sole Work parent/author binding; Work text absent; no cover identity approval inferred"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1114:nl","key":{"work_id":1114,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1114,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":669,"text":"Robert groeit op als pleegzoon van de zangeres Marie-Claire en droomt ervan een held te worden. Zijn geringe lengte maakt hem opvallend, maar hij kan zich juist bijzonder goed verborgen houden. Die vaardigheid trekt de aandacht van veldheer Du Guesclin. Terwijl rondtrekkende benden Frankrijk onveilig maken, krijgt Robert een taak als spion. Zijn verlangen naar avontuur wordt daarmee onderdeel van een strijd waarin informatie en onopgemerkt blijven even belangrijk kunnen zijn als wapens.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"lemniscaat.nl","source_url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/het-rad-van-fortuin","evidence":[{"url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/het-rad-van-fortuin","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Official publisher Work facts; current ISBNs not substituted for historical editions","facts":["Small Robert second foster son of singer Marie-Claire wants to become hero; skilled at concealment and knife throwing","Du Guesclin recruits him as master spy against raiding bands in France; third Hundred Years War trilogy volume"]},{"url":"https://www.bol.com/nl/nl/p/het-rad-van-fortuin-thea-beckman/666750521/","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact selected edition/binding evidence","facts":["Exact Dutch hardcoverISBN9789060693575 is mathematically equivalent to storedISBN10 9060693574; productionISBN13 remainsNULL, no bibliography patch here"]},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL2502760M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Matched exact edition/sole Work parent/author binding; Work text absent; no cover identity approval inferred"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1115:nl","key":{"work_id":1115,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1115,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":669,"text":"Het Badense Rijk waagt opnieuw een poging om Thule te onderwerpen. Een vloot brengt een groot leger naar de kust, waar de bewoners zich inmiddels op een nieuwe aanval hebben voorbereid. Na de bezetting van een stad beschadigt een storm de oorlogsschepen. De invallers besluiten verder te trekken over land. Hun militaire overwicht biedt echter geen vanzelfsprekende bescherming tegen de omstandigheden onderweg. De tocht naar de hoofdstad wordt een beproeving voor hun plannen om het land te overheersen.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"lemniscaat.nl","source_url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/het-helse-paradijs","evidence":[{"url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/het-helse-paradijs","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Official publisher Work facts; current ISBNs not substituted for historical editions","facts":["Badense Rijk sends five warships and1000soldiers to conquer Thule; defenders prepared after earlier invasion","Storm damages invaders'' ships; they march toward capital across unfamiliar land; second Thule volume"]},{"url":"https://www.bol.com/nl/nl/p/helse-paradijs/666750519/","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact selected edition/binding evidence","facts":["9789060696668, Dutch, Thea Beckman, hardcover; exact monthly sole-parent binding separately checked"]},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32532366M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Matched exact edition/sole Work parent/author binding; Work text absent; no cover identity approval inferred"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1116:nl","key":{"work_id":1116,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1116,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":669,"text":"Elvira komt naar Thule terwijl de Badeners een deel van het land bezet houden. Haar vader werkt voor het bestuur van de bezetters, maar de kolonisatie verloopt niet zoals verwacht: de oorspronkelijke bewoners blijven zich verzetten. Elvira besluit hun taal te leren en krijgt daarbij hulp van een Thuleense vrouw. Wanneer haar vader niet terugkeert van een expeditie, gaat zij naar hem op zoek. Haar kennismaking met het land komt daardoor in een ander licht te staan.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"lemniscaat.nl","source_url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/het-gulden-vlies-van-thule","evidence":[{"url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/het-gulden-vlies-van-thule","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Official publisher Work facts; current ISBNs not substituted for historical editions","facts":["Badeners occupy Gothab and other coastal towns; Elvira arrives as daughter of a colonial official","Thuleans resist through sabotage; Elvira learns local language aided by woman; father fails to return from expedition and she searches","Exact ebookISBN9789047750505 on publisherpage, not2026hardcover9789047718796"]},{"url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/het-gulden-vlies-van-thule","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact selected edition/binding evidence","facts":["9789047750505, Dutch, Thea Beckman, ebook; exact monthly sole-parent binding separately checked"]},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61957924M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Matched exact edition/sole Work parent/author binding; Work text absent; no cover identity approval inferred"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1251:nl","key":{"work_id":1251,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1251,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":669,"text":"Eeuwen na een verwoestende kernoorlog heeft zich op het vroegere Groenland een nieuwe samenleving gevormd. In Thule besturen vrouwen een land zonder leger, waar zorg voor de natuur belangrijk is. De komst van een onbekend expeditieschip verstoort die rust. De bezoekers uit het Badense Rijk zien vooral een gebied dat gemakkelijk te veroveren lijkt. Hun plannen botsen met de manier waarop de bewoners willen leven en met een tegenstand die zij niet hadden voorzien.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"lemniscaat.nl","source_url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/kinderen-van-moeder-aarde","evidence":[{"url":"https://lemniscaat.nl/boeken/kinderen-van-moeder-aarde","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Official publisher Work facts; current ISBNs not substituted for historical editions","facts":["Six centuries after devastating nuclear war, former Greenland/Thule has warm climate, rich nature, society led by women with no army","Expedition from Badense Rijk arrives intending conquest; inhabitants resist; first Thule volume"]},{"url":"https://boekenbalie.nl/kinderen-van-moeder-aarde-trilogie-over-de-toekomst-1/9789060696125","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","role":"Exact selected edition/binding evidence","facts":["9789060696125, Dutch, Thea Beckman, hardcover; exact monthly sole-parent binding separately checked"]},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32228770M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Matched exact edition/sole Work parent/author binding; Work text absent; no cover identity approval inferred"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1343:nl","key":{"work_id":1343,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1343,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":719,"text":"Een jongen trekt met een mol, een vos en een paard door een onoverzichtelijke wereld. De vier weten niet precies waarheen hun tocht leidt en merken dat moeilijke momenten steeds terugkeren. Hun gesprekken draaien om wat hen helpt wanneer het uitzicht somber wordt. In dit vervolg op hun eerdere ontmoeting is de onderlinge verbondenheid belangrijker dan een vaste bestemming. Woorden en beelden laten zien hoe de vrienden elkaar tijdens het zoeken gezelschap houden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61048849M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61048849M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Vervolg over jongen,mol,vos,paard onderweg in wildernis; donkere wolken en onderlinge liefde","Exact Dutch title Onthoud dit altijd, hardcover ISBN9789025914189, sole parent OL43541951W"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1357:nl","key":{"work_id":1357,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1357,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":728,"text":"Een zoon probeert te begrijpen hoe de oorlog het leven van zijn ouders en zijn eigen jeugd heeft gevormd. Zijn moeder groeide op in Brabant; zijn vader kwam na de oorlog van Java naar Nederland. In hun gezin werken geweld, angst en herinneringen door. Door zijn ouders steeds opnieuw te bevragen, zoekt de verteller naar samenhang tussen hun verhalen en het verleden waaraan hij zelf niet kan ontsnappen. De familiegeschiedenis verbindt verschillende plaatsen en generaties.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61696789M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61696789M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Moeder schoenmakersdochter Helmond tijdens Tweede Wereldoorlog, vader Indische oorlogstolk vlucht van Oost-Java","Zoon vertelt over terreur vader, internaat en vragen over oorlog; exact ISBN9789044536447 dut parentOL34953874W"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1433:nl","key":{"work_id":1433,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1433,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":756,"text":"Thomas Erikson bespreekt misverstanden tussen mensen aan de hand van een indeling in vier gedragskleuren. Hij gebruikt situaties uit werk en persoonlijke relaties om te laten zien hoe uiteenlopende manieren van reageren kunnen botsen. Het boek biedt een model waarmee lezers hun eigen communicatie en die van anderen kunnen bekijken. De aandacht ligt op het herkennen van verschillen en het aanpassen van gesprekken, niet op het vaststellen van medische of psychologische diagnoses.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL47675803M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL47675803M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Praktisch communicatiemodel rood/geel/groen/blauw; werk en persoonlijke relaties","Geen zelfstandige claim van wetenschappelijke validatie of diagnostiek; exact Dutch paperback ISBN9789402710236 parentOL35266824W"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1514:nl","key":{"work_id":1514,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1514,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":718,"text":"Amande trekt zich met haar verdriet terug in een afgelegen huis in Auvergne. De dagen buiten lijken voor haar weinig betekenis te hebben, tot ze aantekeningen van de vorige bewoonster vindt. Die tuinkalenders brengen haar ertoe de verwaarloosde tuin te verzorgen. Terwijl de seizoenen veranderen, ontstaat er opnieuw ruimte voor contact met de wereld. Haar werk met de aarde en de aanwijzingen van een onbekende vrouw begeleiden een langzaam proces van herstel.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL60681600M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL60681600M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Amande in afgelegen huis Auvergne na intens verdriet; tuinkalenders mevrouw Hugues","Tuin herstellen en nieuwe ontmoetingen door seizoenen; exact Dutch title De dagen die komen, ISBN9789022341155 parentOL24320310W"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1541:nl","key":{"work_id":1541,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1541,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":675,"text":"Eliza wil niet geloven dat vijf van haar broers op zee zijn verdronken, ook al houden haar vader en stiefmoeder dat vol. Ze besluit hen te gaan zoeken en neemt haar overgebleven broertje Krekel mee. Hij is bang en maakt de onderneming niet eenvoudiger, maar ze moeten samen verder. Hun tocht richting de Witte Kliffen stelt hun vastberadenheid op de proef. Tegen weer en tegenslag in blijven de twee kinderen zoeken naar hun verdwenen familie.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL62083313M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL62083313M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Eliza gelooft ouders niet over vijf verdronken broers, gaat met Krekel richting Witte Kliffen","Exact Dutch ISBN9789045131153 parentOL45586821W; source physical_format Hardbook remains unknown, not guessed hardcover"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1568:en","key":{"work_id":1568,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1568,"language":"en","bound_author_id":839,"text":"Two resistance operatives prepare an attack on Reinhard Heydrich in Nazi-occupied Prague. Laurent Binet follows their journey while examining his own effort to turn historical events into a novel. The account moves between the people involved in the operation and the writer''s questions about memory, invention and responsibility. Rather than treating the past as material that can be freely reshaped, it explores the difficulty of telling a compelling story without losing sight of actual lives.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27290510M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27290510M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Gabčík and Kubiš operation against Heydrich; escape from occupied Czechoslovakia and Prague","Novel reflects on memory,history and imagination; exact English paperback HHhH: A Novel ISBN9781250033345 parentOL15619778W"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1641:nl","key":{"work_id":1641,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1641,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":873,"text":"Carlo Masala onderzoekt een denkbeeldige crisis waarin Rusland een aanval op Estland begint. Vanuit dat scenario stelt hij vragen over de slagkracht van Europa en de bereidheid van de NAVO om op te treden. Het boek gebruikt een mogelijke toekomstige confrontatie om kwetsbaarheden in de huidige veiligheidspolitiek te bespreken. De beschreven gebeurtenissen zijn een gedachte-experiment, geen verslag van een aanval die werkelijk heeft plaatsgevonden of een vaststaande voorspelling van wat er zal gebeuren.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61279026M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61279026M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Expliciet hypothetisch scenario maart2028 Russische aanval Narva/Hiiumaa; vragen NAVO artikel5 en Europese militaire zwakte","Niet als werkelijke toekomstfeiten presenteren; exact Dutch ISBN9789044660067 parentOL44901485W"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1692:nl","key":{"work_id":1692,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1692,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":813,"text":"De zestienjarige Sophia wordt wakker in een onbekende omgeving en ontdekt dat ze aan een boom is vastgebonden. Een achtergelaten bericht kondigt aan dat ze die avond zal sterven. Terwijl ontsnappen niet lukt en de kou en regen haar verzwakken, probeert ze zich te herinneren wat eraan voorafging. Losse herinneringen worden belangrijker naarmate de tijd verstrijkt. Ze moet uitzoeken wie haar dit aandoet en wat de dreiging met haar eigen verleden te maken heeft.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL45730611M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL45730611M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Zestienjarige Sophia aan boom gebonden,kou/regen,dreigbrief sterven vanavond","Geleidelijke herinneringen en poging ontsnappen; exact Dutch hardcover ISBN9789044321807 parentOL33761051W"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1789:en","key":{"work_id":1789,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1789,"language":"en","bound_author_id":724,"text":"A young shah inherits a Persian kingdom whose traditions are increasingly challenged by forces beyond the court. His grand vizier wants to open the country to change, while the shah''s mother resists those reforms and works against the adviser. The ruler is caught between competing visions of power and the future. Set in the nineteenth century, the novel explores a court''s internal struggles as industrialisation and foreign influence press against an older political world.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26842026M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26842026M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Nineteenth-century Persia,young Shah Naser inherits kingdom under colonisation/industrialisation pressures","Grand vizier reform versus queen-mother resistance; exact English ISBN9780857862952 soleparentOL19551983W"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1865:nl","key":{"work_id":1865,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1865,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":758,"text":"Na de dood van acteur James Harrison krijgt journaliste Joanna een brief onder ogen die naar een verborgen geschiedenis verwijst. Haar nieuwsgierigheid groeit uit tot een onderzoek waarin niet iedereen wil dat de waarheid bekend wordt. Terwijl ze de aanwijzingen volgt, merkt ze dat anderen eveneens naar de brief op zoek zijn. De tegenwerking brengt haar in conflict met mensen uit invloedrijke kringen, die belang lijken te hebben bij het zwijgen rond Harrisons verleden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL41761836M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL41761836M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","facts":["Journaliste Joanna vindt brief overleden acteur James Harrison met geheim","Anderen willen brief bemachtigen en onderzoek verhinderen,hoogste kringen; exact Dutch paperback ISBN9789401615631 parentOL30378943W"]}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1883:nl","key":{"work_id":1883,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1883,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":373,"text":"Wanneer twee meisjes tijdens de feestelijkheden rond Fourth of July verdwijnen, krijgt agent Emmy Clifton een zaak die haar persoonlijk raakt. Een van hen is de dochter van haar beste vriendin. In North Falls dacht iedereen te weten wie zijn buren waren, maar het onderzoek maakt duidelijk hoeveel er verborgen bleef. Emmy probeert de laatste bewegingen en geheimen van de tieners te reconstrueren. Daarbij moet ze haar vertrouwde beeld van het stadje en zijn bewoners opnieuw beoordelen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL62059363M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL62059363M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"41a66415bddb0cb7da3fe2cda5aaed4bbad9362ef6f7616aba8b4c2ad6fe2050","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Gebroken engelen","author":"Karin Slaughter","isbn":"9789402717648","language":"nld","parent":"OL45399645W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2038:nl","key":{"work_id":2038,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":2038,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1023,"text":"Teun van de Keuken onderzoekt de rol van de voedingsindustrie in wat mensen dagelijks eten. Hij bespreekt hoe productontwikkeling, reclame en verkoopstrategieën de aantrekkelijkheid van sterk bewerkt voedsel vergroten. De vraag wie verantwoordelijk is voor eetgedrag loopt door het boek: de consument, de producent of de overheid. Vanuit zijn kritische kijk op het voedselsysteem verkent hij ook mogelijke veranderingen. Het is een betoog over industrie en beleid, geen persoonlijk dieetadvies.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61398636M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61398636M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"f818a544593ed2ed18c4fb4ff02f1e24b525d257e1d81b90fc907f337b02de78","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"De mens is een plofkip :","author":"Teun van de Keuken","isbn":"9789400412972","language":"nld","parent":"OL45003955W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3208:nl","key":{"work_id":3208,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3208,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1558,"text":"Katria hoopt dat een gearrangeerd huwelijk haar bevrijdt van haar wrede familie. Haar nieuwe echtgenoot Fenwood blijkt echter met een wereld verbonden die zij alleen uit verhalen kent. In zijn huis gelden vreemde regels en gebeuren dingen die zij niet begrijpt. Nadat ze een verborgen ritueel ziet, raakt ze verwikkeld in de strijd om de macht bij de fae. Haar poging een veilig bestaan op te bouwen verandert zo in een gevecht om haar eigen overleving.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61553450M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61553450M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"e5184ea56b8a9e612a70191a10e73bfbfb29d07f4fdca3b45dbd812fb9c98418","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Een dans met de fae prins","author":"Elise Kova","isbn":"9789493419049","language":"nld","parent":"OL24862945W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3340:nl","key":{"work_id":3340,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3340,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":171,"text":"De jonge agente Chevie krijgt de taak een tijdmachine te bewaken. Dat lijkt weinig opwindend, totdat er een jongen uit de Victoriaanse tijd verschijnt. Riley is niet alleen naar haar tijd gekomen: een huurmoordenaar volgt hem. Chevie en Riley moeten samenwerken om de achtervolger tegen te houden. Hun ontmoeting verbindt twee verschillende werelden, terwijl de machine die hen bijeenbracht ook nieuwe gevaren met zich meebrengt. Vluchten is daardoor niet eenvoudig een kwestie van afstand nemen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32986221M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32986221M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"b9f2b27c4431a7610582e51bb49465c8e83697da3c2def4d0a1bd7caad4e59f7","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"De onwillige moordenaar","author":"Eoin Colfer","isbn":"9789000329588","language":"nld","parent":"OL17471996W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3450:nl","key":{"work_id":3450,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3450,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1640,"text":"Tuinier Hallie krijgt werk bij de wijngaard van Julians familie, precies wanneer hij terugkeert om een roman te schrijven. Zij kent hem nog van haar jeugd en heeft haar gevoelens nooit helemaal losgelaten. De inmiddels zeer ordelijke professor raakt door haar aanwezigheid uit zijn zorgvuldig geplande ritme. Een impulsief verstuurde anonieme liefdesbrief maakt de situatie ingewikkelder. Terwijl Hallie haar geheim probeert te beheersen, merken beiden hoe moeilijk hun verwachtingen en hun groeiende aantrekkingskracht te verenigen zijn.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL60586001M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL60586001M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"e375325c9c8d963bce108def7f74ce6c75b473c45bacc7cbb4686ff9e89b036e","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Secretly Yours","author":"Tessa Bailey","isbn":"9789021485478","language":"nld","parent":"OL28020945W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3457:nl","key":{"work_id":3457,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3457,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1642,"text":"Op het eiland Joya mag Isabella haar dorp niet verlaten. Ze kent de kaarten van haar vader en verlangt ernaar zelf onbekend gebied te verkennen. Wanneer haar vriendin verdwijnt, biedt ze aan de zoektocht te leiden. Haar kennis van kaarten en sterren wordt belangrijk in een landschap waar oude verhalen en werkelijke gevaren elkaar raken. De expeditie brengt haar buiten de grenzen van het vertrouwde dorp, naar gebieden waar zij niet alleen een vermist meisje moet vinden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL62542425M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL62542425M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"f6636b38ae625ac3ffdfadfdceab1b87c19cf433ef7bf2364097215a2bf8bdf9","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Het meisje van inkt en sterren","author":"Kiran Millwood Hargrave","isbn":"9789021687810","language":"nld","parent":"OL20098004W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3472:nl","key":{"work_id":3472,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3472,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":164,"text":"Olivia groeit op in een weeshuis en bewaart het dagboek van haar verdwenen moeder als haar belangrijkste bezit. Ze kan niet spreken en ziet verschijningen die voor anderen verborgen blijven. Wanneer een familielid haar uitnodigt naar het landgoed Gallant, ziet ze een kans om haar afkomst te begrijpen. Tegelijk waarschuwt het dagboek haar juist voor die plek. Olivia gaat toch en ontdekt dat de belofte van een familie niet betekent dat het huis haar veiligheid biedt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL46534390M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL46534390M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"7e7a70b87c780c5bce89876fb56428a8f37cdad26a25fc4666cc6a314572132a","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Gallant","author":"V. E. Schwab","isbn":"9789022595213","language":"nld","parent":"OL24783202W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3532:nl","key":{"work_id":3532,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3532,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":342,"text":"De dood van twee invloedrijke mensen trekt onmiddellijk de aandacht van de media. Alex Cross kende de slachtoffers, onder wie een voormalige patiënt, en raakt daardoor ook persoonlijk bij het onderzoek betrokken. Terwijl zijn collega een van de sporen volgt, reist Cross met een FBI-agent naar Alabama. Achter de publieke levens van de doden blijken andere belangen en geheimen schuil te gaan. Cross moet bepalen welke aanwijzingen hij kan vertrouwen wanneer zijn eigen betrokkenheid het onderzoek ingewikkelder maakt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL41758461M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL41758461M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"6c23bdb98bdbd0d224af3e636b58fab8ab8158b7138bcd2e5d7bb022e69e07ab","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Dubbelspel","author":"James Patterson","isbn":"9789403179506","language":"nld","parent":"OL20978085W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:5133:nl","key":{"work_id":5133,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":5133,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":867,"text":"Amandine en Ambrose groeien op binnen de strenge verwachtingen van een Antwerpse bankiersfamilie. Zij krijgt een huwelijk opgelegd, terwijl haar tweelingbroer zich steeds verder verliest in een destructief bestaan. In séances zoeken ze een uitweg uit de wereld die hun leven bepaalt. Tijdens de Eerste Wereldoorlog kijkt Amandine terug op hun jeugd en de keuzes die volgden. Haar verhaal verbindt persoonlijke pogingen tot verzet met de macht en de onrust van haar omgeving.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61048982M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61048982M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"52622f2796dea006a48fc40f0f8ad4bd49412f53443f6f8faa6b8deb20566716","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"De wonderen","author":"Jeroen Olyslaegers","isbn":"9789403187914","language":"nld","parent":"OL44702832W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:5147:nl","key":{"work_id":5147,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":5147,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":636,"text":"De heer Tiennoppen raakt in de nacht en de schemering verwikkeld in een wereld waarin de grenzen van zijn eigen werkelijkheid verschuiven. Wat hij waarneemt en wat hij zich voorstelt, laten zich niet gemakkelijk scheiden. Rond dit personage bouwt Harry Mulisch verhalen waarin herkenbare maatschappelijke patronen een verontrustende gedaante krijgen. De bundel brengt vroege verhalen samen. De handelingen en ervaringen van Tiennoppen vormen een onderzoek naar de verhouding tussen een mens, zijn verbeelding en zijn omgeving.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL62157897M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL62157897M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"472baeda9f02dc3b066e6050cb5b6725c9c7aa1cee2afdff933dac8428c3e92c","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Het mirakel","author":"Harry Mulisch","isbn":"9789403112312","language":"nld","parent":"OL38718959W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:5187:nl","key":{"work_id":5187,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":5187,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":2628,"text":"Charlotte Delbo werd na haar werk voor het Franse verzet gevangengezet en naar Auschwitz-Birkenau gedeporteerd. In korte fragmenten probeert zij herinneringen aan het kamp onder woorden te brengen. Ze richt zich niet alleen op haar eigen ervaringen, maar ook op de vrouwen met wie zij gevangenschap deelde. Hun onderlinge steun staat naast de ontmenselijking van het dagelijks bestaan. De tekst zoekt een vorm om over leven, dood en herinnering te spreken zonder die ervaringen tot een doorlopend verhaal te vereenvoudigen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61366385M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61366385M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"76b22c9825fdadacd2a820ac0ef73199cf624691f92154388915313b29c5df7b","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Niemand van ons zal terugkeren","author":"Charlotte Delbo","isbn":"9789029094344","language":"nld","parent":"OL2398936W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:5196:nl","key":{"work_id":5196,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":5196,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":2444,"text":"Annie Jacobsen volgt een denkbeeldige kernwapenaanval en de beslissingen die daarop zouden kunnen volgen. Het scenario begint bij een lancering vanuit Noord-Korea en onderzoekt hoe weinig tijd er voor beoordeling en reactie beschikbaar is. Interviews en onderzoek naar militaire systemen vormen de achtergrond van de reconstructie. Het boek wil laten zien welke gevolgen escalatie kan hebben. De beschreven gebeurtenissen zijn een hypothetisch scenario, geen verslag van een werkelijke aanval of een vaststaande voorspelling.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL51484966M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL51484966M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"10ace18156cd1255dd8dae58b64b8f5fa5233b9d3c390f3097132d9bc18f9429","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Kernoorlog :","author":"Annie Jacobsen","isbn":"9789044655605","language":"nld","parent":"OL38364901W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:5703:nl","key":{"work_id":5703,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":5703,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3106,"text":"Michal Citroen onderzoekt hoe Nederlandse Joden na de oorlog werden ontvangen wanneer zij uit kampen of onderduik terugkeerden. Een gesprek met haar grootvader vormt een persoonlijk vertrekpunt voor het bredere onderzoek. Via getuigenissen beschrijft zij de problemen rond opvang, erkenning en het opnieuw opbouwen van een bestaan. De aandacht ligt op de eerste naoorlogse jaren en de reacties van de Nederlandse samenleving. Deze herziene uitgave behandelt terugkeer niet als vanzelfsprekend einde van de vervolging.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61329180M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61329180M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"a15fc76a4b2b6dbc5cce9e6ac6d79037bace7bac8f41b5378489873ff1e03b8c","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"U wordt door niemand verwacht","author":"Michal Citroen","isbn":"9789021340067","language":"nld","parent":"OL879909W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6123:nl","key":{"work_id":6123,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6123,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3293,"text":"Adrienne leeft in een Frans provinciestadje in een gezin dat haar weinig ruimte laat. Haar vader beheerst het huis en de verhouding met haar oudere zus wordt door jaloezie gekleurd. Wanneer Adrienne verliefd wordt, lijkt er een andere toekomst denkbaar, maar haar gevoelens bieden geen eenvoudige uitweg. Haar verlangen botst met de benauwende omgeving waarin zij opgroeit. De roman volgt hoe dat conflict steeds sterker haar waarneming en haar verhouding tot anderen bepaalt.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24756256M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24756256M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"26623b09db79ebb1b3de9cbba9a192ffa1199fa4991e08513777eab78e834952","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Adrienne Mesurat","author":"Julien Green","isbn":"9789025464608","language":"nld","parent":"OL569006W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6248:nl","key":{"work_id":6248,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6248,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3352,"text":"Een uitgebreide muizenfamilie trekt door het bos op zoek naar een nieuw thuis. Ouders, grootouders en tien kinderen moeten de verhuizing samen zien te volbrengen. Onderweg blijkt dat ieder familielid op een andere manier aan de tocht bijdraagt. De beelden volgen zowel het gezamenlijke avontuur als de kleine bezigheden van de afzonderlijke muizen. Het prentenboek draait om een veranderende woonplek, samenwerking en de aandacht die een gezin tijdens een onbekende onderneming voor elkaar heeft.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL62547692M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL62547692M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"f3f99571d8f0c6e219872a679f34ec9e21a9baf6fded35d80ce3b7e95df38016","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"14 muisjes verhuizen","author":"Kazuo Iwamura","isbn":"9789044829327","language":"nld","parent":"OL4482786W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6265:nl","key":{"work_id":6265,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6265,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3361,"text":"Wanneer Noa met haar moeder in een oud vakantiehuis terechtkomt, merkt ze dat het verleden er niet verdwenen is. De geest van een vermoord meisje probeert contact met haar te zoeken. Wat een verblijf op een nieuwe plek had moeten zijn, wordt daardoor een confrontatie met een onopgeloste gebeurtenis. Noa moet uitzoeken wat de verschijning haar wil vertellen. Het huis vormt tegelijk de plaats waar de aanwijzingen te vinden zijn en waar zij niet gemakkelijk aan de dreiging kan ontsnappen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35337468M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35337468M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"5c8c79a6e36de2a6108aa1e752fad36bb965c21ecd9b860f3bb5bfb14b1b5279","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Whisper","author":"Isabel Abedi","isbn":"9789047502029","language":"nld","parent":"OL24338494W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6334:nl","key":{"work_id":6334,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6334,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":1516,"text":"Een moordenaar gebruikt de berichten van zijn slachtoffers om hun vrienden gerust te stellen terwijl hij hen gevangenhoudt. Detective Sam Currie onderzoekt de zaak, waarin ook Dave Lewis als verdachte naar voren komt. Dave probeert ondertussen zijn eigen verlies en relaties te begrijpen. Wanneer iemand uit zijn verleden gevaar loopt, raken zijn persoonlijke zorgen en het onderzoek met elkaar verweven. De vraag wie achter de berichten zit, krijgt zo betekenis voor mensen die dachten nog gewoon contact te hebben.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35329941M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35329941M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"7a82b93a979b881b4ff97f218d70a5a3d795cd39624d2828169740e79af0b22a","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Niemand die je hoort","author":"Steve Mosby","isbn":"9789022993552","language":"nld","parent":"OL8475512W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6339:nl","key":{"work_id":6339,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6339,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3401,"text":"Wick Lichtmaker werkt als bibliothecaris in de Veste van Wereldwijsheid. Buiten die beschermde omgeving komt hij terecht in een wereld waarin zijn kennis alleen niet genoeg is om veilig te blijven. Hij moet moed verzamelen en tegelijk voorkomen dat anderen ontdekken waar de Veste zich bevindt. Zijn verantwoordelijkheid voor de bibliotheek reist met hem mee. Het avontuur draait daardoor niet alleen om zijn eigen terugkeer, maar ook om het bewaren van het geheim dat hem is toevertrouwd.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL38244609M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL38244609M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"a03befb4f4a6b380dd5666767dd6413c2307e209847ff42dc3e2a04b9aa9e907","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"De magie van het woord","author":"Mel Odom","isbn":"9789024556243","language":"nld","parent":"OL524337W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6341:nl","key":{"work_id":6341,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6341,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3402,"text":"Studenten denken in een druk winkelcentrum een verstorende mediastunt uit te voeren, maar hun apparatuur blijkt voor een veel gevaarlijker plan te worden gebruikt. Na de explosies moet FBI-agent Maggie O''Dell achterhalen wie de aanslag organiseerde. Een spoor loopt naar haar halfbroer, die kort daarvoor met de studenten contact had. Terwijl zij zijn betrokkenheid onderzoekt, komt er een waarschuwing voor een volgend doelwit. De zoektocht vraagt tegelijk om snelheid en voorzichtigheid bij het beoordelen van vertrouwde mensen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61027559M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61027559M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"62d5882e1f7bd89b856ba2d3ac5f1303ff9a9b819079e714611a289ad73ac763","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Zwarte vrijdag","author":"Alex Kava","isbn":"9789034747709","language":"nld","parent":"OL21418365W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6351:nl","key":{"work_id":6351,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6351,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3408,"text":"Een nachtelijk radioprogramma in Monte Carlo krijgt een beller die zegt een moordenaar te zijn. De volgende dag blijkt de dreiging ernstiger dan een slechte grap. Meer doden volgen en de telefoontjes bevatten muzikale aanwijzingen. FBI-agent Frank Ottobre en politieman Nicolas Hulot proberen het verband te begrijpen voordat er opnieuw iemand wordt aangevallen. Hun tegenstander gebruikt de uitzendingen om het onderzoek te sturen en daagt de speurders uit hem in te halen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL43195502M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL43195502M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"f99a42de2751ef46b2c7b15869455d278aae66c5855eaeb9aa5b1739877814e8","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Ik dood","author":"Giorgio Faletti","isbn":"9789044311341","language":"nld","parent":"OL36884316W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6386:nl","key":{"work_id":6386,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6386,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3438,"text":"Paardentrainer Sonia vertelt over haar leven rond de renbaan. Haar dagelijkse werk met de dieren staat ver af van het welvarende beeld dat toeschouwers bij de races kunnen zien. Ze kent de toewijding die paarden vragen, maar ook de harde arbeidsomstandigheden en de machtsverhoudingen achter de schermen. Kathryn Scanlan brengt haar ervaringen in korte hoofdstukken samen. Zo ontstaat een levensverhaal waarin zorg voor dieren, bestaanszekerheid en de economische wereld van de paardensport voortdurend op elkaar botsen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61297901M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61297901M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"60f13293150057220369ee75ee5ae0c41264b02cff249678cd8ce125ddb4c81f","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Vier de teugels","author":"Kathryn Scanlan","isbn":"9789028243019","language":"nld","parent":"OL27815506W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6390:nl","key":{"work_id":6390,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6390,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3442,"text":"In het door Duitsland bezette Maribor herkent Sonja een vroegere bekende die inmiddels SS-officier is. Ze hoopt via hem haar gevangengenomen geliefde Valentin te helpen. De hulp die zij zoekt, brengt haar echter in een vernederende en gevaarlijke afhankelijkheid. Oorlog en machtsmisbruik bepalen steeds sterker wat de geliefden kunnen doen. De roman volgt hun verbondenheid in omstandigheden waarin iedere keuze gevolgen heeft en waarin vrijlating nog geen einde aan het geweld betekent.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL60623675M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL60623675M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"6b93af7d358e116ce4580a7c4eb07a68687a2003b9a56f31fc2606c43fd00393","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"En ook de liefde","author":"Drago Jancar","isbn":"9789021417172","language":"nld","parent":"OL26416419W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2233:en","key":{"work_id":2233,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":2233,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1088,"text":"Cormoran Strike and Robin Ellacott investigate a body found in the vault of a shop selling silver. The police believe they know the dead man''s identity, but doubts remain. Establishing who the victim really was becomes the starting point for a case in which an apparently settled explanation needs to be questioned. The partners must work through the evidence rather than accept the first identification, while continuing the complicated professional relationship at the centre of the series.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL57592301M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL57592301M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"d44602bdc5ca52c7a80971706e031c444304072b11d05d9d88365752078a149a","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"The Hallmarked Man","author":"Robert Galbraith","isbn":"9780316586023","language":"eng","parent":"OL42397680W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2253:en","key":{"work_id":2253,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":2253,"language":"en","bound_author_id":756,"text":"Thomas Erikson examines manipulation through the personality framework used in his earlier book about communication. He considers how a person''s habits and vulnerabilities may be used by someone seeking control. The discussion focuses on recognising such interactions and responding to them in everyday relationships. Its colour categories and advice are the author''s explanatory model, not a clinical diagnosis of other people. The book presents strategies for setting limits rather than a verified method for identifying a psychiatric condition.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL29483638M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL29483638M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"214fc4d48ed5a68a39449ada2140df7fe54e9694f59121ff68ad6aa96b64ad3a","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Surrounded by Psychopaths","author":"Thomas Erikson","isbn":"9781785043321","language":"eng","parent":"OL20915117W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2499:en","key":{"work_id":2499,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":2499,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1218,"text":"Reverend Sabre Winfrey''s authority reaches beyond his church into the businesses and social life of Dominion, Mississippi. His youngest son is widely admired, and the family''s position appears secure. An unexpected encounter changes that appearance and sets events in motion across the community. Told through the women close to father and son, the novel examines the protection granted to powerful men and the consequences of conduct that people around them have learned to excuse.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL57588776M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL57588776M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"876faf68dff10978aaeae9c38b6080fd0ca0f9af10072dd1e4ddaa54d327669e","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Dominion","author":"Addie E. Citchens","isbn":"9780374609351","language":"eng","parent":"OL42441000W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2928:en","key":{"work_id":2928,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":2928,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1436,"text":"After losing her ability to fly, Broken leaves the organisation that once contained her superhero life. Michael Forward, who can see the future, draws her into an attempt to protect a baby whose survival may matter far beyond them. Their arrival also overturns Monica''s family life. The three become unlikely allies in a world increasingly shaped by fear and repression. Helping one another means acting without the security or powers they might once have expected to rely on.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26454664M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26454664M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"ef9dc559dc8ed80800972bb8b4e379ef0c5e03f64eb0a4d56817b2c09c507756","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Broken","author":"Susan Jane Bigelow","isbn":"9781936460045","language":"eng","parent":"OL17873745W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3102:en","key":{"work_id":3102,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3102,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1521,"text":"Vanessa leaves a Black orphanage in South Carolina and assumes the identity of a deceased white child. Under her new name, she moves to California and builds a different life. Marriage into a wealthy family seems to secure that escape, until a medical finding concerning her child exposes the history she concealed. Her husband''s response leads to a police investigation. A detective''s questions begin to uncover the gap between the family''s public standing and the private story behind it.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL49782722M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL49782722M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"fef4310a99755712701ee421711b3876560ff0304105d3d534bdaf035c18c649","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Deceptive Calm","author":"Patricia Skipper","isbn":"9798822930322","language":"eng","parent":"OL36855916W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3572:en","key":{"work_id":3572,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3572,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1676,"text":"Daksh Tyagi uses humour to examine contradictions in contemporary Indian life. His subjects include religious and social boundaries, family expectations, public behaviour and the difference between professed values and everyday choices. Rather than offering a single account of national character, the book moves through uncomfortable social and moral situations. Its satirical viewpoint invites readers to question familiar habits and assumptions, including the ways people make excuses for conduct they would condemn in somebody else.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL38233686M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL38233686M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"110c4cad89da7c149b308127ebbb5bb8b5272bbcd6d974e14fd61ded54b87d54","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"A Nation of Idiots","author":"Daksh Tyagi","isbn":"9788194275015","language":"eng","parent":"OL27968141W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3656:en","key":{"work_id":3656,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3656,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1746,"text":"Bob Burg discusses persuasion as an interaction that need not depend on pressure or intimidation. He considers how rapport, clear communication and respect can affect a difficult conversation. Examples from personal and professional settings lead into ways of responding to objections and seeking cooperation. The book''s practical approach asks readers to consider the other person''s position as well as their own purpose. Its advice is presented as a communication method, not a guarantee that others will agree.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL30451398M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL30451398M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"794fb3fda8101fb3227d3f186da8bfd8da35f1d30502adbd17db3b24f300c8e5","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"The art of persuasion","author":"Bob Burg","isbn":"9780768413007","language":"eng","parent":"OL22367098W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3761:en","key":{"work_id":3761,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3761,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1829,"text":"Norman Melchert introduces Western philosophy as a continuing exchange of arguments rather than a collection of isolated opinions. Moving from ancient Greek thought through later periods, he follows questions about knowledge, reality, conduct and human life. Each thinker is placed in relation to ideas that came before and challenges that followed. The book gives readers a historical framework for comparing positions and understanding why philosophical disagreements return in changing forms across different times.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61421782M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL61421782M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"132e9c056cea8945bdc2817132896872853eef7dd13e8be4a465c57fe661b349","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"The Great Conversation","author":"Norman Melchert","isbn":"9780195322729","language":"eng","parent":"OL1810842W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3905:en","key":{"work_id":3905,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3905,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1953,"text":"Yoweri Kaguta Museveni recounts his life and political activity from his own perspective. He connects his education and early commitments with the conflicts that shaped Uganda, including opposition to Idi Amin and later struggles over the country''s military and political direction. The memoir also sets out his understanding of national development. These are the author''s recollections and arguments about his role, rather than an independent judgment of his leadership or an endorsement of his account.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL51516353M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL51516353M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"2db2f6ee24adfbbb8bf6f67c0e1c6a516bddcb81c8aa8d18294b1087d39493b8","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Sowing the Mustard Seed","author":"Yoweri Kaguta Museveni","isbn":"9789966630131","language":"eng","parent":"OL9273749W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:4239:en","key":{"work_id":4239,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":4239,"language":"en","bound_author_id":2211,"text":"A supercomputer called AM has destroyed almost all humanity and kept five people alive in an underground world it controls. Their continued existence becomes a means for the machine to punish the species that created it. Told through Ted, the story follows the survivors as they seek food and some possibility of relief. Their dependence on AM makes even ordinary needs part of a struggle against an intelligence that can reshape their surroundings and suffering.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35505875M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35505875M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"6844e307d2788a4a7b10a9d4ba57a1938b890476236090118695cd3e4a991eb8","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"I Have No Mouth and I Must Scream","author":"Harlan Ellison","isbn":"9781497609617","language":"eng","parent":"OL26301720W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:4571:en","key":{"work_id":4571,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":4571,"language":"en","bound_author_id":302,"text":"Christmas brings the Spring siblings together at a difficult point in their family life. Charlie is dealing with an eating disorder, while Tori and Oliver experience the holiday from their own positions within the household. The novella moves between the siblings'' perspectives rather than treating the celebration as a simple reunion. Moments of care sit beside anxiety and misunderstanding. Set in the world of Solitaire and Heartstopper, it focuses on the strain and small connections within one family.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL46125203M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL46125203M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"b1b63a197f0ffdbde74a84d4d8368cee945869baa7210b36b4164f25accbf117","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"This Winter","author":"Alice Oseman","isbn":"9781338885132","language":"eng","parent":"OL21691171W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:4779:en","key":{"work_id":4779,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":4779,"language":"en","bound_author_id":2481,"text":"Jack Kuper recalls his childhood in Nazi-occupied Poland after separation from his family. To survive, he moves between hiding places and households, changing the identity he presents to people who might expose him. Hunger, fear and uncertainty shape the decisions of a child forced to depend on strangers. The memoir describes both assistance and cruelty without making safety seem secure. Its focus is the experience of trying to remain alive while the world around him becomes threatening.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35727000M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35727000M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"c511db7509029a91190ac99ae38f46890508c06115740e8dfabac99c0118a118","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Child of the holocaust","author":"Jack Kuper","isbn":"9780770423254","language":"eng","parent":"OL3580581W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:4887:en","key":{"work_id":4887,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":4887,"language":"en","bound_author_id":2554,"text":"Steven Kotler explores how people approach demanding goals through motivation, attention, creativity and flow. He brings these topics together as parts of sustained performance rather than treating achievement as a single moment of inspiration. The book considers habits and conditions that may support learning and focused work. Examples of ambitious pursuits sit alongside the author''s practical framework. It offers an approach to developing performance, not a promise that every reader can achieve the same result.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL29891575M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL29891575M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"c6b5c5a064849194708e3d9c3ac70d6a9c8273f8996aca6b17d084ef9c9ff2ad","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Art of Impossible","author":"Steven Kotler","isbn":"9780062977533","language":"eng","parent":"OL21915475W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6806:en","key":{"work_id":6806,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6806,"language":"en","bound_author_id":3797,"text":"Evelyn Lord investigates the groups known as Hell-Fire Clubs by looking beyond the sensational stories attached to them. The book asks who joined these clubs, what participants believed and did, and why similar associations appeared in different settings. Accounts of scandal become questions to examine rather than facts to accept uncritically. Its historical approach separates the reputation of the clubs from the evidence for their membership, activities and place in the society around them.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24766460M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24766460M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"bdf5f83e17de761aafe558b44ab51b1e67c354a08198774edf35ceb29fb51513","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"The Hell-Fire clubs","author":"Evelyn Lord","isbn":"9780300116670","language":"eng","parent":"OL15857521W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:7167:en","key":{"work_id":7167,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":7167,"language":"en","bound_author_id":4095,"text":"Cathy Park Hong brings personal recollection into conversation with cultural criticism and history. Growing up as the daughter of Korean immigrants provides a starting point for examining racial identity and the feelings that dominant stories about America fail to acknowledge. The essays move through language, art, friendship and family. Hong uses the tension between public optimism and lived experience to consider how a person comes to understand herself and the categories imposed on her.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL31848207M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL31848207M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"217bea06551683aaf21a4cbc8bd5b01d4439e3896bdb1ef44985f79a917385de","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Minor Feelings","author":"Cathy Park Hong","isbn":"9781984820389","language":"eng","parent":"OL20653266W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:7263:en","key":{"work_id":7263,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":7263,"language":"en","bound_author_id":4175,"text":"Mark Rudd looks back on his involvement in the American student radical movement of the 1960s. He follows his movement from university protest into the organisation associated with the Weathermen and the escalation towards political violence. The memoir considers the ideals, decisions and consequences that shaped that journey. Written after a long period of silence, it is a participant''s attempt to account for his actions rather than a detached history of every group involved.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24947863M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24947863M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"2d6b56f960b57341d4dbfb03495bb549361ea59f1851727b42e2a929416bc54d","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Underground","author":"Mark Rudd","isbn":"9780061472756","language":"eng","parent":"OL16047226W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:7343:en","key":{"work_id":7343,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":7343,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1678,"text":"A struggling business leader encounters Julian Mantle, a former lawyer whose life has taken a different direction. Their conversations form the framework for Robin Sharma''s advice about leadership. Through this fable, the book discusses vision, responsibility, relationships at work and the personal habits of someone guiding others. Eight practices organise the lessons. The narrative is used to explore a style of management based on purpose and service, rather than simply presenting a list of business instructions.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL8369150M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL8369150M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"64f94b3da6093c04c509dec8d2bed1ce395a88ef39acd24f32dad4f9a2f5b5ba","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Leadership Wisdom from the Monk Who Sold His Ferrari","author":"Robin S. Sharma","isbn":"9781401900137","language":"eng","parent":"OL1854816W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:7519:en","key":{"work_id":7519,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":7519,"language":"en","bound_author_id":4394,"text":"Lorna Byrne recounts experiences she understands as encounters with angels and other spiritual beings. Her account connects these experiences with comfort, guidance and the events of her own life. The book presents a personal spiritual outlook in which such beings remain close to ordinary people. It describes what the author believes she has perceived, rather than independently establishing the existence of angels or offering those claims as medical or scientific explanations of human experience.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24967147M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24967147M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"e97b1fa3ea9a50d6234673ecce4acf616996e485cc3f1483f78ac6325ad75fef","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Angels in my hair","author":"Lorna Byrne","isbn":"9780385528962","language":"eng","parent":"OL16070062W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:8125:en","key":{"work_id":8125,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":8125,"language":"en","bound_author_id":4895,"text":"This secondary-school history text surveys societies across different regions and periods. Political events are considered alongside economic life, cultural change, technologies and belief systems. Its chronological structure also draws attention to connections made through trade, migration and conflict. Maps and source material support the account. Rather than following one nation''s story alone, the book gives students a framework for comparing developments and understanding how encounters between societies have contributed to wider historical change.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL9652658M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL9652658M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"fe4060d49025b89e2e8cacd8fbb3266f327c2986df6e51984fac97afdb05a82f","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"World History","author":"Roger B. Beck","isbn":"9780618690084","language":"eng","parent":"OL46520W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:8173:en","key":{"work_id":8173,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":8173,"language":"en","bound_author_id":4930,"text":"Susan Campbell Bartoletti examines the emergence of the Ku Klux Klan after the American Civil War. The book places the group''s origins within the racism, insecurity and political struggles of the period, showing how organised intimidation affected communities and civil rights. Written for younger readers, it distinguishes the Klan''s self-justifications from the violence of its actions. The historical account asks how a movement of terror took shape and what its development reveals about American society.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL23936228M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL23936228M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"9c76c80de91f2af726bbd0316d6f17de1188107095ef996ee729f6f6a96eee26","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"They called themselves the K.K.K.","author":"Susan Campbell Bartoletti","isbn":"9780618440337","language":"eng","parent":"OL15550439W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:9225:en","key":{"work_id":9225,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":9225,"language":"en","bound_author_id":5361,"text":"Janina lives in a remote Polish village, spending time with astrology, William Blake''s poetry and the houses she looks after for absent owners. When a neighbour dies and further deaths follow, she becomes convinced she can help explain what is happening. Others are less willing to listen to a woman they regard as eccentric. Her attempts to enter the investigation bring her views about animals, people and the surrounding community into conflict with accepted explanations.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL57188709M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL57188709M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"dc5b205fec451468f26586cd4ccd70b7980830ce5e7158d80e33d40036306bf7","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Drive Your Plow Over The Bones Of The Dead","author":"Olga Tokarczuk","isbn":"9780525541349","language":"eng","parent":"OL17351965W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:10125:en","key":{"work_id":10125,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":10125,"language":"en","bound_author_id":5233,"text":"Delle wants a place on the cheerleading squad at Salem University. Training under the new coach seems to offer the opportunity she has been waiting for, until she learns what happened to the previous team. The demands placed on the recruits begin to suggest something more dangerous than a difficult selection process. Delle must decide how to respond when pursuing her ambition may expose her to the same threat that faced the girls before her.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL7541451M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL7541451M","snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","sourceTextSha256":"71d7264bd96e16dcd6006e49c4396a8c8b616960913efca6d55d0181466e5669","role":"Exact edition narrative manually read; original short factual account, not copied opinion or bibliography","identity":{"title":"Nightmare Hall #5 The Scream Team","author":"Diane Hoh","isbn":"9780590471374","language":"eng","parent":"OL3585151W"},"factsReview":"Premise and subject checked against the saved substantive source. Promotional judgements, major outcomes, clinical/religious/political truth claims and unsupported ages omitted."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1203:nl","key":{"work_id":1203,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1203,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":704,"text":"Jacob Willem Katadreuffe groeit in het Rotterdam van voor de Tweede Wereldoorlog op bij zijn ongehuwde moeder. Hij is vastbesloten advocaat te worden en probeert zich uit zijn armoedige omstandigheden omhoog te werken. Zijn vader, de machtige deurwaarder Dreverhaven, maakt hem dat bijzonder moeilijk. Tussen beiden ontstaat een strijd waarin geen van de twee wil toegeven. Katadreuffes streven naar onafhankelijkheid vraagt steeds meer van zijn persoonlijke leven en zijn vermogen zich aan anderen te verbinden.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24700930M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24700930M","role":"Exact ISBN9789023652779/title/Katadreuffe narrative, sole OL1355544W parent, Dutch and paperback; author authority retained from saved export.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24700930M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/language/sole parent and book-author binding; content sources above do not replace edition identity","identity":{"title":"Karakter","author":"Ferdinand Bordewijk","isbn":"9789023652779","language":"nld","parent":"OL1355544W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1348:nl","key":{"work_id":1348,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1348,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":658,"text":"Lucia en de jonge Giacomo Casanova ontmoeten elkaar bij Venetië en denken dat hun toekomst samen vastligt. Toch verdwijnt zij uit zijn leven zonder haar vertrek uit te leggen. Wanneer hun wegen jaren later in Amsterdam opnieuw kruisen, kijkt Lucia terug op wat er tussen hen gebeurde. Vanuit haar herinneringen ontstaat een ander beeld van de liefde die Casanova verloor. De roman volgt haar eigen keuzes en de afstand tussen uiterlijk, herinnering en verlangen.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.arthurjapin.nl","source_url":"https://www.arthurjapin.nl/een-schitterend-gebrek","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.arthurjapin.nl/een-schitterend-gebrek","role":"Author original Work premise: Lucia/Casanova young love near Venice, disappearance, later Amsterdam encounter and Lucia''s retrospective.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.singeluitgeverijen.nl/de-arbeiderspers/boek/een-schitterend-gebrek-2/","role":"Publisher confirms same Work/author premise; current2026ISBN not substituted for selected historical ISBN9789029573641.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.bruna.nl/images/active/InkijkPDF/9789029573641.PDF","role":"Exact publisher imprint ISBN9789029573641 and Arthur Japin; no excerpt prose copied.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28289681M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/language/sole parent and book-author binding; content sources above do not replace edition identity","identity":{"title":"Een schitterend gebrek","author":"Arthur Japin","isbn":"9789029573641","language":"nld","parent":"OL660527W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:5935:nl","key":{"work_id":5935,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":5935,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3214,"text":"Na de dood van zijn vader ontdekt Braverman Shaw dat deze een geheime rol vervulde binnen een eeuwenoude orde. Als kenner van de Middeleeuwen en ontcijferaar van codes moet hij de achtergelaten aanwijzingen volgen. Ze leiden naar een verborgen testament dat voor verschillende partijen van groot belang is. Jenny Logan krijgt de taak hem te beschermen, maar haar aanwezigheid neemt zijn wantrouwen niet weg. Bravo zoekt uit welke verplichtingen zijn vader hem heeft nagelaten.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/eric-van-lustbader/het-testament-2/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/eric-van-lustbader/het-testament-2/","role":"Official ebook of same Work, not selected print: BravoShaw, Dexter death, medieval order guarding testament, JennyLogan. Narrative only; do not change editionISBN.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.boekwinkeltjes.nl/b/177232828/Het-testament/","role":"Selected exact9789022992470, EricVanLustbader, Dutch paperback, AWBruna; saved OL35337590M identity independently retained.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35337590M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/language/sole parent and book-author binding; content sources above do not replace edition identity","identity":{"title":"Het testament","author":"Eric Van Lustbader","isbn":"9789022992470","language":"nld","parent":"OL2454249W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6189:nl","key":{"work_id":6189,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6189,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3200,"text":"Aan het einde van een vakantie in een Frans dorp verdwijnen Hermans vrouw en zoontje. Terwijl andere vakantiegangers naar huis terugkeren, blijft hij achter om hen te zoeken. De bewoners en plaatselijke instanties bieden hem weinig houvast. Wat tijdens de zomer vertrouwd leek, wordt in het aanhoudende slechte weer steeds vreemder. Herman raakt afhankelijk van een gemeenschap met ondoorzichtige regels. Zijn zoektocht wordt daardoor ook een confrontatie met de grenzen tussen een bezoeker en een dorpsbewoner.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.catranslation.org","source_url":"https://www.catranslation.org/video/marie-ndiayes-that-time-of-year-jordan-stump-and-imani-perry/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.catranslation.org/video/marie-ndiayes-that-time-of-year-jordan-stump-and-imani-perry/","role":"Publishing institution''s substantive same-Work account: Herman''s missing wife/son, end of tourist season, unhelpful authorities and pressure to assimilate; not selected Dutch edition proof.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.boekwinkeltjes.nl/b/234953733/De-tijd-van-het-jaar-roman/","role":"Exact Dutch9789052262949, MarieNDiaye, DeGeus1996, gekartonneerd met stofomslag. Translator not coauthor.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32986799M","role":"Exact Dutch edition/sole parent retained; English source is only used for verified Work content.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32986799M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/language/sole parent and book-author binding; content sources above do not replace edition identity","identity":{"title":"De tijd van het jaar","author":"Marie NDiaye","isbn":"9789052262949","language":"nld","parent":"OL21176129W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6232:nl","key":{"work_id":6232,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6232,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3200,"text":"Voor haar man en dochter is zij Clarisse, maar bij haar moeder blijft zij Malinka. Jarenlang houdt ze die twee levens uit elkaar en verbergt ze de bezoeken aan haar moeder Ladivine. Ook haar dochter draagt die naam, zonder de familiegeschiedenis te kennen die ermee verbonden is. De geheimhouding trekt sporen door haar huwelijk en de verhoudingen tussen drie generaties. Wanneer het gezinsleven uiteenvalt, blijken afkomst en verzwegen herinneringen zich niet eenvoudig te laten afschudden.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"singeluitgeverijen.nl","source_url":"https://singeluitgeverijen.nl/de-geus/boek/ladivine/","evidence":[{"url":"https://singeluitgeverijen.nl/de-geus/boek/ladivine/","role":"Exact9789044532708 Dutch paperback, MarieNDiaye; Clarisse/Malinka, motherLadivine secretlyvisited, daughteralsoLadivine, husbandRichard. Major later events omitted.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL33334507M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/language/sole parent and book-author binding; content sources above do not replace edition identity","identity":{"title":"Ladivine","author":"Marie NDiaye","isbn":"9789044532708","language":"nld","parent":"OL20024841W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:6486:nl","key":{"work_id":6486,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":6486,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3168,"text":"Steffie Steek zoekt liefde en een leven dat op de beloften uit romantische verhalen lijkt. De raadgevingen van vrouwenbladen en het commentaar van haar tante maken die zoektocht niet eenvoudiger. Dubravka Ugrešić vertelt haar belevenissen in een vorm die verschillende soorten teksten als lapjes aan elkaar verbindt. Zo worden vertrouwde liefdesverhalen en hun verwachtingen zichtbaar gemaakt en onderbroken. De roman richt zich op de spanning tussen een gedroomd vrouwenleven en de pogingen dat werkelijk vorm te geven.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"www.dbnl.org","source_url":"https://www.dbnl.org/tekst/_uit016uitg14_01/_uit016uitg14_01_0012.php","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.dbnl.org/tekst/_uit016uitg14_01/_uit016uitg14_01_0012.php","role":"Library-hosted published critical account of the actual novella: Steffie''s search for partner, aunt''s oversight, patchwork structure from women''s magazines/romance/literary conventions. No quoted passages copied.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://books.google.com/books/about/Steffie_Steek_in_de_klauwen_van_het_leve.html?id=Oz120AEACAAJ","role":"Exact Dutch9789067661744, DubravkaUgresic, Muntinga1994, Rainbow174; satire subject corroborates actual novella.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.bol.com/nl/nl/f/steffie-steek-in-de-klauwen-van-het-leven/34235359/","role":"Exact ISBN formatPaperback only. REJECT advertised child-abuse plot: contradicts independent literary source; not imported as content.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35329310M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/language/sole parent and book-author binding; content sources above do not replace edition identity","identity":{"title":"Steffie Steek in de klauwen van het leven","author":"Dubravka Ugrešić","isbn":"9789067661744","language":"nld","parent":"OL10556778W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3575:en","key":{"work_id":3575,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3575,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1678,"text":"Robin Sharma presents a routine built around protecting the first hour of the day from ordinary demands. His approach divides that time between physical activity, reflection and learning, alongside wider ideas about habits and attention. A story carries the lessons rather than presenting them only as a list of instructions. The book explains Sharma''s proposed method for organising mornings and personal priorities; its promises about performance and wellbeing are the author''s advice, not guaranteed outcomes.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"robinsharma.com","source_url":"https://robinsharma.com/books/","evidence":[{"url":"https://robinsharma.com/books/","role":"Author describes 5AM and20/20/20 morning routine move/reflect/grow. Claims of guaranteed health/productivity outcomes not adopted as fact.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://dhjhkxawhe8q4.cloudfront.net/hcca-wp/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/24143831/WS25-Canadiana-Catalogue.pdf","role":"HarperCollins official catalogue page8 exact9781443460316 RobinSharma Paperback. Do not substitute otherISBN canceled in a different library manifestation.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28940306M","role":"Selected English exactISBN/soleParentOL19665926W and author authority retained; contents include morning formula and sleep.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28940306M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/language/sole parent and book-author binding; content sources above do not replace edition identity","identity":{"title":"The 5 AM Club","author":"Robin S. Sharma","isbn":"9781443460316","language":"eng","parent":"OL19665926W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3594:en","key":{"work_id":3594,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3594,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1694,"text":"Vex King draws on his own experiences to offer advice about self-worth, habits and the way people respond to difficulties. The chapters connect everyday practices such as self-care and reflection with a wider spiritual account of positive thinking. Readers are invited to question limiting beliefs and their dependence on other people''s approval. This is King''s personal-development approach to changing one''s outlook, rather than a clinical treatment or a promise that thoughts alone determine events.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"shop.hayhouse.com","source_url":"https://shop.hayhouse.com/products/good-vibes-good-life","evidence":[{"url":"https://shop.hayhouse.com/products/good-vibes-good-life","role":"Publisher exact9781788171823 VexKing English TradePaperback; self-worth/mindset/self-care, authorpersonalexperience and spirituality. Manifestation/spiritual claims attributed, not scientific guarantees.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28689951M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/language/sole parent and book-author binding; content sources above do not replace edition identity","identity":{"title":"Good Vibes, Good Life","author":"Vex King","isbn":"9781788171823","language":"eng","parent":"OL20884418W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:8588:en","key":{"work_id":8588,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":8588,"language":"en","bound_author_id":5155,"text":"In a small Australian town, Charlie is drawn into a secret when Jasper Jones comes to his window one night asking for help. What Jasper shows him leaves the two boys afraid of the consequences if anyone discovers their involvement. They try to find out who is responsible while suspicion gathers around them. Charlie must navigate his own family and friendships as well as a community where prejudice can shape what people are willing to believe.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"natlib.govt.nz","source_url":"https://natlib.govt.nz/records/22993379","evidence":[{"url":"https://natlib.govt.nz/records/22993379","role":"National library exact9780375866661 tradeHardcover; other librarybinding/ebook ISBNs separatelyqualified. CraigSilvey, smalltown1960sAustralia, Jasper/Charlie hiding discovery while seeking responsible person.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.betterworldbooks.com/product/detail/jasper-jones-9780375866661","role":"Exact EnglishHardcover; narrative Charlie''s nightvisitorJasper, secret discovery, communitysuspicion. No awards or retailer ratings copied.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24913733M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/language/sole parent and book-author binding; content sources above do not replace edition identity","identity":{"title":"Jasper Jones","author":"Craig Silvey","isbn":"9780375866661","language":"eng","parent":"OL16010187W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:8953:en","key":{"work_id":8953,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":8953,"language":"en","bound_author_id":5266,"text":"Grubbs Grady expects his world to consist of ordinary dislikes, family arguments and tricks played on his sister. A decision not to join a family weekend takes him somewhere far more frightening. Demons and werewolves become immediate dangers rather than things safely contained in stories. As the familiar boundaries of his life collapse, he has to confront a reality he did not know existed. This novel begins Darren Shan''s Demonata series.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.hachettebookgroup.com","source_url":"https://www.hachettebookgroup.com/titles/darren-shan/lord-loss/9780316012331/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.hachettebookgroup.com/titles/darren-shan/lord-loss/9780316012331/","role":"Publisher exact9780316012331, DarrenShan, EnglishTradePaperback, Demonata1. GrubbsGrady ordinary siblingpranks then missesfamilytrip and facesdemons/werewolves. Disregard stalepreorder widget for2006date.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL9869030M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/language/sole parent and book-author binding; content sources above do not replace edition identity","identity":{"title":"Demonata #1, The: Lord Loss","author":"Darren Shan","isbn":"9780316012331","language":"eng","parent":"OL5727066W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1500:en","key":{"work_id":1500,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1500,"language":"en","bound_author_id":803,"text":"Minke receives a Dutch education in colonial Java, yet the society around him continues to judge people by ancestry and social position. His relationship with Annelies draws him into the household of her resourceful mother, Nyai Ontosoroh. As personal hopes collide with colonial power, he discovers how little protection education and ambition can provide. The novel follows his growing understanding of the unequal world in which he is trying to make a life.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.penguinrandomhouse.com","source_url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/328806/this-earth-of-mankind-by-pramoedya-ananta-toer/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/328806/this-earth-of-mankind-by-pramoedya-ananta-toer/","role":"Publisher same-Work premise: Minke, colonial Java and Annelies; current paperback9780140256352 is NOT selected hardcover9780688093730.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.publishersweekly.com/9780688093730","role":"Exact selected ISBN, title, author and Morrow publication; independently corroborates Minke, Annelies'' family and colonial legal conflict.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32935009M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/English/sole parent and book-author binding; other market editions supply Work facts only","identity":{"title":"This Earth of Mankind","author":"Pramoedya Ananta Toer","isbn":"9780688093730","language":"eng","parent":"OL307247W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:2268:en","key":{"work_id":2268,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":2268,"language":"en","bound_author_id":961,"text":"The residents of a small village assemble for their annual drawing. Familiar neighbours exchange ordinary remarks while officials prepare an old box and check the participating households. Some traditions surrounding the ceremony have faded, but questioning the event itself meets resistance. Jackson''s short story builds unease through the contrast between everyday community life and unquestioning obedience.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.newyorker.com","source_url":"https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/1948/06/26/the-lottery","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/1948/06/26/the-lottery","role":"Original publisher text: village gathering, household drawing, worn black box and resistance to abandoning the ritual. Ending not disclosed; no story prose copied.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26644866M","role":"Exact ISBN9781563127878 English paperback, sole OL3171085W, ShirleyJackson, TaleBlazers/PerfectionLearning; study exercises/answer key20-30. Not the1949collection.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26644866M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/English/sole parent and book-author binding; other market editions supply Work facts only","identity":{"title":"The Lottery","author":"Shirley Jackson","isbn":"9781563127878","language":"eng","parent":"OL3171085W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:3820:en","key":{"work_id":3820,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":3820,"language":"en","bound_author_id":1879,"text":"Smith and Doe offer a deliberately provocative account of what men may conceal in intimate relationships. They discuss private fantasies, dishonesty, fidelity and the gap between public behaviour and unspoken desires. Addressing women directly, the authors present their observations as a way to understand partners and romantic expectations. The book''s combative claims are the authors'' perspective on relationships, not established conclusions about every man or a clinical guide to psychological treatment.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL9853296M","evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL9853296M","role":"ExactISBN9780312186791, English hardcover, soleOL9283877W, Smith&DoeStaff; saved edition narrative and Work-author binding agree.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://brownsbfs.co.uk/Product/Smith/What-Men-Dont-Want-Women-to-Know/9780312186791","role":"ExactISBN/Hardback/StMartin''sPress and book-specific subject matter. BIC French tag contradicts explicit exact-edition English and is rejected as language evidence.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.foyles.co.uk/book/what-men-dont-want-women-to-know/smith/9780312186791","role":"Independent exact title/ISBN/hardback corroboration. No author-name merge or page/date overwrite.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL9853296M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/English/sole parent and book-author binding; other market editions supply Work facts only","identity":{"title":"What Men Don''t Want Women To Know","author":"Smith & Doe Staff","isbn":"9780312186791","language":"eng","parent":"OL9283877W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:7473:en","key":{"work_id":7473,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":7473,"language":"en","bound_author_id":4355,"text":"Ghost-hunting investigators Jason Hawes and Grant Wilson join Cameron Dokey in presenting suspenseful accounts inspired by their investigations. The stories turn unusual occurrences and possible explanations into mysteries, with misleading clues and moments of uncertainty. Alongside the cases, the book introduces investigation techniques, equipment and ways to recognise a hoax. It describes the authors'' approach to reported paranormal activity without establishing that the supernatural explanations are true.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.hachettebookgroup.com","source_url":"https://www.hachettebookgroup.com/titles/jason-hawes/ghost-hunt/9780316129138/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.hachettebookgroup.com/titles/jason-hawes/ghost-hunt/9780316129138/","role":"Publisher same-Work dramatized investigations, JasonHawes/GrantWilson/withCameronDokey, equipment and hoax recognition. Ebook9780316129138 does not establish format of selected ScholasticISBN9780545419901.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://shop.scholastic.com/content/dam/scholastic/tso/programs---services/curriculum/leveled-reading/leveled-bookroom/LBR_TitleList.pdf","role":"Publisher school catalogue corroborates Ghost Hunt by JasonHawes and GrantWilson with CameronDokey. No claim that paranormal events are proven.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32101843M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/English/sole parent and book-author binding; other market editions supply Work facts only","identity":{"title":"Ghost hunt","author":"Jason Hawes","isbn":"9780545419901","language":"eng","parent":"OL16507722W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:8665:en","key":{"work_id":8665,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":8665,"language":"en","bound_author_id":5183,"text":"Eleven-year-old Jenny travels from China to her grandfather''s home, Graymark House, expecting to find her family. Instead, nobody there recognises her. She accepts work as a maid while trying to understand why her arrival has gone so strangely wrong. Moving through the house as a servant, she must investigate the people around her and the secrets hidden behind its imposing appearance. The mystery centres on her search for recognition and belonging.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"books.google.com","source_url":"https://books.google.com/books/about/Ghosts_in_the_Gallery.html?id=5hUViLO4kWgC","evidence":[{"url":"https://books.google.com/books/about/Ghosts_in_the_Gallery.html?id=5hUViLO4kWgC","role":"Publisher-supplied same-Work account: Jenny11, China, grandfatherGraymarkHouse, unrecognised, maid and investigation. Different AladdinISBN9780689839153 not substituted for selected Scholastic9780439352901.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26336428M","role":"Exact selected ISBN/title/English/BarbaraBrooksWallace and soleOL17737017W; no approved image or format inferred from other editions.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26336428M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/English/sole parent and book-author binding; other market editions supply Work facts only","identity":{"title":"Ghosts in the gallery","author":"Barbara Brooks Wallace","isbn":"9780439352901","language":"eng","parent":"OL17737017W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:9163:en","key":{"work_id":9163,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":9163,"language":"en","bound_author_id":361,"text":"Remy Morgan is married to Cease, a young hustler in Flint, Michigan. After she is shot and killed, he faces a murder trial. On the morning of the proceedings, he turns to her diary and begins discovering a past that their life together had concealed. As he reads, the woman he thought he knew becomes increasingly difficult to understand. The story connects those discoveries with his struggle to defend himself.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.kensingtonbooks.com","source_url":"https://www.kensingtonbooks.com/shop/diary-of-a-street-diva/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.kensingtonbooks.com/shop/diary-of-a-street-diva/","role":"ExactISBN9781893196452, paperback1May2006, UrbanBooks, AshleyandJaQuavis; Remy/Cease/Flint, gunshot death, trial morning and diary. Ebook9781645568209 kept separate.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL23094243M","checkedAt":"2026-10-31","snapshot":"2026-09-30","role":"Exact selected edition ISBN/title/English/sole parent and book-author binding; other market editions supply Work facts only","identity":{"title":"Diary of a street diva","author":"Ashley & JaQuavis","isbn":"9781893196452","language":"eng","parent":"OL8912318W"}}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:389:en","key":{"work_id":389,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":389,"language":"en","bound_author_id":241,"text":"A boy regularly visits a tree, enjoying its fruit, branches and company. As he grows older, the things he asks for change, and the tree keeps finding ways to give him more. Their relationship unfolds across the boy''s life, revealing the unequal demands that affection can carry. Silverstein uses a simple encounter between a person and a tree to explore generosity, dependence and what remains when familiar ways of giving are exhausted.","source_type":"official_publisher","source_name":"www.shelsilverstein.com","source_url":"https://www.shelsilverstein.com/9780060256654/the-giving-tree/","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.shelsilverstein.com/9780060256654/the-giving-tree/","role":"Author official exact selectedISBN/Hardcover and narrative premise; other library/ebook ISBNs remain separate. No2014market-date overwrite of original1964year.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL22142270M","role":"ExactISBN/title/byShelSilverstein/authorOL548174A/English/soleparentOL3368231W. Local Work389 authorityOL3368288W verified as JSON redirect to this parent, not another Work.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL3368288W.json","role":"Live31Oct JSONtype/redirect/locationOL3368231W recorded in remaining-identity-live-probes.json. No duplicate canonical Work in frozen production or currentTEST. Keep local identity/ratingsmeaning; no authority merge.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1698:nl","key":{"work_id":1698,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":1698,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":887,"text":"Kort voor Kerstmis raakt het dagelijkse leven van een schrijver steeds sterker verstrikt in zijn angsten en verlangens. Wat hij waarneemt, roept nieuwe vermoedens en erotische fantasieën op, terwijl ook godsdienstige gedachten zich opdringen. Zijn blik op zichzelf en zijn omgeving levert geen geruststellend overzicht op. Reve laat de innerlijke onrust van de schrijver botsen met alledaagse omstandigheden, waarbij ernst, achterdocht en ironie voortdurend in elkaar overlopen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"rozet.nl","source_url":"https://rozet.nl/catalogus/2373868/","evidence":[{"url":"https://rozet.nl/catalogus/2373868/","role":"Independent Dutch library same-Work narrative: writer beforeChristmas/fears/eroticfantasies/religion/irony. LibraryISBN9789023421788 is different edition, not selectedISBN or cover.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.deslegte.com/antwerpen-wapper/bezorgde-ouders-341134/","role":"ExactISBN9789025401603/title/GerardReve/Paperback/Veen1993/319pages. Supports local book-author binding independently from differing providerauthor keys.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.boekwinkeltjes.nl/b/236928438/Bezorgde-ouders/","role":"ExactISBN9789025401603 explicitlyDutch/Paperback/GerardReve. SameDeSlegte seller, not counted as a second independent seller.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL25844223M","role":"ExactISBN/Dutch/soleOL17271251W/byGerardReve. ProviderauthorOL7272669A not merged with localOL3894395A; independent book-author binding only.","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031"},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:14:en","key":{"work_id":14,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Victor Frankenstein creates a living being through a scientific experiment. His inabili