iptions","ref":"description:288:en","key":{"work_id":288,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Seven pilgrims travel towards Hyperion''s Time Tombs, guarded by the fearsome Shrike. As an invasion approaches, they share the stories that brought them to the pilgrimage.","work_id":288,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1963268W","fact":"Previously manually checked original English Work synopsis; reuse, not new writing or edition-language inference","checkedAt":"2026-10-29","sourceIsbn":"9780553283686"},{"fact":"Read-only reference; no code/PR cherry-pick","originCommit":"af6dd83fdeb83df7cae26ef94960ff4e355d15f7","originFileSha256":"44a0e3a15389f5904bacbe783ff9fd5b69e64e3a9a169ad424d089a72a403e7c"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1963268W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":185},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:304:en","key":{"work_id":304,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Fitz, the illegitimate son of a prince, grows up on the margins of the royal court. Secret training as an assassin draws him into its schemes while raiders threaten the kingdom.","work_id":304,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL2707183W","fact":"Previously manually checked original English Work synopsis; reuse, not new writing or edition-language inference","checkedAt":"2026-10-29","sourceIsbn":"9780553897487"},{"fact":"Read-only reference; no code/PR cherry-pick","originCommit":"af6dd83fdeb83df7cae26ef94960ff4e355d15f7","originFileSha256":"44a0e3a15389f5904bacbe783ff9fd5b69e64e3a9a169ad424d089a72a403e7c"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL2707183W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":191},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:4316:en","key":{"work_id":4316,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"A Security Unit overrides its governor and names itself Murderbot. It wants independence and time to watch serials, but encounters with caring humans complicate that plan.","work_id":4316,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17914663W","fact":"Previously manually checked original English Work synopsis; reuse, not new writing or edition-language inference","checkedAt":"2026-10-29","sourceIsbn":"9780765397539"},{"fact":"Read-only reference; no code/PR cherry-pick","originCommit":"af6dd83fdeb83df7cae26ef94960ff4e355d15f7","originFileSha256":"44a0e3a15389f5904bacbe783ff9fd5b69e64e3a9a169ad424d089a72a403e7c"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17914663W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":2243},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:7:en","key":{"work_id":7,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Frodo Baggins inherits a ring whose importance reaches far beyond his quiet life among the hobbits. Its former master, Sauron, is gathering power and wants it back. Destroying the ring requires a journey into the enemy''s own territory. Frodo must carry that responsibility while the struggle spreads across Middle-earth. This complete narrative brings together the journeys and conflicts published as The Fellowship of the Ring, The Two Towers and The Return of the King.","work_id":7,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27448W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Frodo inherits Bilbo''s One Ring; Sauron seeks it; destruction requires Mordor","Complete Work contains Fellowship,Two Towers,Return; not a new single series installment"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26885115M","isbn":"9780544003415","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL27448W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27448W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":6},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:48:en","key":{"work_id":48,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"A journalist facing the consequences of a libel conviction accepts an unusual investigation into a wealthy Swedish family. Harriet Vanger disappeared decades earlier, but her uncle has never stopped searching for an explanation. Mikael Blomkvist works with Lisbeth Salander, a researcher and hacker whose abilities challenge his assumptions. Their inquiries bring the family''s public standing into conflict with a much darker history. The disappearance becomes a way into questions of violence, secrecy and power.","work_id":48,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/98144/the-girl-with-the-dragon-tattoo-by-stieg-larsson/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Mikael libel conviction; Henrik Vanger hires him over Harriet''s decades-old disappearance","Lisbeth Salander researcher/hacker aids family investigation"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31","originalTitleReview":{"author":"Stieg Larsson","decision":"Independently read publisher English premise and monthly Swedish premise: same Mikael Blomkvist, Lisbeth Salander, Henrik Vanger and Harriet disappearance over forty years; exact English edition sole parent/ISBN/title checked separately. Existing Work retained, no merge, title change or new alias record.","evidence":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/98144/the-girl-with-the-dragon-tattoo-by-stieg-larsson/","workSource":"OL5784622W","sourceTitle":"Män som hatar kvinnor","englishTitle":"The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo"}},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL16819445M","isbn":"9780307269751","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL5784622W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/98144/the-girl-with-the-dragon-tattoo-by-stieg-larsson/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.penguinrandomhouse.com","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":40},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:65:en","key":{"work_id":65,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Claire Randall is visiting the Scottish Highlands with her husband after the Second World War when an encounter with ancient standing stones takes her into the eighteenth century. Her nursing experience cannot fully prepare her for the dangers of a society shaped by clan loyalties and conflict. Jamie Fraser offers a possible source of protection in this unfamiliar world. Claire must find a way to survive while the life she has left behind remains painfully present.","work_id":65,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL3261155W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Claire former combat nurse on1945Scottishhoneymoon; stones send her to1743","Clan conflicts and Jamie Fraser; displaced between familiar life and dangerous past"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL20130983M","isbn":"9780440212560","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL3261155W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL3261155W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":55},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:102:nl","key":{"work_id":102,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"In Panem houdt het Capitool de districten onder controle met een jaarlijks uitgezonden gevecht. Jongeren worden door loting aangewezen om deel te nemen aan de Hongerspelen, waarin overleven ten koste gaat van andere deelnemers. De zestienjarige Katniss Everdeen komt in die gewelddadige wedstrijd terecht. Haar keuzes worden niet alleen bepaald door lichamelijke dreiging, maar ook door een publiek dat meekijkt. Het verhaal verbindt persoonlijke overleving met de macht van het bestuur dat de spelen organiseert.","work_id":102,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5735363W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Katniss16inPanem; Capitol dominates12districts","Boys/girls12–18chosen bylottery for annualtelevisedbattle todeath"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL60075974M","isbn":"9789000399284","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL5735363W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5735363W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":89},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:102:en","key":{"work_id":102,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"The Capitol controls Panem''s districts through an annual spectacle in which young people are selected for a televised fight to the death. Sixteen-year-old Katniss Everdeen enters a contest designed to turn survival into entertainment for an audience. The immediate dangers of the arena exist alongside the political power behind the Games. What she does to stay alive is therefore never entirely private: every choice takes place within a system that wants the districts to remain obedient.","work_id":102,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5735363W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Katniss16inPanem; Capitol controls12districts","Annuallottery ofyoungparticipants for televisedfighttodeath"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL22549594M","isbn":"9780439023481","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL5735363W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5735363W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":89},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:114:en","key":{"work_id":114,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Kya Clark has learned to live largely alone in the marshes along the North Carolina coast. In nearby Barkley Cove, stories about the isolated girl have hardened into suspicion. When a young man is found dead, that reputation makes her an easy target for blame. The narrative connects the investigation with Kya''s upbringing and her attempts to form relationships. Her knowledge of the natural world stands beside the difficulty of finding a place among other people.","work_id":114,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18766691W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Kya survivesaloneinmarshnearBarkleyCoveNorthCarolina","ChaseAndrewsfounddead1969; locals suspecther; growingupandrelationships"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26702293M","isbn":"9780735219090","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL18766691W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18766691W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":99},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:121:en","key":{"work_id":121,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"The Seven Kingdoms are breaking into rival claims for power, and those seeking the Iron Throne prepare for conflict. Political bargains, family loyalties and military ambition pull people in different directions as disorder spreads. The struggle is not confined to the royal court: its consequences reach those who must travel, fight or disguise themselves to survive. This second volume of A Song of Ice and Fire follows a divided realm in which an apparent advantage can quickly become a danger.","work_id":121,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL257939W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["RivalfactionscontestIronThrone afterpoliticalupheaval","WarandplotsacrossSevenKingdoms; secondSongofIceandFirevolume"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL11761312M","isbn":"9781417663200","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL257939W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL257939W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":20},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:125:en","key":{"work_id":125,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Six-year-old Amy becomes the focus of a secret government experiment, and the agent sent to find her begins questioning his assignment. Brad Wolgast tries to protect the child as the project moves toward catastrophe. What follows reaches far beyond the people inside the experiment. The story carries Amy from a threatened childhood into a future transformed by violence, where the possibility of survival is bound to mysteries surrounding the girl herself.","work_id":125,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/33716/the-passage-tv-tie-in-edition-by-justin-cronin/paperback/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Amy6abandonedandheldbygovernmentexperiment; BradWolgasttriesprotecther","Experimentcatastrophe/socialcollapse; narrativefollowsAmyacrossdecades"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24349317M","isbn":"9780345504968","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL15168588W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/33716/the-passage-tv-tie-in-edition-by-justin-cronin/paperback/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.penguinrandomhouse.com","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":106},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:126:en","key":{"work_id":126,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"The great conflict in the Seven Kingdoms appears to be giving way to an uneasy pause, but its survivors are already competing over what remains. Cersei governs in King''s Landing while families and rivals attempt to secure their positions. Beyond the court, the damage of war continues to shape ordinary lives. New bargains grow out of old betrayals, and apparent peace offers little certainty. This volume follows the struggle to turn survival into lasting power.","work_id":126,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL257948W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Uneasyaftermathwar; CerseiregentKingsLanding; survivorsandoutlawsseekadvantage","FourthASOIAFvolume; scatteredfamilies/newalliances; noendingclaims"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL22236422M","isbn":"9780553582024","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL257948W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL257948W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":20},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:138:en","key":{"work_id":138,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Frodo and Sam continue their journey after the companions of the Ring have been separated. Destroying the Ring remains their task, but travelling without the others leaves them exposed to new dangers and to a figure following their movements. The wider struggle in Middle-earth continues around the broken company. This middle part of The Lord of the Rings follows a quest in which friendship and determination must endure without the reassurance of staying together.","work_id":138,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27479W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["FrodoSamseparatedfromcompanionscontinueRingquest","Mysteriousfollower; secondpartofLordRings; sourcealsocontainedinwholeomnibus"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL34091192M","isbn":"9781484490334","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL27479W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27479W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":6},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:151:en","key":{"work_id":151,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Gideon wants to escape the Ninth House rather than spend her life serving its necromancer. Harrowhark, her hostile childhood companion, needs a skilled sword fighter for an invitation from the Emperor. The opportunity promises extraordinary power, but it demands that the two work together in a dangerous trial involving the other Houses. Gideon''s departure is postponed by a bargain that entangles her in rivalries where swordsmanship and necromancy may not be enough to keep either woman safe.","work_id":151,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20128158W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["GideonwantsleaveNinthHouse; Harrowneedsherascavalier","EmperorinvitesHouseheirstodeadlytrial; necromancerrequirespartnerforpromisedimmortality"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27308126M","isbn":"9781250313195","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL20128158W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20128158W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":122},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:166:en","key":{"work_id":166,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Bryce Quinlan and Hunt Athalar want some space to rebuild their lives, but the struggle against the Asteri is drawing closer. Rebel activity makes the rulers'' promises of leaving them alone increasingly uncertain. As friends become entangled in the resistance, avoiding involvement becomes a decision with consequences of its own. The second Crescent City novel follows their attempt to choose a future while loyalty, oppression and the dangers of opposing those in power leave little room for neutrality.","work_id":166,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL21101115W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["BryceandHuntseeknormality; Asterileavethemuntroubledinitially","RebelsopposeAsteri; friendsdrawnin; choicebetweenquietandresistance"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32388161M","isbn":"9781635574074","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL21101115W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL21101115W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":125},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:178:en","key":{"work_id":178,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Lyra reaches a world where the familiar boundaries between places have begun to break down. There she encounters Will Parry, who is trying to find his father while escaping dangers of his own. Their paths become connected with a knife capable of extraordinary things. In the haunted city of Cittàgazze and beyond, they must work out whom to trust. Their search draws them toward a conflict that extends across more than one world.","work_id":178,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28993W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["LyraWillmeetCittagazze hauntedbySpectres","Willsearchesfather; powerfulknife anddissolvingworldboundaries"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL10953480M","isbn":"9780613722551","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL28993W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28993W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":120},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:180:en","key":{"work_id":180,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Carrie White is isolated both at school and at home, where her mother''s severe religious beliefs leave little room for an ordinary adolescence. As other pupils torment her, Carrie begins discovering an ability to move things without touching them. Her hope of being accepted grows alongside a power she does not fully understand. The approach of the senior prom brings those pressures together, turning the desire to fit in into a situation with potentially devastating consequences.","work_id":180,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL81626W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["CarrieWhitehighschooloutsider; domineeringreligiousmother; peerbullying","Discoverstelekineticpowers; confrontationaroundprom"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL9787395M","isbn":"9780816156887","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL81626W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL81626W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":49},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:189:en","key":{"work_id":189,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"In the trading city of Ketterdam, Kaz Brekker is offered a criminal job whose rewards are matched by its dangers. He needs a crew with very different skills, bringing together people shaped by imprisonment, magic, privileged beginnings and life on the streets. Their chances depend on cooperation, but their private histories make trust difficult. The heist forces six outsiders to rely on one another while the consequences of failure reach beyond their own ambitions.","work_id":189,"evidence":[{"url":"https://us.macmillan.com/books/9781627792127/sixofcrows/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["KazBrekkerinKetterdamrecruitscrewforspecialheist","Sixoutcastsincludeconvict,sharpshooter,runaway,spy,Heartrender,thief; trustconflicts"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL25908319M","isbn":"9781627792127","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL17332479W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://us.macmillan.com/books/9781627792127/sixofcrows/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"us.macmillan.com","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":142},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1220:nl","key":{"work_id":1220,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Een gezinsvakantie in Turkije eindigt voor Chantal en Jeroen in een ramp wanneer hun tweeling verdrinkt. Na terugkeer proberen zij op verschillende manieren met het verlies om te gaan. Jeroen wordt verteerd door schuldgevoel, terwijl Chantal houvast zoekt voor hun gezamenlijke leven. Dan krijgt zij informatie die twijfel oproept over de oorzaak van de dood van hun kinderen. Haar zoektocht voert terug naar een vakantieomgeving die veel minder zorgeloos blijkt dan de belofte van het hotel.","work_id":1220,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24452795W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["JeroenChantalvand erSchaaf twinsMaxDennidrownonTurkeyallinclusiveholiday","Guiltstrainscouple; Chantalhearstragedynotordinaryaccident; hotelpracticesinvestigation"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28313071M","isbn":"9789022996072","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL24452795W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24452795W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1222:nl","key":{"work_id":1222,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Koen en Isabel regelen tijdens de zomervakantie een kamp voor hun dochter Bibi, omdat zij nog niet samen op reis kunnen. De dagelijkse telefoongesprekken geven hun aanvankelijk het gevoel dat alles goed gaat. Dat verandert wanneer Bibi wordt vermist en een zoekactie geen antwoord oplevert. Voor Isabel krijgt de verdwijning vervolgens een persoonlijke dreiging. De vertrouwde planning van een gezin maakt plaats voor onzekerheid over waar hun kind is en wat er van haar moeder wordt verlangd.","work_id":1222,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL34868142W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["KoenIsabelsendBibi tosummercamponfriendadvicebridgingchildcareweek","Bibi disappearsdespitedailycalls; searchunsuccessful; kidnappingdemandsfromIsabel"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32157294M","isbn":"9789022994153","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL34868142W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL34868142W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1361:nl","key":{"work_id":1361,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Jude groeit met haar zussen op aan een elfenhof nadat zij als kind uit haar mensenwereld is weggerukt. Zij wil een plaats veroveren tussen wezens die haar vanwege haar sterfelijkheid verachten. Prins Cardan maakt dat verlangen bijzonder moeilijk. Wanneer Jude verder in de intriges van het hof betrokken raakt, moet zij bepalen welke middelen zij zelf bereid is te gebruiken. De strijd om erbij te horen verandert zo in een gevaarlijk spel rond macht en familie.","work_id":1361,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17850410W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["JudehumanraisedinFaerieafterparentskilled; wantsbelong; Cardanhostile","Courtintrigue,potentialviolenceanddangerousalliancetoprotectsisters"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28002476M","isbn":"9789022589571","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL17850410W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17850410W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":729},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1379:nl","key":{"work_id":1379,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Scarlett droomt ervan Caraval te bezoeken, een voorstelling waarbij het publiek zelf aan een spel deelneemt. Haar vader heeft ondertussen een huwelijk voor haar geregeld. Wanneer een uitnodiging toch een reis mogelijk maakt, vertrekt zij met haar zus Tella. Bij aankomst verdwijnt Tella en blijkt de zoektocht naar haar het middelpunt van de wedstrijd. Scarlett moet ontdekken hoe zij kan spelen in een wereld die haar voortdurend waarschuwt dat niets helemaal echt hoeft te zijn.","work_id":1379,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17715454W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Scarlett/Tellalivewithcruelfather; arrangedmarriage andlongawaitedCaravalinvitation","TellakidnappedbyorganizerLegend; findinghergamegoal withinfivenights"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL41564829M","isbn":"9789021028644","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL17715454W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17715454W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":735},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1381:nl","key":{"work_id":1381,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"De dieren van een boerderij komen in opstand tegen de boer die hen verwaarloost. Onder leiding van de varkens proberen zij het werk en de opbrengsten voortaan eerlijker te verdelen. Hun nieuwe samenleving begint met de belofte dat de vroegere ongelijkheid zal verdwijnen. Gaandeweg ontstaat echter verschil tussen wat de leiders verkondigen en wat zij zelf doen. De fabel volgt hoe een gezamenlijk ideaal onder druk komt te staan wanneer enkelen steeds meer macht krijgen.","work_id":1381,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1168007W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["AnimalsrebelagainstneglectfulMrJones; pigsNapoleon/Snowballlead","Idealofequalityaftertakeover becomescorrupted"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL18430168M","isbn":"9789041330369","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL1168007W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1168007W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":2},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1383:nl","key":{"work_id":1383,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Evangeline Fox wil verhinderen dat de jongen van wie zij houdt met iemand anders trouwt. Om de bruiloft tegen te houden, vraagt zij hulp aan de Hartenprins. Zijn prijs lijkt overzichtelijk: drie kussen, op momenten en plaatsen die hij zal aanwijzen. Maar een afspraak met een onsterfelijke laat zich niet gemakkelijk begrenzen. Terwijl Evangeline probeert haar gewenste gelukkige einde te bereiken, moet zij ontdekken welke verwachtingen de prins zelf aan hun overeenkomst heeft verbonden.","work_id":1383,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24706481W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Evangelinewantstopbelovedwedding; bargainswithPrinceofHearts","Pricethreekissesathischosentimes/places; immortalhasfurtherplans"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL60479668M","isbn":"9789049206925","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL24706481W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24706481W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":735},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1407:nl","key":{"work_id":1407,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"In een reeks verbonden verhalen onderzoekt Isaac Asimov hoe mensen en robots met elkaar omgaan. Een journalist luistert naar de ervaringen van robotpsycholoog Susan Calvin, die terugblikt op gebeurtenissen uit de ontwikkeling van de robotica. De afzonderlijke situaties stellen telkens andere vragen over gedrag, verantwoordelijkheid en de verwachtingen die mensen van hun machines hebben. Samen vormen de verhalen een geschiedenis van een technologie waarvan de maatschappelijke betekenis niet losstaat van menselijke keuzes.","work_id":1407,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL46241W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["CollectionofshortstoriesframedbySusanCalvintalkingtojournalist","Interactionhumansrobotsmorality; combinedfictionalhistoryofrobotics; notnewnovella/mainseriesinstallment"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27317563M","isbn":"9789031502004","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL46241W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL46241W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":14},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1411:nl","key":{"work_id":1411,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"In het dorp King''s Abbot wordt de rijke Roger Ackroyd vermoord, kort na de dood van een weduwe over wie al geruchten rondgaan. Zijn huishouden biedt de politie verschillende mogelijke verdachten en motieven. Hercule Poirot, die juist een rustiger bestaan op het platteland heeft gezocht, raakt bij het onderzoek betrokken. Samen met de plaatselijke dokter Sheppard kijkt hij naar wat de bewoners vertellen en verzwijgen. Niet iedere overtuigende verklaring blijkt daarmee ook een betrouwbare aanwijzing.","work_id":1411,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL471932W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["RogerAckroydmurderedinstudyafterMrsFerrarsdeath; householdsuspects","PoirotretiredinKingsAbbot; DrSheppardnarrativeconnection; doNOTdisclosekillerorending"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL47779885M","isbn":"9789024511624","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL471932W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL471932W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":45},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1842:nl","key":{"work_id":1842,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"In een toekomstig Amerika onder een militair en totalitair bewind vindt ieder jaar een uitputtende wandelwedstrijd plaats. De deelnemers moeten blijven doorgaan terwijl de lichamelijke en psychische druk oploopt. Wat als een afgebakende competitie begint, maakt steeds sterker zichtbaar hoeveel macht de organisatoren over hun levens hebben. Stephen King schreef deze dystopische roman onder de naam Richard Bachman. De wedstrijd vormt het uitgangspunt voor een verhaal over uithoudingsvermogen en een samenleving die mensen aan extreme eisen onderwerpt.","work_id":1842,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL9973101W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["FuturetotalitarianmilitaristicAmerica; gruelingannualwalkingcompetition","OriginallyStephenKingasRichardBachman; noendingsorrulesnotinsourceinvented"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27280342M","isbn":"9789024536771","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL9973101W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL9973101W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":49},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:48:nl","key":{"work_id":48,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Journalist Mikael Blomkvist neemt een oud onderzoek naar de verdwijning van Harriet Vanger op zich. Haar familie behoort tot de machtigste van Zweden, maar heeft nooit kunnen verklaren wat er met haar is gebeurd. Voor zijn speurwerk krijgt hij hulp van Lisbeth Salander, een eigenzinnige onderzoeker met grote technische vaardigheden. Samen zoeken zij achter de verhalen die de familie over zichzelf vertelt. Hun samenwerking legt verbanden bloot tussen een verdwenen meisje, verborgen geweld en de bescherming van reputaties.","work_id":48,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/stieg-larsson/mannen-die-vrouwen-haten-millennium/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Mikael investigates Harriet Vanger disappearance40yearsearlier atHenrikVangerrequest","LisbethSalanderhackerhelps uncoverfamilyhistory"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31","originalTitleReview":{"author":"Stieg Larsson","decision":"Exact Dutch libraryISBN record explicitly identifies Swedish original; publisher English and Dutch premises match the existing Work. No Work merge or bibliography rewrite.","evidence":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/stieg-larsson/mannen-die-vrouwen-haten-millennium/","workSource":"OL5784622W","sourceTitle":"Män som hatar kvinnor","englishTitle":"The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo"}},{"url":"https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.439296358.html/mannen-die-vrouwen-haten/","isbn":"9789056727659","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","facts":["Dutch printed Signatuur2023; translatedfromSwedishMänsomhatarkvinnor2005, TinekeJorissenWedzinga"],"title":"Mannen die vrouwen haten","author":"Stieg Larsson","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/stieg-larsson/mannen-die-vrouwen-haten-millennium/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":40},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:65:nl","key":{"work_id":65,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Claire Randall reist in 1945 met haar man naar de Schotse Hooglanden om na de oorlog weer tijd samen door te brengen. Een bezoek aan een oude stenencirkel brengt haar onverwacht in het Schotland van 1743. Daar moet zij haar weg vinden tussen gewelddadige conflicten en verplichtingen die zij niet kent. Haar ontmoeting met Jamie Fraser geeft haar leven een nieuwe richting. Tegelijk blijft de vraag hoe dit bestaan zich verhoudt tot de wereld die zij heeft achtergelaten.","work_id":65,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.lannoo.com/nl-be/literatuur-romans/de-reiziger-9789022574492","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Claireon1945honeymoonwithFrank; stonestransportto1743Scotland","JamieFraserandconflictbetweenlivesandrelationships"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://www.lannoo.com/nl-be/literatuur-romans/de-reiziger-9789022574492","isbn":"9789022574492","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","facts":["ExactEAN9789022574492,Dutch,paperbackBoekerij2015; Outlandercorrespondenceidentified"],"title":"De reiziger","author":"Diana Gabaldon","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.lannoo.com/nl-be/literatuur-romans/de-reiziger-9789022574492","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.lannoo.com","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":55},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:114:nl","key":{"work_id":114,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Kya Clark groeit grotendeels alleen op tussen de moerassen van North Carolina. Ze leert zichzelf te redden met de natuur als vertrouwde omgeving, terwijl de inwoners van het nabije stadje vooral verhalen over haar verspreiden. Nieuwe ontmoetingen brengen liefde en de mogelijkheid van een minder afgezonderd leven. Wanneer een jonge man dood wordt gevonden, keert de verdenking zich echter tegen haar. Het onderzoek loopt door een verhaal over opgroeien, buitensluiting en de zoektocht naar verbondenheid.","work_id":114,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.rainbow.nl/boek/3146/delia-owens-daar-waar-de-rivierkreeften-zingen.html","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["KyaClarkaloneinNorthCarolinamarsh; relationshipswithtwoyoungmen","Onefounddead; locals suspectisolatedgirl"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p443434182","isbn":"9789041716149","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","facts":["Cached exactCC0libraryrowISBN/title/author/languagenl; publisher confirms samepaperbackISBNandstory"],"title":"Daar waar de rivierkreeften zingen","author":"Delia Owens","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.rainbow.nl/boek/3146/delia-owens-daar-waar-de-rivierkreeften-zingen.html","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.rainbow.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":99},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1361:en","key":{"work_id":1361,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Jude has grown up among the faerie nobility since being taken from the human world as a child. She wants a place at court despite the contempt directed at mortals, especially by Prince Cardan. Proving herself draws her into political schemes where belonging and safety are not the same thing. As rivalries threaten her sisters, Jude must decide how far she is willing to go to gain influence in a society that was never meant to welcome her.","work_id":1361,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17850410W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["MortalJudegrowsupFaerie; Cardanhostile; seeksplaceatcourt","Intrigueanddangerousalliancesprotectingsisters"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26435884M","isbn":"9780316310277","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL17850410W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17850410W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":729},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1379:en","key":{"work_id":1379,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Scarlett''s chance to visit Caraval arrives just as an arranged marriage seems to close off the life she wants. She escapes her island with her sister Tella to attend a performance in which the audience participates. Once there, Scarlett discovers that Tella''s disappearance has become the central challenge. Finding her means entering a contest whose appearances cannot be trusted. The promise that it is only a game offers little comfort when her sister''s future seems to depend on winning.","work_id":1379,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17715454W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Scarlettarrangedmarriage; sisterTellatakeshertoCaraval","Tella''sabductionbecomesgamegoal; apparentperformancewithstakes"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26883152M","isbn":"9781250095251","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL17715454W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17715454W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":735},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1381:en","key":{"work_id":1381,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"The animals on a neglected farm drive out their owner and attempt to organise life on their own terms. Led by the pigs, they begin with an ideal of fairness and shared benefit. As their new society develops, the distance between its promises and its practices grows. Some animals acquire privileges that others do not share. Orwell''s fable follows the transformation of a rebellion through the ordinary work, rules and rivalries of the farm.","work_id":1381,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1168007W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["RebellionagainstneglectfulMrJonesledbypigs","Promiseequalitycorruptedaspowerandprivilegesgrow"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL7577246M","isbn":"9780451526342","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL1168007W","editionTitleReview":{"url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouseretail.com/book/?isbn=9780451526342","isbn":"9780451526342","title":"Animal Farm","decision":"Exact publisherISBN page names Animal Farm by George Orwell, Signet mass-market paperback. Provider adds imprint in parentheses; sole parent and exact ISBN match. Retain existing controlled title and Work; no provider-driven overwrite.","editionId":"OL7577246M","sourceTitle":"Animal Farm (Signet Classics)"}}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1168007W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":2},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1383:en","key":{"work_id":1383,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Evangeline Fox hopes to prevent the man she loves from marrying someone else. She turns to the Prince of Hearts and accepts a bargain: his help in return for three kisses, given when and where he chooses. What seems a way to recover her happy ending soon leaves her facing another person''s ambitions. Dealing with an immortal makes the limits of that agreement difficult to see, and each promised payment carries implications she did not anticipate.","work_id":1383,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24706481W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["EvangelinebargainswithPrinceofHeartstostopwedding","Threekissesatimmortal''schosentimes; hisplansgobeyondherexpectations"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32794390M","isbn":"9781250268396","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL24706481W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24706481W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":735},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1407:en","key":{"work_id":1407,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"A reporter listens as robot psychologist Susan Calvin recalls incidents from the development of robotics. The linked stories consider the ways people interpret machines and the difficulties that arise when expectations meet unfamiliar behaviour. Different situations place responsibility, judgment and the relationship between humans and robots under pressure. Read together, the accounts build a fictional history of a technology whose significance depends as much on the people around it as on its own capabilities.","work_id":1407,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL46241W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["LinkedstoriesframedbySusanCalvin''sconversationwithreporter","Humanrobotinteractionandmorality; fictionalroboticshistory"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL22744922M","isbn":"9780553803709","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL46241W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL46241W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":14},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1411:en","key":{"work_id":1411,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Hercule Poirot''s quiet retirement in King''s Abbot is interrupted when the wealthy Roger Ackroyd is found murdered. The death follows that of a local widow, and rumours already connect the people around them. Doctor Sheppard becomes involved as the detective examines a household full of possible motives. What residents choose to say can be as important as what they know. The investigation asks how an apparently familiar village can conceal events that its neighbours have failed to understand.","work_id":1411,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL471932W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["PoirotretirementKingsAbbot; AckroydmurderafterMrsFerrarsdeath","DrSheppardandhouseholdsuspects; nosolutionrevealed"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL7889384M","isbn":"9780735105850","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL471932W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL471932W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":45},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1842:en","key":{"work_id":1842,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"In a future America controlled by a military dictatorship, an annual walking competition pushes its participants toward their physical limits. Continuing the contest becomes harder as exhaustion and psychological pressure accumulate. The event places individual endurance inside a system defined by obedience and state power. First published under Stephen King''s Richard Bachman pseudonym, the novel uses the demands of the walk to examine a society willing to make extreme suffering part of an organised public competition.","work_id":1842,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL9973101W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["FuturetotalitarianmilitaryAmerica; exhaustingannualwalkingcontest","StephenKingasRichardBachman; noinventedparticipantnamesorending"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL7588073M","isbn":"9780613173506","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL9973101W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL9973101W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":49},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1221:nl","key":{"work_id":1221,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Stewardess Dagmar ziet haar vertrouwde leven instorten wanneer haar relatie met Ruben eindigt. Zijn leugens raken vervolgens zowel haar vriendschappen als haar werk. Daar komt het bericht bij dat Marianne, een vriendin die op Mallorca werkt, is vermoord. Dagmar reist naar het eiland om zelf naar antwoorden te zoeken. Achter de vakantieomgeving blijken belangen te schuilen die haar zoektocht naar de waarheid gevaarlijk maken.","work_id":1221,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/de-vlucht/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Dagmar Vredeling stewardess; Ruben ontrouw en verspreidt leugens met gevolgen voor werk/vrienden","Vriendin Marianne reisleidster op Mallorca vermoord; Dagmar onderzoekt dood en criminele belangen"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28120995M","isbn":"9789400507517","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL20778158W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/de-vlucht/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1224:nl","key":{"work_id":1224,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Na het einde van haar relatie woont Manon weer bij haar ouders, die weinig vertrouwen hebben in de keuzes van hun dochter. Een gezinsvakantie in Oostenrijk geeft haar onverwacht een nieuwe richting. Wanneer zij op de piste een kind te hulp schiet, biedt een skischool haar werk aan. Wat een kans op zelfstandigheid lijkt, wordt ondermijnd door verontrustende incidenten rond haar nieuwe baan.","work_id":1224,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/apres-ski/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Manon23 na verbroken relatie thuis; familie Dijkstra op traditionele skivakantie Oostenrijk","Redding kind na snowboardincident leidt tot baan skischool; opeenvolgende incidenten"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26221239M","isbn":"9789022994801","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL17616820W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/apres-ski/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1225:nl","key":{"work_id":1225,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Joyce heeft op Tenerife een goedlopend hotel opgebouwd. Na een overval wordt ze wakker zonder te weten wat haar de vorige avond is overkomen. Een onbekende beweert daar wel bewijs van te hebben en gebruikt die kennis om haar onder druk te zetten. Hij eist de beschikking over een hotelsuite. Joyce moet omgaan met een dreiging die binnendringt in zowel haar werk als haar privéleven.","work_id":1225,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/de-suite/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Joyce runt hotel Tenerife, wordt overvallen en bedwelmd, geheugenverlies voorafgaande avond","Man chanteert haar met bewijs en eist suite volledig tot zijn beschikking"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27676076M","isbn":"9789022999103","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL20451450W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/de-suite/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1229:nl","key":{"work_id":1229,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Kim viert haar dertigste verjaardag met een reis door Noorwegen en hoopt daar ook duidelijkheid over haar toekomst met Brian te krijgen. De vrienden die meegaan brengen echter hun eigen spanningen mee. Ook de gidsen van twee reisgezelschappen lijken iets tegen elkaar te hebben. Wanneer de verjaardagsnacht een dodelijke afloop krijgt, verandert de tocht in een situatie waarin Kim niet meer weet op wie zij kan rekenen.","work_id":1229,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/noorderlicht/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Kim Romeijn30 wil Brian op Noorwegenrondreis ten huwelijk vragen; broer Eric wantrouwt hem","Vijf uitgenodigden onderlinge spanningen; gidsen vijandig; nacht na verjaardag overleeft niet iedereen"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL31888299M","isbn":"9789400502000","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL34826276W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/noorderlicht/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1230:nl","key":{"work_id":1230,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Sara bezoekt met haar nieuwe vriend de bed and breakfast die haar jeugdvriendin Annelies en haar man Wim op IJsland zijn begonnen. Het echtpaar wilde daar na huwelijksproblemen opnieuw beginnen. Tijdens het bezoek merkt Sara dat de spanningen niet verdwenen zijn. Vreemde gebeurtenissen verstoren het samenzijn en een kamermeisje raakt vermist. Het weerzien krijgt daardoor een andere betekenis dan de ontspannen vakantie waarop Sara had gehoopt.","work_id":1230,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/het-chalet/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Annelies en Wim na kinderloosheid en ontrouw naar IJsland voor B&B","Jeugdvriendin Sara op bezoek met nieuwe vriend; huwelijk gespannen, vreemde gebeurtenissen, kamermeisje verdwijnt"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL45729435M","isbn":"9789400503427","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL33760020W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/het-chalet/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1235:nl","key":{"work_id":1235,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Zes vriendinnen uit hun Leidse studententijd houden hun band in stand met gezamenlijke wintersportreizen. Na de dood van Daphne beloven de overgebleven vrouwen voor elkaar te blijven zorgen. Een later ongeluk brengt die verbondenheid opnieuw op de proef. Er zijn omstandigheden die niet passen bij een eenvoudige verklaring. Twijfel aan wat er werkelijk is gebeurd zet de verhoudingen binnen de hechte groep onder druk.","work_id":1235,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/sneeuwengelen/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Zes Leidse studievriendinnen jaarlijkse wintersport, noemen zich sneeuwengelen","Daphne overlijdt; zorgpact; later ongeluk met ongerijmdheden tast vertrouwen aan"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28120994M","isbn":"9789400506374","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL20778157W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/sneeuwengelen/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1236:nl","key":{"work_id":1236,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Een filmopname trekt in een hete Portugese zomer de aandacht van Anoek en haar vriendin Cesária. De bedrijvigheid in de Algarve krijgt een andere lading wanneer bij een klif een dode wordt gevonden. Inspecteur Gabriela Carvalho onderzoekt wie verantwoordelijk is. Een van de mensen die daarbij in beeld komen blijkt ook kennis te hebben van een eerdere verdwijning. Zo raken de nieuwe zaak en een oud mysterie met elkaar verweven.","work_id":1236,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/hittegolf/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Algarve hittegolf, Anoek Huizing en Cesária volgen Hollywoodfilmopnames","Lichaam bij klif geen natuurlijke dood; Gabriela Carvalho onderzoekt; verdachte kent zaak verdwenen meisje zeven jaar eerder"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32464319M","isbn":"9789400507135","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL24500050W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/hittegolf/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1237:nl","key":{"work_id":1237,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Een opvallende gewonnen rechtszaak maakt Chantal bekend buiten haar werk als strafrechtadvocaat, maar brengt ook ongewenste aandacht van een stalker. Ze plant met haar vriend een skireis om afstand te nemen. Kort voor vertrek verschijnt Fenna aan haar deur. Het meisje zegt dat zij de dochter is van Chantals zus, met wie het contact al jaren verbroken is. Haar onverwachte komst maakt ontsnappen aan de onrust ingewikkelder.","work_id":1237,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/lawinegevaar/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Chantal Donkers strafrechtadvocaat media-aandacht na winst, stalker, geplande Zwitserlandreis met Niels","Fenna arriveert week voor vertrek, stelt dochter zus Amber te zijn; zussen tien jaar geen contact"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL45730536M","isbn":"9789400507692","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL33760983W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/lawinegevaar/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1238:nl","key":{"work_id":1238,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Liza krijgt geen contact meer met haar zoon Mark tijdens zijn vakantie op Corfu. Zijn vriend vertelt dat Mark is doorgereisd met een meisje, Thera, maar van beiden ontbreekt daarna een spoor. Liza legt zich niet neer bij de geruststellende verklaringen uit haar omgeving en reist zelf naar Griekenland. Haar onderzoek brengt haar naar Kefalonia, waar informatie over haar zoon verbonden raakt met vragen over haar eigen verleden.","work_id":1238,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/het-paradijs/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Mark op Corfu, vriend Fedde meldt backpacken met Thera; beiden onbereikbaar","Moeder Liza Roozenboom zoekt zelf; naar Kefalonia; oudere man kent Mark en haar verleden"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL42067271M","isbn":"9789400512368","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL30599005W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/het-paradijs/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1240:nl","key":{"work_id":1240,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Johanna verdwijnt als zestienjarige tijdens de nieuwjaarsnacht van 1993. Vijfentwintig jaar later pakt een coldcaseteam de zaak opnieuw op. Niet iedereen in de familie is daar blij mee, maar haar nicht Olivia wil weten wat er met haar tante is gebeurd. Ze begint een eigen zoektocht die haar naar Denemarken en Groenland voert. Het onderzoek brengt niet alleen verborgen familievragen naar boven, maar ook gevaar voor Olivia zelf.","work_id":1240,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/ijskoud/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Johanna van Vliet16 verdwijnt nieuwjaarsnacht1993; Ben de Groot heropent25jaar later","Nicht Olivia onderzoekt tegen terughoudendheid vader/broer in; sporen Denemarken en Groenland; haar leven bedreigd"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32241487M","isbn":"9789400510067","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL24348751W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/ijskoud/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1241:nl","key":{"work_id":1241,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Karin hoort op haar vijfendertigste dat zij als kind is geadopteerd. Omdat haar biologische vader ernstig ziek is, reist ze met haar zoontje Sam naar Ottawa. De kennismaking met haar familie wordt overschaduwd door de verdwijning van een jong meisje. Karin raakt bij die zaak betrokken terwijl ze haar eigen achtergrond probeert te begrijpen. Als daarna meer kinderen verdwijnen, wordt de onrust in haar nieuwe omgeving steeds groter.","work_id":1241,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/winternacht/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Psychologe Karin ter Duin35 ontdekt adoptie, biologische vader stervend, met dove zoon Sam Ottawa","Liv Tremblay5 verdwijnt natuurpark; Karin betrokken; meer kinderen vermist"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26953535M","isbn":"9789400508422","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL19740461W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/winternacht/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1242:nl","key":{"work_id":1242,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Schrijfster Gemma heeft al lange tijd geen contact meer met twee voormalige vriendinnen. Een stalker en verontrustende gebeurtenissen maken het onmogelijk de oude afspraken nog te negeren. De vrouwen vermoeden wie hen lastigvalt, maar juist dat vermoeden lijkt onverklaarbaar. Ze zoeken elkaar weer op in Sardinië, waar Gemma aan een boek werkt. Daar moeten ze zich opnieuw verhouden tot het geheim dat hen ooit van elkaar verwijderde.","work_id":1242,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/het-strandhuis/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Bestsellerauteur Gemma Kastelijn en vroegere vriendinnen contact volledig verbroken","Lichaam, stem verleden, stalking; vermoede identiteit onmogelijk; bijeenkomst Sardinië gezamenlijke geheim"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL32224212M","isbn":"9789400510074","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL24341736W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/het-strandhuis/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1243:nl","key":{"work_id":1243,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Paula en Theo maken eindelijk de camperreis langs de Amerikaanse westkust waar zij lang naar hebben uitgekeken. Een ontmoeting in Las Vegas met iemand uit Paula''s verleden verstoort hun vakantie. Vervolgens verdwijnt Theo zonder verklaring. Paula probeert te achterhalen wat hem is overkomen, terwijl de vondst van een vermoorde man de situatie nog dreigender maakt. De gezamenlijke reis verandert in een zoektocht waarin haar vertrouwde leven geen houvast meer biedt.","work_id":1243,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/roadtrip/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Paula Visser en man Theo droomreis camper Amerikaanse westkust","Las Vegas ontmoeting Paula verleden; Theo verdwijnt dagen later; vermoorde man gevonden"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL37844978M","isbn":"9789400514492","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL27730112W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/roadtrip/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1244:nl","key":{"work_id":1244,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Bo en Inès volgen voor een podcast de reis van een journalistiekstudente die jaren eerder verdween. Hun tocht voert per trein richting Parijs en Bordeaux. De vriendinnen verschillen steeds meer van mening over de manier waarop zij het onderzoek moeten aanpakken. Na een ruzie gaat Bo alleen verder. Wanneer ze opnieuw contact zoekt en Inès onbereikbaar blijkt, komt het oude verdwijningsverhaal plotseling veel dichter bij haar eigen leven.","work_id":1244,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/spoorloos/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Bo en Inès podcast verdwenen journalistiekstudent Julia van der Molen; trein Parijs/Bordeaux","Bo voorzichtig, Inès minder serieus; ruzie; Bo verder alleen; Inès vervolgens onbereikbaar"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL58385964M","isbn":"9789400517523","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL42854974W"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/spoorloos/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:157:en","key":{"work_id":157,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"A new series of killings forces Bryce Quinlan to revisit the loss of her closest friends. The suspect in their deaths has already been imprisoned, so the renewed violence raises questions about the original investigation. Hunt Athalar, an enslaved fallen angel, is offered a chance at freedom if he helps her find the killer. Their search takes them through Crescent City''s hidden power struggles while grief and attraction complicate their uneasy partnership.","work_id":157,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.bloomsbury.com/us/house-of-earth-and-blood-9781635574043/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Bryce''s friends killed by demon; crimes resume after suspect imprisoned","Enslaved fallen angel Hunt offered freedom for helping investigation; hidden dangerous power in Crescent City"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27924119M","isbn":"9781635574043","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL20650912W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.bloomsbury.com/us/house-of-earth-and-blood-9781635574043/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.bloomsbury.com","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":125},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:199:en","key":{"work_id":199,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Three women describe life in and around Gilead more than fifteen years after Offred''s story. Agnes has grown up within the regime, while Daisy must confront unexpected information about her own background. Aunt Lydia offers the perspective of someone who has helped maintain its institutions. Their accounts approach the same society from very different positions, revealing the gap between its public rules and the choices people make to survive under them.","work_id":199,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20129837W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Three narrators Agnes,Daisy,Lydia; more than fifteen years after Offred''s ending","Agnes inside Gilead,Daisy discovers identity,Lydia reflects on choices within regime"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27306829M","isbn":"9780385543781","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL20129837W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20129837W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":8},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:208:en","key":{"work_id":208,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Lauren Olamina grows up behind protective walls near Los Angeles as the society outside struggles with violence and scarce resources. Her unusual sensitivity to other people''s suffering makes that instability especially difficult to bear. When her community is destroyed, she has to travel north with other displaced people. The journey tests practical ways of staying alive while Lauren begins developing a set of beliefs about change and the possibility of a different future.","work_id":208,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL35623W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Lauren Olamina defended enclave near Los Angeles; water shortages,violence,social collapse","Hyperempathy; compound destroyed; northward refugees'' journey and developing new belief"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27288938M","isbn":"9781609807191","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL35623W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL35623W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":127},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:222:en","key":{"work_id":222,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Surviving her first year at Basgiath does not make Violet Sorrengail''s training safer. A new vice commandant turns the demands placed on dragon riders into a more personal struggle, using her loyalties against her. Violet must rely on intelligence and determination as physical endurance alone proves insufficient. Knowledge of what the college conceals also changes the meaning of obedience. Continuing her education now means deciding which rules protect people and which preserve dangerous secrets.","work_id":222,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL34028551W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Violet survived first year; harsher training and new vice commandant targeting her","Loyalty to loved man used against her; hidden Basgiath secret; physical frailty versus intelligence"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL46066228M","isbn":"9780349437026","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL34028551W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL34028551W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":152},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:226:en","key":{"work_id":226,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"With open conflict replacing the relative structure of her training, Violet Sorrengail must look beyond the failing wards around Aretia. She travels into unfamiliar territories to seek help for Navarre, uncertain which potential allies deserve her trust. The mission puts her dragons, family and closest relationships at risk. Finding the strength to resist the enemy requires more than an army: Violet also needs answers to questions others would prefer to keep hidden.","work_id":226,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL41943074W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Violet after nearly eighteen months Basgiath; enemies within and outside","Journey beyond failing Aretian wards for allies supporting Navarre; dragons,family,truth and secrecy"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL57528701M","isbn":"9780349437064","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL41943074W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL41943074W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":152},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:232:en","key":{"work_id":232,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Darrow works beneath Mars believing that his caste''s sacrifices will make the planet habitable for later generations. Discovering that an established society already flourishes above ground exposes the lie sustaining that labour. He sets out to enter the world of the ruling Golds and challenge it from within. At their Institute, competition is violent and alliances uncertain. Fighting the system means learning how its future leaders are trained without losing sight of those left below.","work_id":232,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17076473W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Darrow Red lowest caste mining Mars; habitable surface and ruling cities already exist","Infiltration of Gold Institute; dangerous competition for power motivated by justice and loss"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26456624M","isbn":"9780345539786","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL17076473W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17076473W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":157},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:239:en","key":{"work_id":239,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Harrowhark Nonagesimus has entered the Emperor''s service, but the transformation expected of her is proving unstable. Training alongside a rival and under unwelcoming teachers, she struggles with deteriorating health and a mind she cannot entirely trust. The war she is supposed to help fight seems impossible to win. Inside the Emperor''s stronghold, threats and uncertain memories make it difficult to distinguish an external enemy from the failures of her own perception.","work_id":239,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20723256W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Harrow last necromancer Ninth House drafted by Emperor; detested rival,three hostile teachers","Failing health,mind,sword nausea; Mithraeum,ghostly threat and apparent unwinnable war"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28024928M","isbn":"9781250313225","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL20723256W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20723256W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":122},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:512:en","key":{"work_id":512,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Charlie believes his friendship with Nick cannot become the relationship he hopes for, because he assumes Nick is straight. Nick''s growing feelings challenge that assumption and his understanding of himself. This second graphic-novel volume follows their changing closeness through the everyday world of friends and family. Rather than a single grand declaration resolving everything, small encounters and conversations give their bond shape as they work out what it means to each of them.","work_id":512,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.hachette.co.nz/alice-oseman/heartstopper-volume-2-boy-meets-boy-in-the-phenomenal-graphic-novel-series-also-on-netflix","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Publisher exact9781444951400 paperback,author Alice Oseman,second graphic-novel volume","Nick and Charlie friends;Charlie assumes Nick straight;Nick discovers feelings,self,friends and family; small stories of their lives"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27565853M","isbn":"9781444951400","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL20354499W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.hachette.co.nz/alice-oseman/heartstopper-volume-2-boy-meets-boy-in-the-phenomenal-graphic-novel-series-also-on-netflix","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.hachette.co.nz","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":302},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:580:en","key":{"work_id":580,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Rob Ryan has concealed the childhood incident in which he was found alone in the woods after two companions disappeared. Years later, as a Dublin detective, he returns to the same area to investigate a girl''s murder with his partner Cassie Maddox. The new case draws his professional judgment into contact with memories he cannot fully recover. Finding out what happened to the victim becomes inseparable from the uncertainty surrounding his own survival.","work_id":580,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7989979W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["1984 three children in woods;only one found terrified,blood-filled shoes,amnesia","Survivor Rob Ryan Dublin detective conceals past;twenty years later girl''s murder same woods with Cassie Maddox"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24259329M","isbn":"9781429534314","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL7989979W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7989979W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":352},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:652:en","key":{"work_id":652,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Four residents of a retirement village make a weekly habit of examining crimes that were never solved. Their discussions become something more urgent when a local developer is killed and a mysterious photograph appears beside the body. Suddenly they have a current investigation rather than an old file to consider. As further deaths complicate the case, the friends apply their shared curiosity and contrasting perspectives to events unfolding in their own community.","work_id":652,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20878311W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Four retirement-village friends weekly unsolved-crime group","Developer dead,photograph beside body;first live case and further deaths"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28274140M","isbn":"9781984880963","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL20878311W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20878311W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":391},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:673:en","key":{"work_id":673,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Anastasia Steele has ended her relationship with Christian Grey and begun work at a Seattle publishing house. His offer of a different arrangement draws her back, though the reasons for their separation have not simply disappeared. Greater knowledge of his past makes their renewed intimacy more complicated. While Christian confronts his own difficulties, Anastasia must decide what she wants from him and how to respond to the women whose histories remain entangled with his.","work_id":673,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16550681W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Ana left Christian and starts Seattle publishing job;new arrangement and rekindled relationship","His troubled past and former women challenge Ana''s decisions"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL25240705M","isbn":"9780345803498","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL16550681W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16550681W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":397},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:675:en","key":{"work_id":675,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Naomi arrives in Knockemout to help her estranged twin, only to lose her money and car and discover she is responsible for a niece she never knew existed. With little means of starting over, she accepts help from Knox, a barber who values a quiet, uncomplicated life. Their involvement begins as a practical response to her predicament. Growing attachment becomes harder to dismiss when Naomi''s troubles turn into something more dangerous.","work_id":675,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL26955716W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Runaway bride Naomi helps estranged twin Tina in KnockemoutVirginia;Tina takes car/cash and leaves eleven-year-old niece","Barber Knox prefers solitude but helps Naomi;trouble becomes danger"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL36542796M","isbn":"9781945631832","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL26955716W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL26955716W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":399},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:682:en","key":{"work_id":682,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Lucian Rollins treats wealth and influence as protection against a past he wants to escape. Sloane Walton, a librarian committed to her father''s pursuit of justice, distrusts him for reasons tied to their shared history. Attraction complicates a relationship built on arguments and withheld explanations. Even when they move closer, they want incompatible futures. Lucian''s fear of repeating old harm and Sloane''s refusal to be shut out force them to confront what their estrangement has concealed.","work_id":682,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL34811234W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Lucian builds wealth/power to erase father''s mark;Sloane librarian continues father''s justice goals","Shared old secret and mutual dislike;attraction;Sloane wants family,Lucian rejects marriage/kids,withdrawal intended protection"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL47164031M","isbn":"9781728276120","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL34811234W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL34811234W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":399},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:683:en","key":{"work_id":683,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Alex Volkov has organized his life around ambition and revenge, leaving little space for emotional ties. Agreeing to look after his best friend''s sister puts that distance to the test. Ava Chen approaches people with an openness that contrasts with his guarded manner, despite gaps and nightmares in her own childhood memories. Their growing relationship crosses a boundary both recognize. Secrets from their separate pasts threaten the trust they are beginning to build.","work_id":683,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24390422W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Alex driven by past tragedy,success,revenge;charged with best friend''s sister Ava","Ava childhood nightmares and missing memory;opposite temperaments,attraction and threatening secrets"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL35152719M","isbn":"9781087939278","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL24390422W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24390422W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":405},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:688:en","key":{"work_id":688,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Josh Chen and Jules Ambrose have spent much of their acquaintance irritating one another. An unexpectedly intimate encounter leads them to propose a relationship without commitment or jealousy. Josh is building a medical career, while Jules is concentrating on qualifying as a lawyer, so the arrangement seems to leave their ambitions untouched. Getting to know each other makes those boundaries less convincing. Unresolved experiences from their pasts complicate the feelings neither intended to develop.","work_id":688,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27245843W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Doctor Josh and aspiring lawyer Jules antagonistic;enemies-with-benefits arrangement no jealousy or falling in love","Jules bar exam;intimacy reveals complexity and past threats to relationship"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL36978096M","isbn":"9781735056692","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL27245843W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27245843W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":405},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:698:en","key":{"work_id":698,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Anastasia Steele and Christian Grey have made a stronger commitment to one another, but a shared future does not erase their differences. Ana must find a place in Christian''s privileged world without giving up her independence. His need to control situations continues to clash with the trust their relationship requires. Outside hostility and problems rooted in the past test the security they believe they have achieved, turning their new life together into another negotiation.","work_id":698,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/series/FS3/fifty-shades-of-grey-series/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Publisher Book3 FiftyShadesFreed,not Book6 Freed retelling","Ana wants deeper commitment;Christian agrees;wealthy shared life,her identity,his control and past,external malice threaten them"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL25240706M","isbn":"9780345803504","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL16550682W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/series/FS3/fifty-shades-of-grey-series/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.penguinrandomhouse.com","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":397},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:699:en","key":{"work_id":699,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Kai Young is approaching a decisive vote over leadership of his family''s media business. His carefully controlled public and private life leaves little room for someone as spontaneous as Isabella Valencia. She works at the club he belongs to, making their attraction inappropriate as well as inconvenient. Their opposing habits initially make closeness seem unlikely. As their interest deepens, Kai must weigh the security of his established rules against a relationship that refuses to fit them.","work_id":699,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL29330646W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Kai reserved heir facing media empire CEO vote","Isabella impulsive bartender at his exclusive club;off-limits attraction/opposite temperaments"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL40323055M","isbn":"9780349436340","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL29330646W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL29330646W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":405},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:715:en","key":{"work_id":715,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"After a brief encounter at a party, Russ Callaghan and Aurora Roberts unexpectedly meet again as summer-camp counsellors. Both have taken the job partly to get away from difficulties at home. Russ wants distance from his father''s gambling problems, while Aurora hopes to recover a sense of belonging. Working together renews an attraction neither planned to pursue. The camp''s rule against relationships between staff makes their summer more complicated than either had intended.","work_id":715,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL34955908W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Russ and Aurora Maple Hills students end-year party encounter then both camp counsellors","His father''s gambling,her need for attention/belonging;strict no staff fraternizing rule"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL47317227M","isbn":"9781668026274","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL34955908W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL34955908W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":419},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:772:en","key":{"work_id":772,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Dante Russo''s determination to control his life is disrupted when blackmail forces him to become engaged to Vivian Lau. She accepts the arrangement as an obligation to a family seeking entry into a more exclusive social world. Dante intends to remove the threat and end the engagement rather than build a marriage. As they spend time together, attraction gives both reasons to question a partnership that began with pressure, conflicting interests and very little trust.","work_id":772,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28744393W","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["BillionaireCEO Dante blackmailed into engagement with jewelry heiress Vivian,daughter of enemy","Vivian agrees out of family duty/socialstatus;Dante wants evidence destroyed/betrothal ended but develops attachment"],"snapshot":"2026-09-30","checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL39449247M","isbn":"9781957464084","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL28744393W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28744393W","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"Open Library","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":405},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:4143:en","key":{"work_id":4143,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Robert Graves presents imperial Rome through a fictional account written by Claudius himself. Dismissed by his relatives because of physical disabilities, Claudius observes a ruling family shaped by rivalry, ambition and the threat of poisoning. The reigns of Augustus, Tiberius and Caligula become the setting for his precarious survival. His position at the edge of power offers an unusual view of those who wield it, before events bring him unexpectedly to the imperial throne.","work_id":4143,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/70667/i-claudius-by-robert-graves/9780679724773/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Publisher labels historical fictional autobiography,first of two volumes,not Graves actual autobiography","Claudius dismissed for disabilities;intrigue/poisonings under Augustus,Tiberius,Caligula;becomesemperor41AD"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL24951042M","isbn":"9780394725369","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL5036952W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/70667/i-claudius-by-robert-graves/9780679724773/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.penguinrandomhouse.com","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":2156},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:4191:en","key":{"work_id":4191,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Santiago Nasar is murdered in a small town despite widespread knowledge of the threat against him. Years later, a returning investigator tries to reconstruct the circumstances from accounts that do not agree. The question is not simply who carried out the killing, but how so many people could know about it without preventing it. Gabriel García Márquez turns the reconstruction into an examination of shared responsibility, public judgment and the uncertain evidence left by memory.","work_id":4191,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/482991/chronicle-of-a-death-foretold-by-marquez-gabriel-garcia/9780241968628","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Publisher:two brothers murder Santiago Nasar;town knew but nobody prevented;man returns27yearslater reconstructing contradictorytestimonies","MonthlyWorkdescription is only CollectedNovellas containmentlink,NOT storyfacts;Englishpublisher used instead. Exact selected earlierISBN remains separate edition proof."],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL30103540M","isbn":"9780141032467","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL274574W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/482991/chronicle-of-a-death-foretold-by-marquez-gabriel-garcia/9780241968628","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.penguin.co.uk","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":35},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1259:nl","key":{"work_id":1259,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Anna probeert met een wintersportreis de spanningen in haar gezin te doorbreken. Haar drukke werk dwingt haar echter later naar Oostenrijk te vertrekken dan haar man en kinderen. Wanneer ze hun vakantiechalet bereikt, blijkt er te zijn ingebroken en is niemand aanwezig. Een achtergelaten bericht maakt duidelijk dat ze niet zomaar vermist zijn. Anna moet uitzoeken hoe ze haar gezin kan terugvinden terwijl de afzender haar verbiedt de politie in te schakelen.","work_id":1259,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/sneeuwexpress/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Anna van Laarhoven directrice imagobureau,gezinsproblemen;skiweekKirchberg,werk laat haar later arriveren","Chalet overhoop,man/kinderen spoorloos,brief dreigt en verbiedtpolitie"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL42208329M","isbn":"9789400511019","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL30710666W"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p422971561","isbn":"9789400511019","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Sneeuwexpress","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/sneeuwexpress/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1282:nl","key":{"work_id":1282,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Een examenreis naar Benidorm loopt voor Nicole, Marjolein en hun klasgenoten uit op jaloezie en ruzie. Niet iedereen keert na die zomer terug naar Nederland. Dertig jaar later krijgt Iris tijdens een verblijf in Bergen aan Zee een onverwacht werkaanbod van een jonge ondernemer. De kennismaking lijkt een nieuwe mogelijkheid te bieden, maar wordt gevolgd door vreemde gebeurtenissen. Wat Iris overkomt blijkt verbonden met de vakantie die destijds zo verkeerd eindigde.","work_id":1282,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/zuidenwind/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["1988Nicole/Marjolein na eindexamenBenidorm metklasgenoten;jaloezie,ruzie,iemandkeertnietterug","30jaarlaterIrisPeters21 BergenaanZee metmoeder;PatrickICTondernemer geeftbaan;vreemde gebeurtenissenverbondenmetverleden"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p421777451","isbn":"9789044977257","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Zuidenwind","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p421777451","isbn":"9789044977257","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Zuidenwind","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/zuidenwind/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1283:nl","key":{"work_id":1283,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Na het overlijden van haar grootmoeder gaat Julia nog eenmaal naar het Tsjechische landhuis waar zij vroeger haar vakanties doorbracht. Voordat de familie het verkoopt, wil ze er met haar nichtje en een vriendin verblijven. Op de eerste avond rijdt Julia een jonge vrouw aan, die in coma raakt. Het slachtoffer kende haar grootmoeder. Die verbinding roept vragen op over de aanrijding en over wat er rond het huis heeft gespeeld.","work_id":1283,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/lentevuur/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Julia van Galen metnichtje/vriendin huisoverledenomaEvaChorinsky93Tsjechië,verkoopgepland","Aanrijdingjongvrouw eersteavond,coma;slachtoffer kendeoma,aanwezigheidniettoevallig"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p423058177","isbn":"9789044978445","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Lentevuur","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p423058177","isbn":"9789044978445","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Lentevuur","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/lentevuur/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1285:nl","key":{"work_id":1285,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Claudette heeft in Umbrië met haar man een succesvol gastenverblijf opgebouwd. De kookcursussen die zij geeft passen bij het rustige nieuwe bestaan dat zij aan bezoekers laat zien. Haar vertrek uit Amsterdam had echter een reden waarover ze zwijgt. Wanneer een Nederlandse vrouw met haar moeder arriveert, komt een oude naam ter sprake. Claudette merkt dat de afstand tot Nederland het verleden niet heeft uitgewist en dat zij het niet langer kan ontwijken.","work_id":1285,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/waterland/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Claudette/manB&B Umbrië metkookcursussen;vertrekAmsterdamnietvrijwillig","Geheimmeer10jaar,jongeNederlandsevrouw/metmoeder,naamuitverleden dwingtterugkeer"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p425814378","isbn":"9789400512498","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Waterland","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"unknown","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p425814378","isbn":"9789400512498","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Waterland","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/waterland/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1287:nl","key":{"work_id":1287,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Tijdens haar reis door de Verenigde Staten krijgt Paula de vraag een oude verdenking te onderzoeken. De weduwe van Jim wil dat zijn naam wordt gezuiverd rond de dood van zijn assistent Lucy. Paula werkt daarvoor samen met privédetective Stewart. Over Lucy blijkt weinig eenvoudig te achterhalen, terwijl hun onderzoek nadrukkelijk wordt tegengewerkt. De aanwijzingen voeren hen vanuit Los Angeles verder naar Mexico, waar de gevaren van de zaak steeds concreter worden.","work_id":1287,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/koraalrif/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Jimsweduwe vraagtPaulaVisseronderzoekdoodassistentLucyzevenjaareerdervoornaamszuivering","SamenprivédetectiveStewart,bewustonopvallendeLucy,tegenwerking,LAn aarMexico;uitgevernoemtvervolgRoadtrip"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p435543148","isbn":"9789400515178","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Koraalrif","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"unknown","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p435543148","isbn":"9789400515178","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Koraalrif","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/koraalrif/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1288:nl","key":{"work_id":1288,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Tijdens een kampeertocht in Noorwegen verdwijnt iemand uit de vriendengroep van Lieke. Een plaatselijke legende over vermiste vijftienjarigen geeft de gebeurtenis een dreigende verklaring, maar geen oplossing. Vijfentwintig jaar later ontvangt Lieke een telefoontje over de verdwenen zoon van hun vriendin Freya. De nieuwe vermissing brengt haar terug naar Stavanger. Samen met Birgit probeert zij verbanden te vinden tussen wat er nu gebeurt en de vragen die sinds hun jeugd zijn blijven bestaan.","work_id":1288,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/nachtvorst/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["LiekeBrouwerfamiliereisNoorwegen,wildkamperen vriendverdwijnt,mytheNachtvorst15jarigen","25jaarlaterBirgitbelt zoonFreya verdwenen;LieketerugStavangeronderzoek"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p433387653","isbn":"9789044932577","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Nachtvorst","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p433387653","isbn":"9789044932577","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Nachtvorst","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/nachtvorst/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1289:nl","key":{"work_id":1289,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Maaike en Judith keren voor een gezamenlijke skivakantie terug naar het Duitse gebied dat zij van vroeger kennen. Judiths politieke werk had zulke reizen steeds moeilijker gemaakt, waardoor de week samen bijzonder is. Dan komt Judith om het leven en verdwijnt de ontspannen tijd die de zussen hadden gehoopt te vinden. Maaike kan zich niet neerleggen bij de verklaring dat het een ongeluk was. Ze begint zelf naar de omstandigheden van haar zusters dood te zoeken.","work_id":1289,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/gletsjer/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["ZussenMaaikeJudithskiweekGarmischPartenkirchen,Duitsland,jeugdjaarlijksmaarpolitiekecarrièreJudithbeperkt","Judithverongelukt;Maaikegelooftnietongelukenonderzoekt"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p436755564","isbn":"9789044934489","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Gletsjer","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p436755564","isbn":"9789044934489","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Gletsjer","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/gletsjer/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1290:nl","key":{"work_id":1290,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Na het verlies van haar partner gaat Hannah met zijn kinderen Vera en Max naar een resort bij het Meer van Ohrid. Ze hopen tijdens hun eerste vakantie zonder hem weer wat ruimte voor ontspanning te vinden. De dood van een medewerker van het animatieteam verandert de sfeer. Wanneer Hannah hoort over eerdere verdrinkingen van jongeren, twijfelt ze aan een ongeluk. Ook de feesten op het strand krijgen daarmee een verontrustende betekenis.","work_id":1290,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/strandfeest/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["HannahstiefkinderenVeraMaxresortOhrid eerstevakantienaoverlijdenvader/echtgenoot","Animatieteamlidsterft,geen eersteverdronkenjongere,plaatselijkestrandfeesten roepenvragenop"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p437790843","isbn":"9789044934632","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Strandfeest","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p437790843","isbn":"9789044934632","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Strandfeest","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/strandfeest/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1291:nl","key":{"work_id":1291,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Emily heeft met Christiaan en hun kinderen een vertrouwd bestaan opgebouwd. De onverwachte dood van haar broer dwingt haar naar Australië te reizen om zijn wijngaard af te wikkelen. Daar ontdekt ze dat zijn leven anders was dan zij dacht. Wat een zakelijke afhandeling leek, wordt een persoonlijke crisis met gevolgen voor haar gezin. In Hunter Valley moet Emily beslissen hoe ze met zijn geheim omgaat, terwijl de situatie steeds gevaarlijker wordt.","work_id":1291,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/de-vallei/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Emily moet na plotselinge dood broer zijn Australische wijngaard afwikkelen","In Hunter Valley vindt zij geheim met gevolgen voor gezin en gevaar"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p438342682","isbn":"9789400516267","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"De vallei","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"unknown","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p438342682","isbn":"9789400516267","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"De vallei","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/de-vallei/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1292:nl","key":{"work_id":1292,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Op vakantie in Stockholm hoort Charlie dat de zeiltocht van haar broer Peter rampzalig is geëindigd. Zijn reisgenoten zijn gevonden, maar hijzelf en de boot blijven vermist. De autoriteiten zien een ongeluk als verklaring. Een onrustbarend bericht dat Peter eerder achterliet, maakt die conclusie voor Charlie moeilijk te aanvaarden. Met journaliste Elina Kjellberg probeert ze de gebeurtenissen op de Oostzee te reconstrueren en te begrijpen wat er met haar broer is gebeurd.","work_id":1292,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/mayday/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Peter verdwijnt na zinken zeilboot Oostzee, Femke en Robert gevonden","Charlie vertrouwt ongeval niet door voicemail; zoekt met journalist Elina Kjellberg"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p439140242","isbn":"9789044936117","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Mayday","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p439140242","isbn":"9789044936117","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Mayday","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/mayday/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1293:nl","key":{"work_id":1293,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Een fotografieopdracht brengt Rianne naar het uiterste noorden van Noorwegen. Aron, die ze tijdens haar verblijf ontmoet, neemt haar mee naar natuurgebieden buiten de gebruikelijke toeristische routes. Hun tocht krijgt een ander karakter wanneer ze in de bossen een dode man aantreffen. Het lijkt een jachtongeluk, maar Arons reactie roept bij Rianne vragen op. Wanneer hij haar op afstand houdt, probeert ze zelf te achterhalen wat hun ontdekking betekent en waarom hij zwijgt.","work_id":1293,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/sneeuwstorm/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Fotografe Rianne leert Aron kennen bij opdracht Noordkaap","Lichaam in bos nationaal park Ånderdalen; Aron trekt zich terug"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p439140447","isbn":"9789044934649","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Sneeuwstorm","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p439140447","isbn":"9789044934649","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Sneeuwstorm","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/sneeuwstorm/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1294:nl","key":{"work_id":1294,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Na het verlies van haar moeder lukt het Pien moeilijk om haar dagelijkse leven weer op te pakken. Samen met haar vriendin Leonor wil ze even weg uit de omgeving die haar aan het verdriet herinnert. Een onverwacht bericht geeft hun reis een bestemming: Madeira. Op het eiland vindt Pien echter meer dan afleiding. Nieuwe informatie brengt haar verleden aan het wankelen en dwingt haar anders te kijken naar wat ze over zichzelf en haar familie wist.","work_id":1294,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/bloemeneiland/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Pien rouwt om moeder, plant met vriendin Leonor vakantie","Onverwacht bericht brengt hen naar Madeira en familieverleden verandert"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p440643430","isbn":"9789044936278","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Bloemeneiland","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p440643430","isbn":"9789044936278","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Bloemeneiland","author":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/.well-known/genid/7358ab4eeaba046657c76eff6b0273c0","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/bloemeneiland/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1295:nl","key":{"work_id":1295,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Stella wil haar overleden grootvader Evangelis terugbrengen naar Kreta, waar hij opgroeide voordat hij naar Nederland verhuisde. Met haar gezin reist ze naar het eiland om zijn as te verstrooien en meer over haar afkomst te ontdekken. De ontmoeting met de familie verloopt heel anders dan gehoopt. Afwijzende reacties en vreemde gebeurtenissen maken duidelijk dat haar bezoek onrust veroorzaakt. Stella''s zoektocht naar haar wortels raakt aan iets uit het verleden dat anderen liever verborgen houden.","work_id":1295,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/nachtvlucht/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Stella brengt as grootvader Evangelis naar Kreta, zoekt roots","Familie reageert afwijzend; komst dreigt oud geheim te onthullen"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p444024387","isbn":"9789400517738","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Nachtvlucht","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"unknown","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p444024387","isbn":"9789400517738","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Nachtvlucht","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/nachtvlucht/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1297:nl","key":{"work_id":1297,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Een verblijf in de Italiaanse Alpen moet Manouk en haar collega''s dichter bij elkaar brengen. Op het werk botert het niet en de gezamenlijke vakantie biedt ruimte om die spanningen te verminderen. Een sneeuwstorm sluit de groep echter op in hun villa. Wanneer een van hen dood wordt gevonden, verandert het samenzijn in een situatie waarin niemand nog vanzelfsprekend veilig is. Oude conflicten krijgen een nieuwe betekenis terwijl contact met de buitenwereld onmogelijk blijft.","work_id":1297,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/ingesneeuwd/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Manouk en vier collega''s naar Alpen om samenwerking te verbeteren","Sneeuwstorm isoleert vakantievilla; dood van collega maakt conflicten verdacht"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p450375447","isbn":"9789400517721","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Ingesneeuwd","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"unknown","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p450375447","isbn":"9789400517721","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Ingesneeuwd","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/ingesneeuwd/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1298:nl","key":{"work_id":1298,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Aan het einde van een reis door Indonesië verblijven Manon en haar vriendin Ellen in een resort op Bali. Voor Manon roept de kust herinneringen op aan een gebeurtenis die haar leven veranderde. Dan ziet ze in een surfwinkel een recente foto die niet lijkt te kunnen bestaan: de afgebeelde man lijkt op Ricardo, die volgens haar acht jaar geleden is gestorven. Die ontdekking maakt haar onzeker over wat er destijds werkelijk is gebeurd.","work_id":1298,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/onderstroom/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Manon en Ellen sluiten maand Indonesië af op Bali","Recente foto in surfwinkel lijkt Ricardo, die acht jaar dood zou zijn"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p456100806","isbn":"9789400519664","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Onderstroom","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"unknown","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p456100806","isbn":"9789400519664","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Onderstroom","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","batchId":"e98346e5357cfc5f54582ac1ad17b662bc4e92c1d370b0d877722d1b22aed929","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:32.035Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/onderstroom/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1299:nl","key":{"work_id":1299,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Tijdens een gezinsvakantie in Frankrijk verliest Lauren haar jongere zus Celeste door een gewelddadige dood. Een verdachte wordt veroordeeld, maar blijft zijn betrokkenheid ontkennen. Twaalf jaar later werkt Lauren bij justitie wanneer een Franse journaliste haar benadert voor een onderzoek naar de zaak. Ze wil aanvankelijk niet terug naar die pijnlijke periode. Toch reist ze opnieuw naar Aubenas, waar de vragen van Nadine Dubois haar dwingen het verlies en de veroordeling opnieuw onder ogen te zien.","work_id":1299,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/zomeravond/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Celeste wordt tijdens gezinsvakantie Ardèche vermoord, Julien veroordeeld","Twaalf jaar later onderzoekt journaliste Nadine Dubois zaak met zus Lauren"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p430509707","isbn":"9789044932560","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Zomeravond","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p430509707","isbn":"9789044932560","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Zomeravond","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/zomeravond/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1300:nl","key":{"work_id":1300,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"De dood van Vincent Mulder tijdens een vakantie in het Zwarte Woud lijkt aanvankelijk een mountainbikeongeval. De vondst van een tweede slachtoffer met vergelijkbare verwondingen zet die verklaring onder druk. Als een getuige zijn vrouw Silvia met de plek in verband brengt, richten verdenkingen zich ook op haar. Silvia ontkent dat ze verantwoordelijk is. Met hulp van juriste Lauren Martens probeert ze te achterhalen wat er achter Vincents dood schuilgaat en haar eigen positie te verdedigen.","work_id":1300,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/dwaalspoor-2/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Vincent Mulder sterft bij mountainbiken Zwarte Woud; tweede dode met vergelijkbare verwondingen","Silvia wordt verdacht en vraagt juriste Lauren Martens om hulp"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p432194304","isbn":"9789044933192","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Dwaalspoor","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p432194304","isbn":"9789044933192","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Dwaalspoor","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p422815640","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/dwaalspoor-2/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1302:nl","key":{"work_id":1302,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Een uitnodiging voor een loterij geeft de vakantie van Robert en Karin op Mallorca een onverwachte wending. Na hun winst gaan ze mee voor een bezoek aan het resort Golden Oasis. Daar blijkt achter de aantrekkelijke aanbieding iets anders schuil te gaan dan ze verwachtten. Dit korte verhaal, afkomstig uit De bestemming, draait om een vakantiebelofte die haar onschuld verliest.","work_id":1302,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/vakantiegeld/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Robert en Karin winnen loterij op Mallorca en bezoeken Golden Oasis","Kort verhaal uit De bestemming; rondleiding blijkt onbetrouwbaar"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p394654730","isbn":"9789044970814","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Vakantiegeld","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p394654730","isbn":"9789044970814","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Vakantiegeld","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p296290033","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/vakantiegeld/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1303:nl","key":{"work_id":1303,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Achter het succesvolle uiterlijk van Landon en Madison Camus gaat een ongelukkig huwelijk schuil. Wanneer Landon ontdekt dat Madison een ander heeft, zoeken beiden een manier om hun gezamenlijke leven te beëindigen. Hun plannen krijgen een dreigende betekenis. Dit korte verhaal uit De bestemming gaat over het verschil tussen de indruk die een stel maakt en de vijandigheid binnen de relatie.","work_id":1303,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/de-scheiding/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Ongelukkig huwelijk Landon en Madison Camus, ontdekking overspel","Beiden bedenken hoe elkaar kwijt te raken; kort verhaal De bestemming, Winterberg-voorpublicatie niet onderdeel synopsis"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p394654692","isbn":"9789044970777","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"De scheiding","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p394654692","isbn":"9789044970777","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"De scheiding","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p296290033","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/de-scheiding/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1304:nl","key":{"work_id":1304,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Sander en Rachel willen tijdens hun vakantie vooral afstand nemen van het dagelijkse werk. De vliegreis begint met ergernis over een luidruchtig Nederlands echtpaar. Bij aankomst in het hotel denken ze daarvan af te zijn, maar de rust blijft uit: nieuwe problemen dwingen Sander toch aan het werk. Het is een afzonderlijk kort verhaal uit De bestemming, niet de volledige bundel.","work_id":1304,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/een-vluchtig-gebaar/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Sander en Rachel ergeren zich tijdens vlucht aan opscheppend Nederlands stel","In hotel nieuwe problemen, Sander moet werken; kort verhaal uit De bestemming"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p394654706","isbn":"9789044970784","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"Een vluchtig gebaar","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p394654706","isbn":"9789044970784","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"Een vluchtig gebaar","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p296290033","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/een-vluchtig-gebaar/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1306:nl","key":{"work_id":1306,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Op een zeiltocht met Lodewijk verandert Jasmijns romantische uitje wanneer dichte mist het zicht op de Middellandse Zee wegneemt. Een botsing maakt de situatie acuut: ze raakt haar hoofd en verliest het bewustzijn. Het afzonderlijk verschenen korte verhaal komt uit De bestemming en zet een intiem vakantiemoment tegenover plotseling gevaar op het water. De afloop blijft hier onbesproken.","work_id":1306,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/in-de-mist/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Jasmijn en Lodewijk op romantisch zeiluitje Middellandse Zee","Dichte mist, botsing, Jasmijn raakt bewusteloos; kort verhaal De bestemming"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p394654722","isbn":"9789044970807","role":"Manually reviewed exact publisher/library title/author/ISBN/language and translation identity; no provider identifier invented; cover remains separate","title":"In de mist","author":"Suzanne Vermeer","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"},{"book":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p394654722","isbn":"9789044970807","role":"Previously retrieved exact national-library ISBN/title/author/language evidence; fills absent Work author assertion, never overrides a conflicting authority or merges IDs","title":"In de mist","author":"http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/thes/p296290033","format":"http://schema.org/EBook","batchId":"bfe8a556321abbd54eac2f7d1103eafd3066600f4b44a112657e5ff4158a40f5","language":"nl","checkedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z","authorName":"Suzanne Vermeer","sourceCheckedAt":"2026-10-30T14:42:15.447Z"}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/in-de-mist/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1223:en","key":{"work_id":1223,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"An anniversary cruise promises a married couple a chance to enjoy their life together. The holiday ends abruptly when the husband vanishes, leaving his wife to return to the Netherlands without an explanation. Months later, a message from a lender raises questions that her search had not answered. As she learns about matters he concealed, her attempt to find him becomes an investigation into a marriage she may not have understood.","work_id":1223,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/cruise/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["A couple mark fifteen years of marriage with a cruise; husband disappears","Wife returns Netherlands alone; credit provider''s contact reveals husband''s hidden affairs"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL29349953M","isbn":"9781480471184","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL21609237W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/cruise/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1227:en","key":{"work_id":1227,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"A family''s first camping holiday beside Lake Garda is shattered when their young son fails to return on time. His father finds him beside another boy''s body, too shocked to explain what happened. Back home, the child struggles to speak about that night. A later killing in the same area brings the investigation back into their lives. Returning to Italy means confronting the event that changed their holiday and their sense of safety.","work_id":1227,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/bella-italia/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Parents take eleven-year-old son camping near Lake Garda; father finds dead boy beside traumatized son","Later murder and returning memories lead to request for family to return Italy"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL29349954M","isbn":"9781480471153","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL21609238W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/bella-italia/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1228:en","key":{"work_id":1228,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Two Dutch students expect their Caribbean holiday to be an uncomplicated break of parties and time on the beach. A visit from men looking for one girl''s father suggests there are parts of his business she does not understand. After a night out, her friend fails to come home. What first seems like an ordinary change of plans becomes increasingly alarming as the silence continues and the promised carefree holiday falls apart.","work_id":1228,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/bon-bini-beach/","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Dutch students holiday in Caribbean house owned by one girl''s father","Unknown men ask for father; after night out one friend disappears"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL29349955M","isbn":"9781480443778","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL21609239W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.awbruna.nl/boek/thrillers/suzanne-vermeer/bon-bini-beach/","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.awbruna.nl","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":713},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:1456:en","key":{"work_id":1456,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Yuval Noah Harari turns from humanity''s past to the ambitions that may shape its future. He examines the pursuit of longer lives, greater happiness and powers once attributed to gods. Drawing on history and developments in technology, he asks how those projects could change human societies and people''s place within them. The book presents possible directions and their dangers, inviting readers to question who might benefit from the capabilities humanity is creating.","work_id":1456,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.wilibraries.org.uk/Record/102419","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Yuval Noah Harari examines future projects after historical struggle with famine, plague and war","Happiness, immortality, technological powers and risks to human future are questions, not established predictions"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL26326058M","isbn":"9781910701874","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL17641518W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.wilibraries.org.uk/Record/102419","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.wilibraries.org.uk","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":65},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:9688:en","key":{"work_id":9688,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"In Depression-era Minnesota, Odie lives under harsh authority at the Lincoln Indian Training School. When remaining there becomes impossible, he escapes with his brother Albert and two other children. They take to the rivers in a canoe, searching for somewhere they can belong. Their journey through a troubled country brings encounters beyond the institution they have fled. Survival depends on the bond between the four travellers and their hope of finding a home.","work_id":9688,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/This-Tender-Land/William-Kent-Krueger/9781476749303","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["1932 Minnesota: orphan Odie at abusive Lincoln Indian Training School","Flees by canoe with brother Albert, friend Mose and Emmy toward Mississippi seeking home"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL27300929M","isbn":"9781476749297","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL20120987W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/This-Tender-Land/William-Kent-Krueger/9781476749303","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.simonandschuster.com","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":5502},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:9761:en","key":{"work_id":9761,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"Tan Yunxian grows up learning medicine from her grandmother in fifteenth-century China. Her friendship with a girl training as a midwife gives that education a shared purpose. Marriage threatens both: the expectations of her new household restrict whom she may see and how she may help other women. Inspired by a historical physician, the novel follows the conflict between Yunxian''s abilities and the boundaries placed around her life, with female friendship central to her choices.","work_id":9761,"evidence":[{"url":"https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Lady-Tans-Circle-of-Women/Lisa-See/9781982117085","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Historical novel inspired by fifteenth-century physician Tan Yunxian, taught by grandmother","Friendship with midwife Meiling and arranged marriage restrictions create central conflict"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL42752206M","isbn":"9781982117085","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL31130116W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Lady-Tans-Circle-of-Women/Lisa-See/9781982117085","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"www.simonandschuster.com","source_type":"official_publisher","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":590},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","ref":"description:303:en","key":{"work_id":303,"language":"en"},"before":null,"after":{"text":"The war against the Parshendi enters a dangerous phase as Dalinar takes the human armies further into the Shattered Plains. Elsewhere, Shallan pursues the lost city of Urithiru, while Kaladin learns to understand the powers of a Windrunner. Their separate responsibilities place them within a conflict that is changing around them. The second Stormlight Archive novel follows these different efforts to act and learn in a world whose older powers are becoming increasingly important.","work_id":303,"evidence":[{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL25438720M","role":"Original Work synopsis facts; not edition/format/cover proof","facts":["Exact English edition ISBN9780765326362, sole WorkOL16813053W and authorBrandonSanderson","Dalinar leads human armies deeper into Shattered Plains as war with Parshendi changes; Shallan searches for Urithiru; Kaladin learns Windrunner powers","Current stored firstPublishYear2012 is preserved, not verified as original publication by the2014 printing"],"snapshot":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31"},{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL25438720M","isbn":"9780765326362","role":"Exact selected test edition sole parent/ISBN/title plus existing Work-author authority binding; cover remains separate","snapshot":"2026-09-30","workParent":"OL16813053W"}],"language":"en","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL25438720M","reviewed_at":"2026-10-31T00:00:00+00:00","source_name":"openlibrary.org","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":19},"origin":"integrity-reviewed"},{"relation":"catalog_edition_metadata","ref":"metadata:@edition:9789023425540","key":{"edition_id":"@edition:9789023425540"},"before":null,"after":{"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","review_batch":"catalog-integrity-release-20261031","evidence":[{"url":"https://metadata.isbn.nl/138134/de-oversteek.html","checkedAt":"2026-10-29T20:53:51.159Z","sha256":"a9551a5f6595307d87afa7d21375e0cc944ab31b1b0204dea8e290c0b7f9046c","isbn":"9789023425540","facts":"Paperbac